window.__CAPM_DATA=(window.__CAPM_DATA||"")+"\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The project’s duration is 10 days, which is calculated based on the critical path—the longest path through the network diagram, determining the shortest time to complete the project.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":64,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following activities would most likely be classified as operations?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following activities would most likely be classified as operations?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Developing a new software application<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Developing a new software application\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Upgrading a building’s security system<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Upgrading a building’s security system\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Manufacturing a product on a regular basis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Manufacturing a product on a regular basis\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Implementing a new marketing campaign for a product launch<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Implementing a new marketing campaign for a product launch\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Manufacturing a product regularly is an example of operational work because it involves continuous production.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Manufacturing a product regularly is an example of operational work because it involves continuous production.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":65,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which Agile framework is specifically designed for scaling Agile across large enterprises ?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which Agile framework is specifically designed for scaling Agile across large enterprises ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scrum of scrums<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Scrum of scrums\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>eXtreme programming<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. eXtreme programming\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>SAFe<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. SAFe\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lean<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Lean\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C SAFe (Scaled Agile Framework) focuses on providing a knowledge base of patterns for scaling development work across all levels of the enterprise (Agile Practice Guide, page 113)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Scrum of Scrums is a technique used to scale Scrum to larger teams by having multiple Scrum teams collaborate and not a full framework designed for enterprise scale<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C SAFe (Scaled Agile Framework) focuses on providing a knowledge base of patterns for scaling development work across all levels of the enterprise (Agile Practice Guide, page 113) Option A: Scrum of Scrums is a technique used to scale Scrum to larger teams by having multiple Scrum teams collaborate and not a full framework designed for enterprise scale .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":66,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A graphical display of project team members and their hierarchical links is called:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A graphical display of project team members and their hierarchical links is called:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource Schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Resource Schedule\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Organization Chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project Organization Chart\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource Breakdown Structure (RBS)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Resource Breakdown Structure (RBS)\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM/RACI)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM/RACI)\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The Project Organization Chart is a graphical display that shows project team members and their hierarchical links within the project (PMI Process Group, Page 229).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Resource Schedule outlines when and where resources will be used in the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Resource Breakdown Structure (RBS) categorizes resources by type and availability.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM/RACI) shows who is responsible for what tasks but does not show hierarchical links.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The Project Organization Chart is a graphical display that shows project team members and their hierarchical links within the project (PMI Process Group, Page 229). Option A: Resource Schedule outlines when and where resources will be used in the project. Option C: Resource Breakdown Structure (RBS) categorizes resources by type and availability. Option D: Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM/RACI) shows who is responsible for what tasks but does not show hierarchical links.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":67,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A business analyst is tasked with improving the efficiency of customer support service. The business analyst anticipated that the average response time to customer inquiries would decrease as changes were implemented, but instead, it has increased. What method should the business analyst use to identify the underlying issue?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst is tasked with improving the efficiency of customer support service. The business analyst anticipated that the average response time to customer inquiries would decrease as changes were implemented, but instead, it has increased. What method should the business analyst use to identify the underlying issue?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Root cause analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Root cause analysis\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Observation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Observation\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Interviews<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Interviews\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Process modeling<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Process modeling\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Root cause analysis involves systematically investigating the underlying causes of problems or issues. It helps identify why the response time has increased and what changes or factors might have led to this outcome. Techniques like the &quot;Five Whys&quot; or fishbone diagrams can be used within this method.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Root cause analysis involves systematically investigating the underlying causes of problems or issues. It helps identify why the response time has increased and what changes or factors might have led to this outcome. Techniques like the \\\"Five Whys\\\" or fishbone diagrams can be used within this method.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":68,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which interpersonal skill should the project manager have to convince others to cooperate toward common goals?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which interpersonal skill should the project manager have to convince others to cooperate toward common goals?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Collaboration<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Collaboration\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Negotiation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Negotiation\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Decision-making<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Decision-making\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Influence<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Influence\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Influence is the key interpersonal skill that involves sharing power and using interpersonal skills to convince others to work towards common goals.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Collaboration involves working together towards a common goal but doesn't necessarily involve the use of persuasion.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Negotiation involves reaching agreements, but it doesn't always imply the use of interpersonal skills to sway cooperation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Decision-making involves choosing between alternatives, not necessarily about influencing others.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Influence is the key interpersonal skill that involves sharing power and using interpersonal skills to convince others to work towards common goals. Option A: Collaboration involves working together towards a common goal but doesn't necessarily involve the use of persuasion. Option B: Negotiation involves reaching agreements, but it doesn't always imply the use of interpersonal skills to sway cooperation. Option C: Decision-making involves choosing between alternatives, not necessarily about influencing others.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":69,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which statement is true about scope creep?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which statement is true about scope creep?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It refers to the process of managing changes to the project scope as they arise<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. It refers to the process of managing changes to the project scope as they arise\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It is the gradual increase in the scope of the project without modification in resources, time, and budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. It is the gradual increase in the scope of the project without modification in resources, time, and budget\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It is the initial phase where the scope is defined and documented<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. It is the initial phase where the scope is defined and documented\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It involves the systematic approach to scope validation and verification<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. It involves the systematic approach to scope validation and verification\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Scope creep refers to the uncontrolled expansion or changes in a project’s scope without corresponding adjustments to time, cost, and resources. This often happens when additional features or requirements are added to the project incrementally, which can lead to delays and budget overruns.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Managing changes to the project scope is a part of change control.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The initial phase where the scope is defined and documented refers to scope planning or scoping.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The systematic approach to scope validation and verification involves ensuring the project’s deliverables meet the defined requirements, which is part of scope management but not scope creep<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Scope creep refers to the uncontrolled expansion or changes in a project’s scope without corresponding adjustments to time, cost, and resources. This often happens when additional features or requirements are added to the project incrementally, which can lead to delays and budget overruns. Option A: Managing changes to the project scope is a part of change control. Option C: The initial phase where the scope is defined and documented refers to scope planning or scoping. Option D: The systematic approach to scope validation and verification involves ensuring the project’s deliverables meet the defined requirements, which is part of scope management but not scope creep .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":70,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What is the purpose of a Sprint Review?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the purpose of a Sprint Review?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To review the validity of the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. To review the validity of the project\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To review the team’s performance during the sprin<span><\\/span>t<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. To review the team’s performance during the sprin t\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To inspect the product increment with the stakeholders and collect feedback on next steps<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. To inspect the product increment with the stakeholders and collect feedback on next steps\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To inspect progress toward the Sprint Goal<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. To inspect progress toward the Sprint Goal\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The purpose of the Sprint Review is to inspect the outcome of the Sprint and determine future adaptations. The Scrum Team presents the results of their work to key stakeholders and progress toward the Product Goal is discussed.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Inspecting progress toward the Sprint Goal is the purpose of a daily standup.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The purpose of the Sprint Review is to inspect the outcome of the Sprint and determine future adaptations. The Scrum Team presents the results of their work to key stakeholders and progress toward the Product Goal is discussed. Option D: Inspecting progress toward the Sprint Goal is the purpose of a daily standup.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":71,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">During the planning phase, a project manager identified several risks. How should the project manager deal with these risks during project execution? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During the planning phase, a project manager identified several risks. How should the project manager deal with these risks during project execution? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Record risks in the issue log<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Record risks in the issue log\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Develop risk response strategies<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Develop risk response strategies\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Actively monitor risks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Actively monitor risks\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ignore risks until they become issues<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Ignore risks until they become issues\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Implement response plans as needed<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Implement response plans as needed\"}],\"key\":[\"C\",\"E\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C &amp; E<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The project manager should continuously monitor the identified risks to assess any changes in their likelihood or impact. When risks materialize, the project manager should execute the pre-developed risk response plans to reduce the negative impact on the project and maintain progress.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> An issue log is used to document problems or issues that have already occurred. Risks are typically documented in a risk register.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Risk response strategies should already have been developed during the planning phase when the risks were first identified. During execution, the focus should be on implementing and refining these strategies if needed, not creating them from scratch.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The project manager should take proactive steps to manage risks before they turn into actual issues.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C & E The project manager should continuously monitor the identified risks to assess any changes in their likelihood or impact. When risks materialize, the project manager should execute the pre-developed risk response plans to reduce the negative impact on the project and maintain progress. Option A: An issue log is used to document problems or issues that have already occurred. Risks are typically documented in a risk register. Option B: Risk response strategies should already have been developed during the planning phase when the risks were first identified. During execution, the focus should be on implementing and refining these strategies if needed, not creating them from scratch. Option D: The project manager should take proactive steps to manage risks before they turn into actual issues.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":72,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What should a business analyst do after discovering two conflicting requirements?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What should a business analyst do after discovering two conflicting requirements?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update the requirements baseline<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Update the requirements baseline\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Perform an impact analysis and propose a lower-cost alternative<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Perform an impact analysis and propose a lower-cost alternative\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Communicate the conflict to stakeholders and facilitate a resolution<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Communicate the conflict to stakeholders and facilitate a resolution\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adjust the project scope to align with only one of the solution requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Adjust the project scope to align with only one of the solution requirements\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C The primary step is to bring the conflict to the attention of the relevant stakeholders. The business analyst should work with stakeholders to understand the implications of the conflict and facilitate a resolution that aligns with the project&#x27;s constraints and objectives.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The primary step is to bring the conflict to the attention of the relevant stakeholders. The business analyst should work with stakeholders to understand the implications of the conflict and facilitate a resolution that aligns with the project's constraints and objectives.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":73,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What is the primary difference between a risk and an issue?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the primary difference between a risk and an issue?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A risk has occurred, while an issue is a potential future event.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A risk has occurred, while an issue is a potential future event.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An issue has already occurred and requires immediate attention, while a risk is a potential event that may or may not happen.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. An issue has already occurred and requires immediate attention, while a risk is a potential event that may or may not happen.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A risk is always negative, while an issue is always positive.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A risk is always negative, while an issue is always positive.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An issue affects only the schedule, while a risk affects only the budget.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. An issue affects only the schedule, while a risk affects only the budget.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B A risk is a potential event that may or may not occur in the future. It can be either positive (opportunity) or negative (threat), and the focus is on mitigating or exploiting its potential impact. On the other hand, an issue is a problem or event that has already occurred and requires immediate attention to resolve or manage it.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A risk is a potential event that may or may not occur in the future. It can be either positive (opportunity) or negative (threat), and the focus is on mitigating or exploiting its potential impact. On the other hand, an issue is a problem or event that has already occurred and requires immediate attention to resolve or manage it.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":74,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>In Scrum, what should a test team be responsible for? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In Scrum, what should a test team be responsible for? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Helping Developers find bugs<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Helping Developers find bugs\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Everyone in the Development Team is responsible for quality<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Everyone in the Development Team is responsible for quality\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Monitoring the Developers’ performance using various quality metrics<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Monitoring the Developers’ performance using various quality metrics\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Test team is not a role in Scrum<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Test team is not a role in Scrum\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Review test results against requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Review test results against requirements\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B &amp; D Test team is not a role in Scrum; only three roles are defined in Scrum: the Development Team, the Scrum Master, and the Product Owner.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B & D Test team is not a role in Scrum; only three roles are defined in Scrum: the Development Team, the Scrum Master, and the Product Owner.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":75,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>In an agile project, which stakeholder is responsible for approving the deliverables?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In an agile project, which stakeholder is responsible for approving the deliverables?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product owner<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Product owner\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Sponsor\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project manager\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business analys<span><\\/span>t<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Business analys t\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A As the recipient of the project’s deliverables, the product owner is responsible for approving the deliverables of agile projects .<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A As the recipient of the project’s deliverables, the product owner is responsible for approving the deliverables of agile projects .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":76,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following involves determining, documenting, and managing stakeholder needs and requirements:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following involves determining, documenting, and managing stakeholder needs and requirements:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Collect requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Collect requirements\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Plan scope management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Plan scope management\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Define scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Define scope\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Define activities<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Define activities\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Collect Requirements is the process that involves determining, documenting, and managing stakeholder needs and requirements to meet project objectives.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Plan Scope Management involves creating the scope management plan, which details how the scope will be defined and controlled.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Define Scope involves developing a detailed description of the project and product.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Define Activities involves identifying the specific actions needed to produce the project deliverables.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Collect Requirements is the process that involves determining, documenting, and managing stakeholder needs and requirements to meet project objectives. Option B: Plan Scope Management involves creating the scope management plan, which details how the scope will be defined and controlled. Option C: Define Scope involves developing a detailed description of the project and product. Option D: Define Activities involves identifying the specific actions needed to produce the project deliverables.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":77,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>An assumption is best described as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An assumption is best described as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A risk that is expected to occur during the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A risk that is expected to occur during the project.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A factor that is considered true or certain without proof at the start of the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A factor that is considered true or certain without proof at the start of the project.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A limitation that restricts the project’s flexibility.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A limitation that restricts the project’s flexibility.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An issue that has already affected the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. An issue that has already affected the project.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B An assumption is something that is accepted as true or certain for the purpose of planning and execution, even though it might not have been proven or verified. Assumptions are made to facilitate the project’s progress and planning but need to be monitored and validated as the project progresses.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A risk is a potential future event that could impact the project, not something assumed to be true.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A limitation describes constraints that restrict flexibility but don’t specifically address assumptions.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> An issue is a problem that has already occurred and is affecting the project, which is different from an assumption.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B An assumption is something that is accepted as true or certain for the purpose of planning and execution, even though it might not have been proven or verified. Assumptions are made to facilitate the project’s progress and planning but need to be monitored and validated as the project progresses. Option A: A risk is a potential future event that could impact the project, not something assumed to be true. Option C: A limitation describes constraints that restrict flexibility but don’t specifically address assumptions. Option D: An issue is a problem that has already occurred and is affecting the project, which is different from an assumption.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":78,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following is a key benefit of the requirements traceability matrix (RTM)?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is a key benefit of the requirements traceability matrix (RTM)?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It provides a detailed schedule of all project activities.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. It provides a detailed schedule of all project activities.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It documents the project team’s roles and responsibilities.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. It documents the project team’s roles and responsibilities.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It tracks the project’s budget and resource allocation.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. It tracks the project’s budget and resource allocation.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It ensures that all project requirements are linked to deliverables.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. It ensures that all project requirements are linked to deliverables.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D A requirements traceability matrix (RTM) helps track and ensure that every project requirement is addressed and linked to corresponding deliverables. It provides a way to verify that all requirements have been met and facilitates easier validation and acceptance by stakeholders, ensuring that the final product aligns with the agreed-upon specifications<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A detailed schedule of all project activities is typically managed by a project schedule.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Documenting the project team’s roles and responsibilities is usually done through a responsibility assignment matrix (RACI)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Tracking the project’s budget and resource allocation is handled through financial and resource management tools<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D A requirements traceability matrix (RTM) helps track and ensure that every project requirement is addressed and linked to corresponding deliverables. It provides a way to verify that all requirements have been met and facilitates easier validation and acceptance by stakeholders, ensuring that the final product aligns with the agreed-upon specifications Option A: A detailed schedule of all project activities is typically managed by a project schedule. Option B: Documenting the project team’s roles and responsibilities is usually done through a responsibility assignment matrix (RACI) Option C: Tracking the project’s budget and resource allocation is handled through financial and resource management tools\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":79,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>To paint the office, the painter starts preparing the walls while choosing the paint with the office owner. This is an example of:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"To paint the office, the painter starts preparing the walls while choosing the paint with the office owner. This is an example of:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lead<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Lead\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lag<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Lag\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Mandatory Dependency<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Mandatory Dependency\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Internal Dependency<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Internal Dependency\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Lead refers to an acceleration of the successor activity. In this case, the painter starts preparing the walls (successor activity) while still choosing the paint (predecessor activity) .<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Lag is a delay between activities, not an acceleration.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Mandatory Dependency is a dependency required by the contract or the nature of the work.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Internal Dependency involves activities that are within the project team’s control but do not define the relationship here.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Lead refers to an acceleration of the successor activity. In this case, the painter starts preparing the walls (successor activity) while still choosing the paint (predecessor activity) . Option B: Lag is a delay between activities, not an acceleration. Option C: Mandatory Dependency is a dependency required by the contract or the nature of the work. Option D: Internal Dependency involves activities that are within the project team’s control but do not define the relationship here.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":80,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The development team has delivered a completed solution. The quality assurance team has passed the solution. What should the business analyst do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The development team has delivered a completed solution. The quality assurance team has passed the solution. What should the business analyst do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Evaluate the solution with the sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Evaluate the solution with the sponsor\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Conduct user acceptance testing.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Conduct user acceptance testing.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Review the product against the project scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Review the product against the project scope\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Perform load and stress testing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Perform load and stress testing\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B After the software developers deliver a completed solution and the quality assurance team passes it, the next step for the business analyst is to conduct user acceptance testing (UAT). UAT ensures that the solution meets the business requirements and works as intended for end users. It involves key stakeholders and users verifying that the system functions correctly and aligns with their expectations before the solution is deployed.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Evaluating the solution with the sponsor(s) typically happens after UAT, when the solution has been validated by users.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Reviewing the product against the project scope is part of an earlier phase and ensures that the solution aligns with the agreed-upon scope.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Conducting performance testing is usually done by the technical team, not the business analyst, and is done earlier in the process to ensure system performance.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B After the software developers deliver a completed solution and the quality assurance team passes it, the next step for the business analyst is to conduct user acceptance testing (UAT). UAT ensures that the solution meets the business requirements and works as intended for end users. It involves key stakeholders and users verifying that the system functions correctly and aligns with their expectations before the solution is deployed. Option A: Evaluating the solution with the sponsor(s) typically happens after UAT, when the solution has been validated by users. Option C: Reviewing the product against the project scope is part of an earlier phase and ensures that the solution aligns with the agreed-upon scope. Option D: Conducting performance testing is usually done by the technical team, not the business analyst, and is done earlier in the process to ensure system performance.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":81,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>In Scrum, who should start the daily standup?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In Scrum, who should start the daily standup?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The person coming in last, to encourage people to join on time.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The person coming in last, to encourage people to join on time.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Product Owner, to make sure the highest-value item is discussed first<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The Product Owner, to make sure the highest-value item is discussed first .\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Scrum Master, to facilitate the meeting.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The Scrum Master, to facilitate the meeting.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Anyone from the development team.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Anyone from the development team.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D The Development Team is responsible for managing and facilitating their standup meeting. This improves ownership and self-management.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The Development Team is responsible for managing and facilitating their standup meeting. This improves ownership and self-management.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":82,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>In business analysis, a complete set of processes associated with a particular function is known as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In business analysis, a complete set of processes associated with a particular function is known as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Knowledge Area<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Knowledge Area\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Process Group<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Process Group\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Organizational Process Assets<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Organizational Process Assets\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Portfolio Management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Portfolio Management\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Knowledge Areas are fields or areas of specialization that are commonly employed when performing business analysis. A Knowledge Area is a set of processes associated with a particular function (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 22).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> A Process Group focuses on the sequence or phase of the project and describes the categorization of processes within the project life cycle rather than grouping the processes by their purpose or function.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Portfolio Management is the management of multiple programs and projects aligned with organizational strategy.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Knowledge Areas are fields or areas of specialization that are commonly employed when performing business analysis. A Knowledge Area is a set of processes associated with a particular function (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 22). Option B: A Process Group focuses on the sequence or phase of the project and describes the categorization of processes within the project life cycle rather than grouping the processes by their purpose or function. Option D: Portfolio Management is the management of multiple programs and projects aligned with organizational strategy.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":83,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The risk response strategy in which the project team acts to reduce the probability of occurrence or impact of a risk is known as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The risk response strategy in which the project team acts to reduce the probability of occurrence or impact of a risk is known as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Exploit<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Exploit\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Avoid<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Avoid\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Mitigate<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Mitigate\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Share<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Share\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C “ Mitigate” involves taking actions to reduce the probability of occurrence or impact of a risk.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> “Exploit” is a strategy to take advantage of opportunities, not to reduce risks<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> “Avoid” involves eliminating the threat by changing the project plan.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> “Share” involves allocating some or all of the ownership of the risk to a third party.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C “ Mitigate” involves taking actions to reduce the probability of occurrence or impact of a risk. Option A: “Exploit” is a strategy to take advantage of opportunities, not to reduce risks . Option B: “Avoid” involves eliminating the threat by changing the project plan. Option D: “Share” involves allocating some or all of the ownership of the risk to a third party.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":84,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A project manager notices frequent information requests from stakeholders. What does it indicate?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager notices frequent information requests from stakeholders. What does it indicate?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project plan is flawless<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project plan is flawless\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The stakeholders are not satisfied with the current project deliverables<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The stakeholders are not satisfied with the current project deliverables\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The communication plan needs further refinement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The communication plan needs further refinement\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The stakeholders do not trust the project team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The stakeholders do not trust the project team\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Frequent requests from stakeholders often indicate that they are not receiving the information they need in a timely or effective manner, suggesting the communication plan may need refinement. A good communication plan ensures that stakeholders receive necessary updates through formal channels, reducing the need for unscheduled communication (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 73).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A flawless project plan includes clear communication strategies, preventing the need for constant unscheduled communication.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> While dissatisfaction might be a reason for communication, ad-hoc communication requests typically point to an issue with how information is being shared rather than a specific problem with the deliverables.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Lack of trust could manifest in different ways, but frequent ad-hoc communication is more related to information gaps. If stakeholders didn't trust the team, it might result in escalations or more formal interventions, rather than just frequent communication requests.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Frequent requests from stakeholders often indicate that they are not receiving the information they need in a timely or effective manner, suggesting the communication plan may need refinement. A good communication plan ensures that stakeholders receive necessary updates through formal channels, reducing the need for unscheduled communication (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 73). Option A: A flawless project plan includes clear communication strategies, preventing the need for constant unscheduled communication. Option B: While dissatisfaction might be a reason for communication, ad-hoc communication requests typically point to an issue with how information is being shared rather than a specific problem with the deliverables. Option D: Lack of trust could manifest in different ways, but frequent ad-hoc communication is more related to information gaps. If stakeholders didn't trust the team, it might result in escalations or more formal interventions, rather than just frequent communication requests.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":85,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Project management processes ensure:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Project management processes ensure:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Alignment with organizational strategy<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Alignment with organizational strategy\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Effective means to achieve project objectives<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Effective means to achieve project objectives\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project team performance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project team performance\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Effective project execution<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Effective project execution\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Project management processes provide effective means to achieve project objectives, ensuring that the project meets its goals.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Alignment with organizational strategy is achieved through portfolio management.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Project team performance is ensured through resource management and team development activities.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Processes are important tools that can be used in all steps of the project, not only the execution.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Project management processes provide effective means to achieve project objectives, ensuring that the project meets its goals. Option A: Alignment with organizational strategy is achieved through portfolio management. Option C: Project team performance is ensured through resource management and team development activities. Option D: Processes are important tools that can be used in all steps of the project, not only the execution.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":86,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following is an output of the Sprint Planning meeting? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is an output of the Sprint Planning meeting? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Product backlog<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The Product backlog\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Sprint backlog<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The Sprint backlog\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Sprint goal<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The Sprint goal\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Definition of done<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The Definition of done\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>The Sprint velocity<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. The Sprint velocity\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B &amp; C During the sprint planning meeting, the product owner and the development team define the Sprint Backlog &amp; the Sprint Goal. As the Developers work on the selected user stories during the Sprint, they keep the Sprint Goal in mind.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B & C During the sprint planning meeting, the product owner and the development team define the Sprint Backlog & the Sprint Goal. As the Developers work on the selected user stories during the Sprint, they keep the Sprint Goal in mind.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":87,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What does the project management plan include ?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What does the project management plan include ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Change Management Plan, Quality Management Plan, and Scope Management Plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Change Management Plan, Quality Management Plan, and Scope Management Plan\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Agreements, Procurement Management Plan, and Work Performance Information<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Agreements, Procurement Management Plan, and Work Performance Information\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Schedule Management Plan, Project Schedule, and Resource Calendars<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Schedule Management Plan, Project Schedule, and Resource Calendars\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope Baseline, Project Statement of Work, and Requirements Traceability Matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Scope Baseline, Project Statement of Work, and Requirements Traceability Matrix\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A The elements of a project management plan include various subsidiary plans such as the Change Management Plan, Quality Management Plan, and Scope Management Plan .<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Agreements and Work Performance Information are important project documents but not part of the project management plan’s subsidiary plans.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Project Schedule and Resource Calendars are outputs and tools used in the project, not elements of the management plan.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Requirements Traceability Matrix is a project document that is not part of the project management plan.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The elements of a project management plan include various subsidiary plans such as the Change Management Plan, Quality Management Plan, and Scope Management Plan . Option B: Agreements and Work Performance Information are important project documents but not part of the project management plan’s subsidiary plans. Option C: The Project Schedule and Resource Calendars are outputs and tools used in the project, not elements of the management plan. Option D: The Requirements Traceability Matrix is a project document that is not part of the project management plan.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":88,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A project manager must communicate resolved project-related issues to stakeholders by updating the:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager must communicate resolved project-related issues to stakeholders by updating the:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project records<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project records\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project reports<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project reports\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Issue log<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Issue log\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stakeholder register\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C The Issue Log is updated to communicate resolved project-related issues to stakeholders.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Project Records include various documents related to the project but do not specifically communicate issue resolutions.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Project Reports provide a summary of the project’s status but are not the primary tool for communicating resolved issues.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Stakeholder Register tracks stakeholder information, not issues.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The Issue Log is updated to communicate resolved project-related issues to stakeholders. Option A: Project Records include various documents related to the project but do not specifically communicate issue resolutions. Option B: Project Reports provide a summary of the project’s status but are not the primary tool for communicating resolved issues. Option D: The Stakeholder Register tracks stakeholder information, not issues.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":89,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>In adaptive approaches, what tool is used to capture stakeholder requirements from the user&#x27;s perspective, focusing on the value perceived by the user?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In adaptive approaches, what tool is used to capture stakeholder requirements from the user's perspective, focusing on the value perceived by the user?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use Case<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Use Case\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>User Story<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. User Story\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Context Diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Context Diagram\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Earned Value<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Earned Value\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B A User Story is a brief, simple description of a feature told from the perspective of the person who desires the capability, usually a user or customer. It is a tool commonly used in adaptive approaches, like Agile, to capture stakeholder requirements in the form of &quot;As a [type of user], I want [some goal] so that [some reason].&quot; The user story focuses on the value to the user and what they need from the system. (PMI guide to business analysis, page 215)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A Use Case describes a detailed interaction between a user and a system, focusing on the functional or nonfunctional requirements and covering normal and alternative paths in achieving a goal.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A Context Diagram is a tool used to visually represent the interactions between a system and external entities (like users, systems, or databases). It provides a high-level overview but does not focus on user value in the same way a user story does.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A User Story is a brief, simple description of a feature told from the perspective of the person who desires the capability, usually a user or customer. It is a tool commonly used in adaptive approaches, like Agile, to capture stakeholder requirements in the form of \\\"As a [type of user], I want [some goal] so that [some reason].\\\" The user story focuses on the value to the user and what they need from the system. (PMI guide to business analysis, page 215) Option A: A Use Case describes a detailed interaction between a user and a system, focusing on the functional or nonfunctional requirements and covering normal and alternative paths in achieving a goal. Option C: A Context Diagram is a tool used to visually represent the interactions between a system and external entities (like users, systems, or databases). It provides a high-level overview but does not focus on user value in the same way a user story does.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":90,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The progressive elaboration of high-level information into detailed plans is carried out by:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The progressive elaboration of high-level information into detailed plans is carried out by:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Management Office (PMO)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project Management Office (PMO)\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Portfolio Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Portfolio Manager\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Program Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Program Manager\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Project Manager\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D The Project Manager carries out the progressive elaboration of high-level information into detailed plans, as part of the iterative planning process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The PMO provides support and guidance but does not perform this task directly.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Portfolio Manager oversees the alignment of projects with organizational strategy, not detailed planning<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Program Manager coordinates multiple projects but does not perform detailed planning for individual projects.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The Project Manager carries out the progressive elaboration of high-level information into detailed plans, as part of the iterative planning process. Option A: The PMO provides support and guidance but does not perform this task directly. Option B: The Portfolio Manager oversees the alignment of projects with organizational strategy, not detailed planning . Option C: The Program Manager coordinates multiple projects but does not perform detailed planning for individual projects.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":91,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>To ensure that the final product aligns with the specified design requirements, what should the business analyst do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"To ensure that the final product aligns with the specified design requirements, what should the business analyst do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Conduct multiple internal design reviews<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Conduct multiple internal design reviews\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Review lessons learned results<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Review lessons learned results\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use a traceability matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Use a traceability matrix\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Engage an experienced development team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Engage an experienced development team\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C A traceability matrix is a tool that links requirements to their corresponding design elements and final deliverables. It allows the business analyst to track and verify that each requirement is implemented as specified, ensuring alignment between the final product and the design requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Internal design reviews do not provide a continuous or comprehensive way to ensure alignment throughout the entire development process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Reviewing lessons learned helps improve future projects but doesn't directly ensure alignment of the current product with its design requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> An experienced team is beneficial, but without proper tracking and verification, there's no guarantee that the product will fully align with the design requirements.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A traceability matrix is a tool that links requirements to their corresponding design elements and final deliverables. It allows the business analyst to track and verify that each requirement is implemented as specified, ensuring alignment between the final product and the design requirements. Option A: Internal design reviews do not provide a continuous or comprehensive way to ensure alignment throughout the entire development process. Option B: Reviewing lessons learned helps improve future projects but doesn't directly ensure alignment of the current product with its design requirements. Option D: An experienced team is beneficial, but without proper tracking and verification, there's no guarantee that the product will fully align with the design requirements.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":92,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What is the main focus of the &#x27;Manage Stakeholder Engagement&#x27; process:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the main focus of the 'Manage Stakeholder Engagement' process:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identifying stakeholders<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Identifying stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensuring stakeholder expectations are met<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Ensuring stakeholder expectations are met\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Developing the stakeholder engagement plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Developing the stakeholder engagement plan\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Analyzing stakeholder communication need<span><\\/span>s<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Analyzing stakeholder communication need s\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The main focus of the Manage Stakeholder Engagement process is to ensure that stakeholder expectations are met, fostering their continued support for the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Identifying stakeholders is part of the Identify Stakeholders process, not managing engagement.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Developing the stakeholder engagement plan is part of the Plan Stakeholder Engagement process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Analyzing stakeholder communication needs is part of stakeholder analysis and communication planning, not managing engagement.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The main focus of the Manage Stakeholder Engagement process is to ensure that stakeholder expectations are met, fostering their continued support for the project. Option A: Identifying stakeholders is part of the Identify Stakeholders process, not managing engagement. Option C: Developing the stakeholder engagement plan is part of the Plan Stakeholder Engagement process. Option D: Analyzing stakeholder communication needs is part of stakeholder analysis and communication planning, not managing engagement.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":93,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which quality management tool or technique is used to identify a problem, discover the underlying causes that lead to it, and develop response plans accordingly?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which quality management tool or technique is used to identify a problem, discover the underlying causes that lead to it, and develop response plans accordingly?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Inspection<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Inspection\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Quality audits<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Quality audits\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Process analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Process analysis\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Root cause analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Root cause analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Root Cause Analysis is used to identify a problem, discover the underlying causes that lead to it, and develop response plans to proactively address negative product risks or take advantage of potential opportunities.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Inspection is the examination of deliverables to ensure they meet quality standards but does not identify the root cause of problems.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Quality Audits are a systematic review of the quality management system and do not specifically address root causes.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Process Analysis focuses on improving processes but is not specifically aimed at identifying root causes<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Root Cause Analysis is used to identify a problem, discover the underlying causes that lead to it, and develop response plans to proactively address negative product risks or take advantage of potential opportunities. Option A: Inspection is the examination of deliverables to ensure they meet quality standards but does not identify the root cause of problems. Option B: Quality Audits are a systematic review of the quality management system and do not specifically address root causes. Option C: Process Analysis focuses on improving processes but is not specifically aimed at identifying root causes .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":94,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A disadvantage associated with virtual teams is that they:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A disadvantage associated with virtual teams is that they:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Require communication technology that is difficult to obtain<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Require communication technology that is difficult to obtain\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create challenges in including individuals with disabilities<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Create challenges in including individuals with disabilities\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Often struggle to accommodate teams working at different times or schedules<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Often struggle to accommodate teams working at different times or schedules\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create the potential for misunderstandings<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Create the potential for misunderstandings\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Virtual teams create the potential for misunderstandings due to differences in communication styles, cultural backgrounds, and time zones.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> While some technology might be challenging, it is generally available and not a significant disadvantage.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Virtual teams can include individuals with disabilities, often with fewer challenges than physical teams.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Time zone challenges are a factor but are often managed effectively; misunderstandings are a broader issue.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Virtual teams create the potential for misunderstandings due to differences in communication styles, cultural backgrounds, and time zones. Option A: While some technology might be challenging, it is generally available and not a significant disadvantage. Option B: Virtual teams can include individuals with disabilities, often with fewer challenges than physical teams. Option C: Time zone challenges are a factor but are often managed effectively; misunderstandings are a broader issue.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":95,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>In which phase of team development activities do team members start working together and adjust their work habits and behavior to support the team:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In which phase of team development activities do team members start working together and adjust their work habits and behavior to support the team:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Performing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Performing\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Storming<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Storming\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Norming<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Norming\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Forming<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Forming\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C In the Norming phase, team members start working together effectively, adjusting their work habits and behavior to support the team.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The Performing phase involves team members working at their highest productivity levels.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Storming phase involves conflict and competition among team members as they begin to express their opinions.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Forming phase is when the team is initially formed and begins to understand the project and their roles.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C In the Norming phase, team members start working together effectively, adjusting their work habits and behavior to support the team. Option A: The Performing phase involves team members working at their highest productivity levels. Option B: The Storming phase involves conflict and competition among team members as they begin to express their opinions. Option D: The Forming phase is when the team is initially formed and begins to understand the project and their roles.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":96,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which statement best describes the sprint backlog items?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which statement best describes the sprint backlog items?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>User stories that have been completed in a Sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. User stories that have been completed in a Sprint\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>User stories selected to be done in a Sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. User stories selected to be done in a Sprint\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>User stories refined by the product owner and the team during a sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. User stories refined by the product owner and the team during a sprint\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>User stories created during a sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. User stories created during a sprint\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The Sprint Backlog items are the user stories selected to be done in a Sprint in order to achieve the Sprint Goal.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The Sprint Backlog items are the user stories selected to be done in a Sprint in order to achieve the Sprint Goal.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":97,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following is an enterprise environmental factor?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is an enterprise environmental factor?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Market conditions<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Market conditions\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Company policies and procedures<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Company policies and procedures\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Previous project files<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Previous project files\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lessons learned from past projects<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Lessons learned from past projects\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Market Conditions are an enterprise environmental factor that can influence the project, as they are external factors that affect how the project is executed.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Company policies and procedures are organizational process assets, not external environmental factors.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Previous project files are also organizational process assets.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Lessons learned from past projects are also organizational process assets.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Market Conditions are an enterprise environmental factor that can influence the project, as they are external factors that affect how the project is executed. Option B: Company policies and procedures are organizational process assets, not external environmental factors. Option C: Previous project files are also organizational process assets. Option D: Lessons learned from past projects are also organizational process assets.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":98,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Project stakeholder engagement management is primarily focused on:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Project stakeholder engagement management is primarily focused on:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Collecting requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Collecting requirements\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Obtaining the project team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Obtaining the project team\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Conflict of interest managemen<span><\\/span>t<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Conflict of interest managemen t\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Communication methods<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Communication methods\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Communication Methods are critical in project stakeholder engagement management, as they define how information is shared with and received from stakeholders .<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Obtaining the Project Team is part of resource management, not stakeholder engagement.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Conflict of Interest Management is a specific issue but not the primary focus of stakeholder engagement.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Communication Methods are critical in project stakeholder engagement management, as they define how information is shared with and received from stakeholders . Option B: Obtaining the Project Team is part of resource management, not stakeholder engagement. Option C: Conflict of Interest Management is a specific issue but not the primary focus of stakeholder engagement.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":99,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A risk resulting directly from implementing a risk response is called:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A risk resulting directly from implementing a risk response is called:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Contingent Risk<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Contingent Risk\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Residual Risk<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Residual Risk\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Potential Risk<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Potential Risk\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Secondary Risk<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Secondary Risk\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D A Secondary Risk is a risk that arises as a direct result of implementing a risk response.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Contingent Risk is a risk that might occur depending on the outcome of a decision or event.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Residual Risk is the risk that remains after risk responses have been implemented.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Potential Risk refers to a risk that might occur in the future but is not necessarily a result of implementing a response.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D A Secondary Risk is a risk that arises as a direct result of implementing a risk response. Option A: Contingent Risk is a risk that might occur depending on the outcome of a decision or event. Option B: Residual Risk is the risk that remains after risk responses have been implemented. Option C: Potential Risk refers to a risk that might occur in the future but is not necessarily a result of implementing a response.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":100,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The development of a project scope management plan specifically aims to:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The development of a project scope management plan specifically aims to:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Manage project completion on time<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Manage project completion on time\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensure that the project includes all required work<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Ensure that the project includes all required work\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensure that the project will meet the needs for which it was initiated<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Ensure that the project will meet the needs for which it was initiated\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Reduce the risk of negative events in the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Reduce the risk of negative events in the project\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The Project Scope Management Plan ensures that the project includes all the work required and only the work required to complete the project successfully.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Managing project completion on time is part of schedule management.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Ensuring the project meets its objectives is part of the integrated project management, but specifically, the scope management plan focuses on the work included.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Reducing risks is part of risk management, not scope management.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The Project Scope Management Plan ensures that the project includes all the work required and only the work required to complete the project successfully. Option A: Managing project completion on time is part of schedule management. Option C: Ensuring the project meets its objectives is part of the integrated project management, but specifically, the scope management plan focuses on the work included. Option D: Reducing risks is part of risk management, not scope management.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":101,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A tool or technique used in the process of developing a project charter is:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A tool or technique used in the process of developing a project charter is:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Change control process<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Change control process\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Expert judgment<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Expert judgment\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Performance reviews<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Performance reviews\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Meetings<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Meetings\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Expert judgment is used in the development of the project charter to make informed decisions about the project’s objectives and requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The change control process is used to manage changes to the project, not for developing the charter.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Performance reviews are used to assess project and team performance, not for charter development.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Meetings are a part of project management processes but are not specifically a tool for developing the project charter.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Expert judgment is used in the development of the project charter to make informed decisions about the project’s objectives and requirements. Option A: The change control process is used to manage changes to the project, not for developing the charter. Option C: Performance reviews are used to assess project and team performance, not for charter development. Option D: Meetings are a part of project management processes but are not specifically a tool for developing the project charter.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":102,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Scrum is defined as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Scrum is defined as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A defined process that uses a waterfall project management principle<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A defined process that uses a waterfall project management principle\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A complete methodology for software development<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A complete methodology for software development\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A lightweight framework that helps people, teams, and organizations generate value through adaptive solutions for complex products<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A lightweight framework that helps people, teams, and organizations generate value through adaptive solutions for complex products\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A complicated framework to solve multiple complex products simultaneously<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A complicated framework to solve multiple complex products simultaneously\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Key points of scrum definition are:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Scrum is a framework, not a methodology or process<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>       <span><\\/span> <\\/span>Scrum is lightweight, not complicated<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Scrum helps people, teams and organizations generate value through adaptive solutions for complex products.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Key points of scrum definition are: ● Scrum is a framework, not a methodology or process ● Scrum is lightweight, not complicated ● Scrum helps people, teams and organizations generate value through adaptive solutions for complex products.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":103,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A procurement document used to request offers from prospective sellers is called a:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A procurement document used to request offers from prospective sellers is called a:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Statement of Work<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Statement of Work\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Request for Proposal (RFP)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Request for Proposal (RFP)\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Proposal<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Proposal\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Contract<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Contract\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B A Request for Proposal (RFP) is a procurement document used to request offers or proposals from prospective sellers.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The Statement of Work describes the procurement requirements but is not a request for offers.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Proposal or offer is the response to the RFP.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A contract is signed with the provider who wins the bid.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A Request for Proposal (RFP) is a procurement document used to request offers or proposals from prospective sellers. Option A: The Statement of Work describes the procurement requirements but is not a request for offers. Option C: Proposal or offer is the response to the RFP. Option D: A contract is signed with the provider who wins the bid.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":104,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager is leading the development of a new electronics product. During the design phase, the team faces issues with assembly efficiency and high manufacturing costs. What tool can help manage quality while ensuring fast and cost-effective assembly?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading the development of a new electronics product. During the design phase, the team faces issues with assembly efficiency and high manufacturing costs. What tool can help manage quality while ensuring fast and cost-effective assembly?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\" id=\\\"page_211\\\"><p><span>Data representation<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Data representation\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Design for X<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Design for X\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Data gathering<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Data gathering\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Audits<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Audits\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Design for X refers to a set of technical guidelines applied during product design to optimize specific aspects, such as reliability, assembly, manufacturing, cost, service, usability, safety, and quality. DfX aims to enhance the final product’s characteristics by controlling or improving these factors. Implementing Design for X can lead to cost reductions, quality improvements, better performance, and increased customer satisfaction.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options A, C, D:<\\/span> Data representation, Data gathering, and Audits are tools to manage quality, but they are not fit for this situation.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Design for X refers to a set of technical guidelines applied during product design to optimize specific aspects, such as reliability, assembly, manufacturing, cost, service, usability, safety, and quality. DfX aims to enhance the final product’s characteristics by controlling or improving these factors. Implementing Design for X can lead to cost reductions, quality improvements, better performance, and increased customer satisfaction. Options A, C, D: Data representation, Data gathering, and Audits are tools to manage quality, but they are not fit for this situation.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":105,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A business analyst wants to compare the performance of the product against a competitor&#x27;s performance, standards, and best practices. What technique should the business analyst use?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst wants to compare the performance of the product against a competitor's performance, standards, and best practices. What technique should the business analyst use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Benchmarking<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Benchmarking\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>SWOT analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. SWOT analysis\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Root cause analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Root cause analysis\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Competitive analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Competitive analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Benchmarking is a technique used to compare the current performance of a process, system, or organization against a predefined standard, best practice, or competitor&#x27;s performance. It helps identify areas for improvement and sets goals based on high-performance standards. This technique is often used to assess the effectiveness and efficiency of processes by learning from the best practices in the industry (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 60).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> SWOT Analysis is a tool used to analyze Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, and Threats related to a project or business but does not focus on comparing performance to a predefined standard.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Root Cause Analysis is used to identify the underlying causes of problems or failures, not to compare performance against standards or best practices.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Competitive Analysis involves analyzing competitors’ strengths and weaknesses but does not include comparing the performance against a standard or best practice.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Benchmarking is a technique used to compare the current performance of a process, system, or organization against a predefined standard, best practice, or competitor's performance. It helps identify areas for improvement and sets goals based on high-performance standards. This technique is often used to assess the effectiveness and efficiency of processes by learning from the best practices in the industry (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 60). Option B: SWOT Analysis is a tool used to analyze Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, and Threats related to a project or business but does not focus on comparing performance to a predefined standard. Option C: Root Cause Analysis is used to identify the underlying causes of problems or failures, not to compare performance against standards or best practices. Option D: Competitive Analysis involves analyzing competitors’ strengths and weaknesses but does not include comparing the performance against a standard or best practice.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":106,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>In an industrial project, a business analyst realized the need for a visual representation of the manufacturing process flow, which could also be used to determine when quality checks should be conducted. Which diagramming technique would be most useful for the business analyst’s needs?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In an industrial project, a business analyst realized the need for a visual representation of the manufacturing process flow, which could also be used to determine when quality checks should be conducted. Which diagramming technique would be most useful for the business analyst’s needs?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>Flowchart<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Flowchart\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>Pareto chart<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Pareto chart\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7E\\\"><p><span>Context diagram<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Context diagram\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7H\\\"><p><span>Scatter diagram<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Scatter diagram\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A flowchart (also referred to as process maps, progress flows, and progress flow diagrams) graphically displays the logical order of the project’s progress flow. Flowcharts can be used for process improvement as well as identifying where quality defects can occur or where to incorporate quality checks.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options B &amp; D:<\\/span> A Pareto chart is displayed as a histogram, illustrating the most serious causes of an error, while a scatter diagram is used to determine the correlation between two variables. Both diagrams don't show the manufacturing process flow.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Context diagrams are used to visually demonstrate how a business process, other systems, and people, all interact. So, context diagrams can include a business process as one of its components, but they can’t give you an inside look at how the process flows.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A flowchart (also referred to as process maps, progress flows, and progress flow diagrams) graphically displays the logical order of the project’s progress flow. Flowcharts can be used for process improvement as well as identifying where quality defects can occur or where to incorporate quality checks. Options B & D: A Pareto chart is displayed as a histogram, illustrating the most serious causes of an error, while a scatter diagram is used to determine the correlation between two variables. Both diagrams don't show the manufacturing process flow. Option C: Context diagrams are used to visually demonstrate how a business process, other systems, and people, all interact. So, context diagrams can include a business process as one of its components, but they can’t give you an inside look at how the process flows.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":107,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What should the project manager do when a process is out of control?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What should the project manager do when a process is out of control?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Allow the process to continue<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Allow the process to continue\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adjust the limits to bring the process back into control<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Adjust the limits to bring the process back into control\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Shut down the process until it is brought back into control<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Shut down the process until it is brought back into control\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Investigate the root cause and recommend corrective action<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Investigate the root cause and recommend corrective action\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D When a process is out of control, the project manager should investigate the root cause and recommend corrective action to bring the process back into control.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Allowing the process to continue without intervention would not resolve the issue.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Adjusting the limits is not a solution, as it does not address the underlying problem.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Shutting down the process might be necessary in extreme cases, but typically the first step is to investigate and correct.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D When a process is out of control, the project manager should investigate the root cause and recommend corrective action to bring the process back into control. Option A: Allowing the process to continue without intervention would not resolve the issue. Option B: Adjusting the limits is not a solution, as it does not address the underlying problem. Option C: Shutting down the process might be necessary in extreme cases, but typically the first step is to investigate and correct.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":108,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The project sponsor requests information on the resource levels and resource use throughout the project. What should the project manager share with the sponsor?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The project sponsor requests information on the resource levels and resource use throughout the project. What should the project manager share with the sponsor?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource schedules<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Resource schedules\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource histogram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Resource histogram\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource calendar<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Resource calendar\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource breakdown structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Resource breakdown structure\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B A Resource Histogram shows resource levels and usage throughout the project, providing a visual representation of resource allocation over time.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Resource Schedules outline when and where resources will be used in the project but do not provide a visual representation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Resource Calendars show the availability of resources but not their usage over time.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Resource Breakdown Structure (RBS) categorizes resources by type but does not show their use over time.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A Resource Histogram shows resource levels and usage throughout the project, providing a visual representation of resource allocation over time. Option A: Resource Schedules outline when and where resources will be used in the project but do not provide a visual representation. Option C: Resource Calendars show the availability of resources but not their usage over time. Option D: The Resource Breakdown Structure (RBS) categorizes resources by type but does not show their use over time.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":109,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The project manager’s role in the executing process is to:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The project manager’s role in the executing process is to:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work with the sponsor to define project objectives<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Work with the sponsor to define project objectives\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Supervise the work being performed<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Supervise the work being performed\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Develop corrective actions for variances<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Develop corrective actions for variances\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Review project document<span><\\/span>s<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Review project document s\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The role of the project manager in the executing process is to supervise the performed work to ensure that project activities are carried out according to plan.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Defining project objectives is part of the initiating process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Developing corrective actions for variances is part of monitoring and controlling, not executing<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Reviewing project documents is an ongoing activity but not specific to executing.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The role of the project manager in the executing process is to supervise the performed work to ensure that project activities are carried out according to plan. Option A: Defining project objectives is part of the initiating process. Option C: Developing corrective actions for variances is part of monitoring and controlling, not executing . Option D: Reviewing project documents is an ongoing activity but not specific to executing.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":110,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which document includes information on each identified stakeholder’s position regarding the project?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which document includes information on each identified stakeholder’s position regarding the project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder engagement plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Stakeholder engagement plan\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Stakeholder register\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Stakeholder analysis\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Communications management plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Communications management plan\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The Stakeholder Register includes information on each identified stakeholder’s position regarding the project, their influence, and their interest.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The Stakeholder Engagement Plan outlines how to engage stakeholders, not their positions.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Stakeholder Analysis is a tool used to assess stakeholders but does not contain all their information.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Communications Management Plan details how project information will be shared but does not focus on stakeholder positions.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The Stakeholder Register includes information on each identified stakeholder’s position regarding the project, their influence, and their interest. Option A: The Stakeholder Engagement Plan outlines how to engage stakeholders, not their positions. Option C: Stakeholder Analysis is a tool used to assess stakeholders but does not contain all their information. Option D: The Communications Management Plan details how project information will be shared but does not focus on stakeholder positions.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":111,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What is the earliest point at which the project manager can identify resources assigned to a project?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the earliest point at which the project manager can identify resources assigned to a project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Initiating<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Initiating\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Planning\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Executing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Executing\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Monitoring<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Monitoring\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Resources can be identified as early as the Initiating phase, often through pre-assignment or resource negotiations. Pre-assignment might include the team members who have already been identified in the Develop Project Charter Process (Initiating process group) or other processes before the initial resource management plan has been completed (PMI Process Groups, page 214).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Planning is when resources are typically planned, but they can be identified earlier.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Executing is when resources are actively used, not when they are first identified.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Monitoring involves tracking resource usage, not identifying them initially.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Resources can be identified as early as the Initiating phase, often through pre-assignment or resource negotiations. Pre-assignment might include the team members who have already been identified in the Develop Project Charter Process (Initiating process group) or other processes before the initial resource management plan has been completed (PMI Process Groups, page 214). Option B: Planning is when resources are typically planned, but they can be identified earlier. Option C: Executing is when resources are actively used, not when they are first identified. Option D: Monitoring involves tracking resource usage, not identifying them initially.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":112,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The project scope statement should contain all of the following, except:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The project scope statement should contain all of the following, except:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project objectives<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project objectives\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project deliverables<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project deliverables\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Detailed risks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Detailed risks\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project exclusions<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Project exclusions\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Detailed risks are not typically included in the project scope statement; they are addressed in the risk register and risk reports.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Project objectives are a key part of the project scope statement.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Project deliverables are clearly defined in the scope statement.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Project exclusions outline what is not included in the project and are part of the scope statement.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Detailed risks are not typically included in the project scope statement; they are addressed in the risk register and risk reports. Option A: Project objectives are a key part of the project scope statement. Option B: Project deliverables are clearly defined in the scope statement. Option D: Project exclusions outline what is not included in the project and are part of the scope statement.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":113,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>During which process are the scope baseline and the project scope statement created?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During which process are the scope baseline and the project scope statement created?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Plan scope management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Plan scope management\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Define scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Define scope\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Control scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Control scope\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create WBS<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Create WBS\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The scope baseline and project scope statement are created during the Define Scope process, which defines the detailed project scope, deliverables, and work required .<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Plan Scope Management creates the scope management plan but does not include the scope baseline.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Control Scope involves monitoring and controlling changes to the scope baseline.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Create WBS involves subdividing project deliverables and work but not creating the scope baseline.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The scope baseline and project scope statement are created during the Define Scope process, which defines the detailed project scope, deliverables, and work required . Option A: Plan Scope Management creates the scope management plan but does not include the scope baseline. Option C: Control Scope involves monitoring and controlling changes to the scope baseline. Option D: Create WBS involves subdividing project deliverables and work but not creating the scope baseline.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":114,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>During a Sprint, a Product Owner may engage in which of the following two activities? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During a Sprint, a Product Owner may engage in which of the following two activities? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Facilitate the daily standup<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Facilitate the daily standup\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update management on what is being worked on<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Update management on what is being worked on\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Prioritize the team’s work on the sprint backlog<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Prioritize the team’s work on the sprint backlog\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create and clearly communicate product backlog items<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Create and clearly communicate product backlog items\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Resolve problems encountered by the team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Resolve problems encountered by the team\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B &amp; D The Product Owner may represent the needs of many stakeholders including management. They are required to create and clearly communicate the Product Backlog items.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The daily standup is for the team. It is not for the Product Owner to facilitate it.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The developers prioritize their work during the sprint, not the product owner.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option E:<\\/span> As a servant leader, the agile project manager is responsible for resolving problems encountered by the team.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B & D The Product Owner may represent the needs of many stakeholders including management. They are required to create and clearly communicate the Product Backlog items. Option A: The daily standup is for the team. It is not for the Product Owner to facilitate it. Option C: The developers prioritize their work during the sprint, not the product owner. Option E: As a servant leader, the agile project manager is responsible for resolving problems encountered by the team.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":115,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following is a tool used in stakeholder engagement?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is a tool used in stakeholder engagement?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>RACI chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. RACI chart\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Votin<span><\\/span>g<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Votin g\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Net Promoter Score (NPS)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Net Promoter Score (NPS)\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Kano model<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Kano model\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Net Promoter Score (NPS) allows stakeholders to assign a numerical score that ranges from 0 to 10 to indicate their satisfaction level with the project, product, or service, as well as their willingness to recommend it to others.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Net Promoter Score (NPS) allows stakeholders to assign a numerical score that ranges from 0 to 10 to indicate their satisfaction level with the project, product, or service, as well as their willingness to recommend it to others.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":116,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>In a matrix organization, a project manager shares the responsibility of managing the project team with:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In a matrix organization, a project manager shares the responsibility of managing the project team with:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The sponsor\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The functional manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The functional manager\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The HR manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The HR manager\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The business analyst<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The business analyst\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B In a matrix organization, the project manager shares responsibility for managing the project team with the Functional Manager, who oversees the team members’ functional work.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B In a matrix organization, the project manager shares responsibility for managing the project team with the Functional Manager, who oversees the team members’ functional work.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":117,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What is the primary focus of the business analyst when dealing with internal stakeholders?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the primary focus of the business analyst when dealing with internal stakeholders?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensuring the stakeholders’ career growth.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Ensuring the stakeholders’ career growth.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sharing the product’s vision and building relationships with project teams to foster product development.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Sharing the product’s vision and building relationships with project teams to foster product development.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Overseeing the marketing strategies of the organization.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Overseeing the marketing strategies of the organization.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensuring compliance with external regulations.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Ensuring compliance with external regulations.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The business analyst acts as a bridge between the business and the project team, ensuring that the business vision is communicated clearly and that stakeholder needs are met (PMI guide to business analysis, page 49).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The business analyst's role is not focused on the career growth of stakeholders but rather on understanding and addressing business needs.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The business analyst's role typically involves eliciting, analyzing, and documenting requirements, not overseeing marketing strategies, which is more of a marketing or strategic role.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Ensuring compliance is more the responsibility of roles focused on governance or legal aspects, not the core focus of a business analyst when dealing with internal stakeholders.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The business analyst acts as a bridge between the business and the project team, ensuring that the business vision is communicated clearly and that stakeholder needs are met (PMI guide to business analysis, page 49). Option A: The business analyst's role is not focused on the career growth of stakeholders but rather on understanding and addressing business needs. Option C: The business analyst's role typically involves eliciting, analyzing, and documenting requirements, not overseeing marketing strategies, which is more of a marketing or strategic role. Option D: Ensuring compliance is more the responsibility of roles focused on governance or legal aspects, not the core focus of a business analyst when dealing with internal stakeholders.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":118,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What is the role of Subject Matter Experts (SMEs) in business analysis?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the role of Subject Matter Experts (SMEs) in business analysis?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To manage project finances and timelines.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. To manage project finances and timelines.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To provide specialized knowledge and insights during elicitation and analysis activities.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. To provide specialized knowledge and insights during elicitation and analysis activities.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To oversee the quality control team.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. To oversee the quality control team.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To define business cases independently from business analysts.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. To define business cases independently from business analysts.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Subject Matter Expert (SME) offers their knowledge and expertise in a specific domain, process, or technology during the elicitation and analysis phases. SMEs provide valuable insights that help business analysts understand requirements, processes, and potential solutions. They assist in ensuring that the solutions align with business needs and industry standards (PMI guide to business analysis, page 51).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Managing project finances and timelines is not the role of the SME; it falls under the project manager's responsibility.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> SMEs are not responsible for overseeing the quality control team.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Business analysts typically work with stakeholders, including SMEs, to define business cases. SMEs do not define business cases independently from business analysts; instead, they contribute their knowledge to the process.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Subject Matter Expert (SME) offers their knowledge and expertise in a specific domain, process, or technology during the elicitation and analysis phases. SMEs provide valuable insights that help business analysts understand requirements, processes, and potential solutions. They assist in ensuring that the solutions align with business needs and industry standards (PMI guide to business analysis, page 51). Option A: Managing project finances and timelines is not the role of the SME; it falls under the project manager's responsibility. Option C: SMEs are not responsible for overseeing the quality control team. Option D: Business analysts typically work with stakeholders, including SMEs, to define business cases. SMEs do not define business cases independently from business analysts; instead, they contribute their knowledge to the process.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":119,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>How can product roadmaps help align multiple products in a portfolio?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"How can product roadmaps help align multiple products in a portfolio?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>By setting the vision, strategy, and timing for a group of products.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. By setting the vision, strategy, and timing for a group of products.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>By ensuring consistent financial reporting across projects.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. By ensuring consistent financial reporting across projects.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>By tracking individual project team performance.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. By tracking individual project team performance.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>By consolidating all product releases into a single document.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. By consolidating all product releases into a single document.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Product roadmaps are used to align multiple products in a portfolio by providing a unified vision, strategy, and timing for a set of products. This helps ensure that each product supports the overall business goals and is aligned with organizational priorities, while still allowing for strategic adjustments when necessary (PMI guide to business analysis, page 93).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Financial reporting is not the main function of a product roadmap. The roadmap focuses more on aligning product development with business strategy rather than on financial metrics.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Tracking project team performance is typically handled by project management tools, not the product roadmap, which is more focused on the product’s strategic direction.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A product roadmap provides more than just a list of releases; it also outlines the strategic objectives and timing for product features, ensuring they are aligned with business goals. Simply consolidating releases does not capture the full purpose of a roadmap.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Product roadmaps are used to align multiple products in a portfolio by providing a unified vision, strategy, and timing for a set of products. This helps ensure that each product supports the overall business goals and is aligned with organizational priorities, while still allowing for strategic adjustments when necessary (PMI guide to business analysis, page 93). Option B: Financial reporting is not the main function of a product roadmap. The roadmap focuses more on aligning product development with business strategy rather than on financial metrics. Option C: Tracking project team performance is typically handled by project management tools, not the product roadmap, which is more focused on the product’s strategic direction. Option D: A product roadmap provides more than just a list of releases; it also outlines the strategic objectives and timing for product features, ensuring they are aligned with business goals. Simply consolidating releases does not capture the full purpose of a roadmap.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":120,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A complete project statement of work (SOW) includes all of the following, except:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A complete project statement of work (SOW) includes all of the following, except:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business need<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Business need\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project objectives<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project objectives\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Organizational strategy<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Organizational strategy\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product scope description<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Product scope description\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Organizational Strategy is not part of the project statement of work (SOW), which focuses on the business need, project objectives, and product scope description.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The business need is a key part of the SOW, justifying the project’s existence.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Project objectives outline what the project aims to achieve.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The product scope description details the deliverables and work required.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Organizational Strategy is not part of the project statement of work (SOW), which focuses on the business need, project objectives, and product scope description. Option A: The business need is a key part of the SOW, justifying the project’s existence. Option B: Project objectives outline what the project aims to achieve. Option D: The product scope description details the deliverables and work required.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":121,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What should the Scrum Master do to increase the productivity of the development team? (Select two )<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What should the Scrum Master do to increase the productivity of the development team? (Select two )\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Facilitate development team decisions.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Facilitate development team decisions.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Remove impediments hindering the development team.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Remove impediments hindering the development team.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Help the team refine the product backlog items.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Help the team refine the product backlog items.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensure that meetings start and end on time.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Ensure that meetings start and end on time.\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Keep high-value features prioritized in the product backlog.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Keep high-value features prioritized in the product backlog.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A &amp; B A Scrum Master is a servant-leader for the development team. Facilitating and removing impediments helps optimize the team’s productivity .<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A & B A Scrum Master is a servant-leader for the development team. Facilitating and removing impediments helps optimize the team’s productivity .\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":122,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A new project has been launched to resolve issues raised by a department that was not involved in the last project. What should the business analyst do to ensure the satisfaction of this department?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A new project has been launched to resolve issues raised by a department that was not involved in the last project. What should the business analyst do to ensure the satisfaction of this department?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sX\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Share all finalized project documents with the department for informational purposes.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Share all finalized project documents with the department for informational purposes.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Involve the department early in the requirements-gathering phase to define acceptance criteria.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Involve the department early in the requirements-gathering phase to define acceptance criteria.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ask the project manager to identify all relevant stakeholders affected by the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Ask the project manager to identify all relevant stakeholders affected by the project.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Request from the department to define the scope of the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Request from the department to define the scope of the project.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Engaging the department early allows them to provide input on what they expect from the update, ensuring that their specific needs and concerns are addressed. Defining acceptance criteria ensures that the update meets their expectations.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The business analyst should elicit requirements; it’s not the responsibility of the department to define the project scope.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Engaging the department early allows them to provide input on what they expect from the update, ensuring that their specific needs and concerns are addressed. Defining acceptance criteria ensures that the update meets their expectations. Option D: The business analyst should elicit requirements; it’s not the responsibility of the department to define the project scope.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":123,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following processes is used to create a detailed description of the project work?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following processes is used to create a detailed description of the project work?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Collect Requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Collect Requirements\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Plan Scope Management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Plan Scope Management\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Define Scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Define Scope\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create WBS<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Create WBS\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Define Scope is the process of creating a detailed description of the project and product, specifying what will be included and excluded.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Collect Requirements involves gathering stakeholder needs and expectations.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Plan Scope Management involves creating the scope management plan.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Create WBS involves breaking down the project work into smaller, manageable components.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Define Scope is the process of creating a detailed description of the project and product, specifying what will be included and excluded. Option A: Collect Requirements involves gathering stakeholder needs and expectations. Option B: Plan Scope Management involves creating the scope management plan. Option D: Create WBS involves breaking down the project work into smaller, manageable components.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":124,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which type of organizational structure allows project team members to report to both the project manager and the functional manager?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which type of organizational structure allows project team members to report to both the project manager and the functional manager?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Functional<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Functional\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Projectized<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Projectized\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Matrix\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Corporate<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Corporate\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C A Matrix organizational structure allows project team members to report to both the project manager and the functional manager, balancing authority between them.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> In a Functional structure, team members report to their functional manager.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> In a Projectized structure, the project manager has full authority over the project team.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Corporate is a large company, not an organizational structure.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A Matrix organizational structure allows project team members to report to both the project manager and the functional manager, balancing authority between them. Option A: In a Functional structure, team members report to their functional manager. Option B: In a Projectized structure, the project manager has full authority over the project team. Option D: Corporate is a large company, not an organizational structure.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":125,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>In the “Monitor and Control Project Work” process, the project manager reviews and approves changes to the project’s scope, schedule, and cost. This process also involves:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In the “Monitor and Control Project Work” process, the project manager reviews and approves changes to the project’s scope, schedule, and cost. This process also involves:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Defining project objectives<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Defining project objectives\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Conducting performance reviews<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Conducting performance reviews\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Facilitating lessons learned<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Facilitating lessons learned\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Updating the project management plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Updating the project management plan\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D The Monitor and Control Project Work process involves updating the project management plan to reflect changes in scope, schedule, and cost (PMI Process Groups, page 163).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Defining project objectives is part of the initiating process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Conducting performance reviews is part of monitoring project performance but is not the focus of this process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Facilitating lessons learned is typically done during the project closing phase.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The Monitor and Control Project Work process involves updating the project management plan to reflect changes in scope, schedule, and cost (PMI Process Groups, page 163). Option A: Defining project objectives is part of the initiating process. Option B: Conducting performance reviews is part of monitoring project performance but is not the focus of this process. Option C: Facilitating lessons learned is typically done during the project closing phase.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":126,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What is a Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM)?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is a Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM)?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A document that maps project roles and responsibilities<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A document that maps project roles and responsibilities\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A diagram that depicts the project’s organizational structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A diagram that depicts the project’s organizational structure\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A chart that displays the project schedul<span><\\/span>e<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A chart that displays the project schedul e\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A matrix that identifies stakeholder interests<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A matrix that identifies stakeholder interests\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A A Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM) is a document that maps project roles and responsibilities, showing who is responsible, accountable, consulted, and informed (RACI) for each task.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> A diagram depicting the project’s organizational structure is an organization chart, not a RAM.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A chart that displays the project schedule is a Gantt chart or timeline.<br/> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A matrix identifying stakeholder interests is not a RAM; it’s part of stakeholder analysis.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM) is a document that maps project roles and responsibilities, showing who is responsible, accountable, consulted, and informed (RACI) for each task. Option B: A diagram depicting the project’s organizational structure is an organization chart, not a RAM. Option C: A chart that displays the project schedule is a Gantt chart or timeline. Option D: A matrix identifying stakeholder interests is not a RAM; it’s part of stakeholder analysis.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":127,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which tool or technique is used to determine whether a project or phase should be started, continued, or terminated?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which tool or technique is used to determine whether a project or phase should be started, continued, or terminated?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost-benefit analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Cost-benefit analysis\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Decision tree analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Decision tree analysis\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lessons learned<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Lessons learned\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Definition of Done<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Definition of Done\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A The Cost-Benefit Analysis is used to determine whether a project or phase should be started, continued, or terminated by comparing the expected benefits to the costs.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Decision Tree Analysis is used to evaluate possible outcomes and decisions but is not specifically about project continuation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Lessons Learned are used for knowledge transfer and improvement, not decision-making about project continuation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Definition of Done (DoD) is a checklist of all the criteria required to be met so that a deliverable can be considered ready for customer use.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The Cost-Benefit Analysis is used to determine whether a project or phase should be started, continued, or terminated by comparing the expected benefits to the costs. Option B: Decision Tree Analysis is used to evaluate possible outcomes and decisions but is not specifically about project continuation. Option C: Lessons Learned are used for knowledge transfer and improvement, not decision-making about project continuation. Option D: Definition of Done (DoD) is a checklist of all the criteria required to be met so that a deliverable can be considered ready for customer use.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":128,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>How is the product backlog ordered?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"How is the product backlog ordered?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The business analyst and project manager collaborate to define the priorities of the product backlog items.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The business analyst and project manager collaborate to define the priorities of the product backlog items.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The team prioritized the product backlog items based on their size; smaller items at the top and larger items at the bottom.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The team prioritized the product backlog items based on their size; smaller items at the top and larger items at the bottom.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The product owner places the most valuable items at the top.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The product owner places the most valuable items at the top.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The sponsor decides the priority of product backlog items based on the need.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The sponsor decides the priority of product backlog items based on the need.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Ordering Product Backlog items is one of the Product Owner’s responsibilities although they may delegate the responsibility to others. Regardless, the Product Owner remains accountable. The most valuable product backlog items should be placed at the top.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Ordering Product Backlog items is one of the Product Owner’s responsibilities although they may delegate the responsibility to others. Regardless, the Product Owner remains accountable. The most valuable product backlog items should be placed at the top.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":129,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following is a technique used to shorten a project schedule?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is a technique used to shorten a project schedule?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Crashing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Crashing\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope decomposition<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Scope decomposition\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Critical path method<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Critical path method\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Rolling wave planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Rolling wave planning\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Crashing is a technique used to shorten a project schedule by adding more resources to critical path activities to complete them faster.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Scope decomposition involves breaking down project work into smaller components, not shortening the schedule.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Critical Path Method is a project management technique for determining the project schedule using the network diagram, not shortening the schedule.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Rolling Wave Planning is a form of progressive elaboration, not a schedule compression technique.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Crashing is a technique used to shorten a project schedule by adding more resources to critical path activities to complete them faster. Option B: Scope decomposition involves breaking down project work into smaller components, not shortening the schedule. Option C: Critical Path Method is a project management technique for determining the project schedule using the network diagram, not shortening the schedule. Option D: Rolling Wave Planning is a form of progressive elaboration, not a schedule compression technique.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":130,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which document authorizes the project?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which document authorizes the project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Charter<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project Charter\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Management Plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project Management Plan\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope Statement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Scope Statement\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business Case<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Business Case\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A The Project Charter is the document that formally authorizes the project, providing the project manager with the authority to apply organizational resources to project activities .<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Project Management Plan defines how the project will be executed, monitored, and controlled but does not authorize it.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Scope Statement defines the project’s scope but does not authorize it.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Business Case provides the justification for the project but does not authorize it.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The Project Charter is the document that formally authorizes the project, providing the project manager with the authority to apply organizational resources to project activities . Option B: The Project Management Plan defines how the project will be executed, monitored, and controlled but does not authorize it. Option C: The Scope Statement defines the project’s scope but does not authorize it. Option D: The Business Case provides the justification for the project but does not authorize it.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":131,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The completion of a project phase or major deliverable is often marked by:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The completion of a project phase or major deliverable is often marked by:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A milestone<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A milestone\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A risk analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A risk analysis\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A stakeholder review<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A stakeholder review\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A performance review<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A performance review\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A A Milestone marks the completion of a project phase or major deliverable and is a significant point in the project schedule.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Risk Analysis is conducted to assess risks but does not mark the completion of phases.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Stakeholder Review is an assessment process but not a milestone.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Performance Review evaluates project or team performance but does not mark the completion of phases.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A Milestone marks the completion of a project phase or major deliverable and is a significant point in the project schedule. Option B: Risk Analysis is conducted to assess risks but does not mark the completion of phases. Option C: Stakeholder Review is an assessment process but not a milestone. Option D: Performance Review evaluates project or team performance but does not mark the completion of phases.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":132,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following is the main characteristic of an agile team ?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is the main characteristic of an agile team ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It has all the skills necessary to create a product increment.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. It has all the skills necessary to create a product increment.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It has a team lead with strong interpersonal skills to manage all other team members.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. It has a team lead with strong interpersonal skills to manage all other team members.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It has a tech lead to guide junior developers with less experience.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. It has a tech lead to guide junior developers with less experience.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It should be composed of no less than 9 members.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. It should be composed of no less than 9 members.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A The agile team should be cross-functional, meaning it collectively possesses all the skills required to produce a potentially shippable product increment.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The agile team should be cross-functional, meaning it collectively possesses all the skills required to produce a potentially shippable product increment.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":133,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which tool or technique is used to assess project risks?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which tool or technique is used to assess project risks?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Expert judgment<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Expert judgment\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Probability and impact matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Probability and impact matrix\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Quality audit<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Quality audit\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Risk register\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The Probability and Impact Matrix is used to assess project risk by evaluating the likelihood of risk events and their potential impact on the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Expert judgment is used in many processes, including risk assessment, but is not a specific tool for assessing risk.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Quality audits are used to review project quality processes, not to assess risk.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The risk register is a document or spreadsheet used to catalog project risks and then record the assessment and analysis results. Helps track risks throughout the entire project life cycle.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The Probability and Impact Matrix is used to assess project risk by evaluating the likelihood of risk events and their potential impact on the project. Option A: Expert judgment is used in many processes, including risk assessment, but is not a specific tool for assessing risk. Option C: Quality audits are used to review project quality processes, not to assess risk. Option D: The risk register is a document or spreadsheet used to catalog project risks and then record the assessment and analysis results. Helps track risks throughout the entire project life cycle.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":134,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A project is struggling to meet its original schedule due to underestimated complexities in system integration. What should the business analyst do to prevent further delays?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project is struggling to meet its original schedule due to underestimated complexities in system integration. What should the business analyst do to prevent further delays?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Reprioritize the remaining deliverables to focus on essential integrations.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Reprioritize the remaining deliverables to focus on essential integrations.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Suggest adding more resources to accelerate the work.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Suggest adding more resources to accelerate the work.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adjust stakeholder expectations by communicating the delays.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Adjust stakeholder expectations by communicating the delays.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Conduct a business analysis performance assessment to identify process improvements.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Conduct a business analysis performance assessment to identify process improvements.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D A business analysis performance assessment is a formal evaluation process used to understand the effectiveness of the business analysis practices employed in a project. This process helps identify the strengths and weaknesses of the techniques being used and suggests improvements or changes that can help address issues like underestimated complexities in system integration. This would allow the team to pinpoint the root causes of the delays and suggest process improvements to avoid further problems (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 309) .<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> While reprioritizing might seem like an immediate fix, it does not address the underlying issues with the integration complexities or the causes of delays. Without understanding the root cause of the problem through an assessment, reprioritizing could simply delay the inevitable problems​.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Adding more resources to a project facing integration issues often does not resolve the complexities and can even make the situation worse due to coordination overhead. This approach doesn’t tackle the root cause of the problem; ineffective analysis or missed requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> While it's important to manage stakeholder expectations, simply communicating delays does not prevent further delays or fix the underlying issues causing the delays. It is a reactive approach rather than a proactive solution.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D A business analysis performance assessment is a formal evaluation process used to understand the effectiveness of the business analysis practices employed in a project. This process helps identify the strengths and weaknesses of the techniques being used and suggests improvements or changes that can help address issues like underestimated complexities in system integration. This would allow the team to pinpoint the root causes of the delays and suggest process improvements to avoid further problems (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 309) . Option A: While reprioritizing might seem like an immediate fix, it does not address the underlying issues with the integration complexities or the causes of delays. Without understanding the root cause of the problem through an assessment, reprioritizing could simply delay the inevitable problems. Option B: Adding more resources to a project facing integration issues often does not resolve the complexities and can even make the situation worse due to coordination overhead. This approach doesn’t tackle the root cause of the problem; ineffective analysis or missed requirements. Option C: While it's important to manage stakeholder expectations, simply communicating delays does not prevent further delays or fix the underlying issues causing the delays. It is a reactive approach rather than a proactive solution.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":135,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>In which approach does the business analyst focus on gathering detailed requirements before development begins?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In which approach does the business analyst focus on gathering detailed requirements before development begins?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adaptive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Adaptive\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Iterative<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Iterative\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Incremental<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Incremental\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Predictive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Predictive\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D In the Predictive approach, the business analyst&#x27;s primary focus is on detailed requirements elicitation before development begins. This method follows a structured and linear process where all requirements are gathered and documented comprehensively upfront, ensuring that the development team has a clear and complete understanding of what needs to be built.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D In the Predictive approach, the business analyst's primary focus is on detailed requirements elicitation before development begins. This method follows a structured and linear process where all requirements are gathered and documented comprehensively upfront, ensuring that the development team has a clear and complete understanding of what needs to be built.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":136,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A business analyst identifies several stakeholders and wants to categorize them according to their needs. Which tool or technique should the business analyst use?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst identifies several stakeholders and wants to categorize them according to their needs. Which tool or technique should the business analyst use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder engagement assessment matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Stakeholder engagement assessment matrix\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Stakeholder register\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder mapping<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Stakeholder mapping\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Persona analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Persona analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Stakeholder mapping and representation is a method of categorizing stakeholders using various methods. Categorizing stakeholders assists the project team in building relationships with the identified stakeholders (PMI Process Groups, page 301).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Stakeholder Engagement Assessment Matrix: A matrix that compares current and desired stakeholder engagement levels. It’s considered a mapping technique that plots stakeholders based on their engagement levels, though in this context, we are mapping them according to their needs.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Stakeholder register is a record that includes information about project stakeholders such as their names, contacts, roles, classifications, etc.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Persona is a fictional model of a potential user of the product. It is used to help the agile team understand the needs, behaviors, goals, and pain points of the target audience.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Stakeholder mapping and representation is a method of categorizing stakeholders using various methods. Categorizing stakeholders assists the project team in building relationships with the identified stakeholders (PMI Process Groups, page 301). Option A: Stakeholder Engagement Assessment Matrix: A matrix that compares current and desired stakeholder engagement levels. It’s considered a mapping technique that plots stakeholders based on their engagement levels, though in this context, we are mapping them according to their needs. Option B: Stakeholder register is a record that includes information about project stakeholders such as their names, contacts, roles, classifications, etc. Option D: Persona is a fictional model of a potential user of the product. It is used to help the agile team understand the needs, behaviors, goals, and pain points of the target audience.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":137,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which tool or technique is used to compress the project schedule by running activities in parallel?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which tool or technique is used to compress the project schedule by running activities in parallel?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Fast-tracking<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Fast-tracking\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Activity sequencing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Activity sequencing\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Critical Path Method<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Critical Path Method\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource levelin<span><\\/span>g<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Resource levelin g\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Fast Tracking is a schedule compression technique that involves performing activities in parallel that were originally planned in sequence.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Activity Sequencing is about determining the order of activities, not compressing the schedule.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Critical Path Method (CPM) identifies the longest path through the project schedule but is not specifically for compression<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Resource Leveling adjusts the project schedule to address resource constraints, not for compression.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Fast Tracking is a schedule compression technique that involves performing activities in parallel that were originally planned in sequence. Option B: Activity Sequencing is about determining the order of activities, not compressing the schedule. Option C: The Critical Path Method (CPM) identifies the longest path through the project schedule but is not specifically for compression . Option D: Resource Leveling adjusts the project schedule to address resource constraints, not for compression.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":138,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following is an appropriate topic to be discussed by the Scrum team during a Sprint Retrospective? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is an appropriate topic to be discussed by the Scrum team during a Sprint Retrospective? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Problems occurred during this Sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Problems occurred during this Sprint\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Communication issues between Scrum team members<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Communication issues between Scrum team members\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The product roadmap<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The product roadmap\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Future releases<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Future releases\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A &amp; B The purpose of the Sprint Retrospective is to plan ways to improve processes. The Scrum team inspects how the last sprint went with regard to individuals, interactions, processes, tools, and their Definition of “Done”. The team members discuss what went well during the Sprint, what problems they encountered, and how those problems were (or were not) solved.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A & B The purpose of the Sprint Retrospective is to plan ways to improve processes. The Scrum team inspects how the last sprint went with regard to individuals, interactions, processes, tools, and their Definition of “Done”. The team members discuss what went well during the Sprint, what problems they encountered, and how those problems were (or were not) solved.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":139,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>In which approach does the business analyst continuously refine the product backlog items based on changing requirements?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In which approach does the business analyst continuously refine the product backlog items based on changing requirements?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Predictive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Predictive\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Incremental<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Incremental\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adaptive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Adaptive\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Hybrid<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Hybrid\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C In adaptive approaches, the business analyst works closely with the product owner to continuously refine the product backlog. This includes adding or removing items, elaborating on requirements, and reprioritizing tasks based on evolving business conditions and priorities (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 233).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C In adaptive approaches, the business analyst works closely with the product owner to continuously refine the product backlog. This includes adding or removing items, elaborating on requirements, and reprioritizing tasks based on evolving business conditions and priorities (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 233).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":140,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What is the primary benefit of the “Validate Scope” process?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the primary benefit of the “Validate Scope” process?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Facilitates the acceptance of the deliverables by the customer<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Facilitates the acceptance of the deliverables by the customer\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensures that changes to the project scope are properly managed<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Ensures that changes to the project scope are properly managed\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Validates the overall concept and objectives of the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Validates the overall concept and objectives of the project\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensures that the project’s scope is accurately defined<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Ensures that the project’s scope is accurately defined\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A The primary benefit of the Validate Scope process is that it facilitates the acceptance of the deliverables by the customer, ensuring that the work meets the project requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Managing changes to the project scope is part of scope control, not validation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Validating the overall concept and objectives of the project is done through the feasibility study and the business case.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Defining the project’s scope is done during the planning process, not during validation.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The primary benefit of the Validate Scope process is that it facilitates the acceptance of the deliverables by the customer, ensuring that the work meets the project requirements. Option B: Managing changes to the project scope is part of scope control, not validation. Option C: Validating the overall concept and objectives of the project is done through the feasibility study and the business case. Option D: Defining the project’s scope is done during the planning process, not during validation.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":141,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A business analyst is tasked to increase sales by analyzing similar products offered by competitors. Which technique should the business analyst use?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst is tasked to increase sales by analyzing similar products offered by competitors. Which technique should the business analyst use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Competitive analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Competitive analysis\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Focus group<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Focus group\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Benchmarking<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Benchmarking\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Trend analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Trend analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Competitive analysis involves researching and analyzing competitors&#x27; products, strategies, and market positioning. It helps the business analyst understand the competitive landscape and identify opportunities to differentiate and improve their own products.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Benchmarking involves comparing specific aspects of the product with competitors, industry best practices, or standards. In this scenario, the business analyst is focusing on competitors' analysis rather than comparing performance or strategies.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Competitive analysis involves researching and analyzing competitors' products, strategies, and market positioning. It helps the business analyst understand the competitive landscape and identify opportunities to differentiate and improve their own products. Option C: Benchmarking involves comparing specific aspects of the product with competitors, industry best practices, or standards. In this scenario, the business analyst is focusing on competitors' analysis rather than comparing performance or strategies.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":142,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following is NOT typically used to define acceptance criteria?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is NOT typically used to define acceptance criteria?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business goals and objectives<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Business goals and objectives\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Stakeholder analysis\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Key performance indicators (KPIs)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Key performance indicators (KPIs)\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Financial metrics<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Financial metrics\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Stakeholder analysis is not used to define acceptance criteria. Stakeholder analysis identifies and assesses the stakeholders&#x27; needs, roles, and influence, but it does not directly determine the conditions under which a product or feature is considered complete (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 217).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Stakeholder analysis is not used to define acceptance criteria. Stakeholder analysis identifies and assesses the stakeholders' needs, roles, and influence, but it does not directly determine the conditions under which a product or feature is considered complete (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 217).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":143,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which concept ensures that a project team agrees on a set of conditions that must be met for a user story or iteration to be considered complete and accepted by the product owner?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which concept ensures that a project team agrees on a set of conditions that must be met for a user story or iteration to be considered complete and accepted by the product owner?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Definition of Read<span><\\/span>y<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Definition of Read y\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Definition of Done<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Definition of Done\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint Goal<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Sprint Goal\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Acceptance Criteria<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Acceptance Criteria\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The definition of done (DoD) is a series of conditions that the entire team agrees to complete before an item is considered sufficiently developed to be accepted by the business stakeholders. The definition of done for a user story or iteration helps the project team know that the work is complete so the team can move on to the next user story or iteration (The PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 219).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The definition of done (DoD) is a series of conditions that the entire team agrees to complete before an item is considered sufficiently developed to be accepted by the business stakeholders. The definition of done for a user story or iteration helps the project team know that the work is complete so the team can move on to the next user story or iteration (The PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 219).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":144,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A risk response strategy in which the project team takes no action toward a risk except to document it and revisit it periodically is called:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A risk response strategy in which the project team takes no action toward a risk except to document it and revisit it periodically is called:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Mitigate<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Mitigate\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Accept<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Accept\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Avoid<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Avoid\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Transfer<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Transfer\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B “ Accept” is the risk response strategy where the project team takes no action toward a risk except to document it and revisit it periodically.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> “Mitigate” involves taking action to reduce the probability or impact of a risk.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> “Avoid” involves taking steps to eliminate the risk entirely.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> “Transfer” involves shifting the risk to a third party, such as through insurance.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B “ Accept” is the risk response strategy where the project team takes no action toward a risk except to document it and revisit it periodically. Option A: “Mitigate” involves taking action to reduce the probability or impact of a risk. Option C: “Avoid” involves taking steps to eliminate the risk entirely. Option D: “Transfer” involves shifting the risk to a third party, such as through insurance.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":145,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which document is used to record the details of each change request, including the analysis of its impact on project constraints?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which document is used to record the details of each change request, including the analysis of its impact on project constraints?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sX\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Change log<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Change log\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Change management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Change management\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Change register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Change register\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Change clause<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Change clause\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A The change log is used to record the details of each change request, including the analysis of its impact on project constraints like scope, time, cost, and quality.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Change management is not a document, it's a process for managing change.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Change register is made up.<br/> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A change clause is a contract clause that defines how change is managed.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The change log is used to record the details of each change request, including the analysis of its impact on project constraints like scope, time, cost, and quality. Option B: Change management is not a document, it's a process for managing change. Option C: Change register is made up. Option D: A change clause is a contract clause that defines how change is managed.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":146,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What is the primary purpose of the lessons learned document?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the primary purpose of the lessons learned document?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To ensure that future projects do not repeat the same mistakes<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. To ensure that future projects do not repeat the same mistakes\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To measure project performance against project baselines<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. To measure project performance against project baselines\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To assess project risks that were encountered<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. To assess project risks that were encountered\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To provide historical data for estimating future project costs<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. To provide historical data for estimating future project costs\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A The primary purpose of a &#x27;lessons learned&#x27; document is to ensure that future projects do not repeat the same mistakes by documenting what was learned from the current project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Measuring project performance against baselines is part of project monitoring and control, not lessons learned.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Assessing project risks encountered is part of risk management, not lessons learned specifically.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> While lessons learned can provide historical data, their primary purpose is to avoid repeating mistakes.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The primary purpose of a 'lessons learned' document is to ensure that future projects do not repeat the same mistakes by documenting what was learned from the current project. Option B: Measuring project performance against baselines is part of project monitoring and control, not lessons learned. Option C: Assessing project risks encountered is part of risk management, not lessons learned specifically. Option D: While lessons learned can provide historical data, their primary purpose is to avoid repeating mistakes.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":147,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Midway through a project, the business analyst realizes that the project&#x27;s expenses are surpassing the expected benefits. Which of the following documents should the business analyst use to deal with the risk of discontinuing the project?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Midway through a project, the business analyst realizes that the project's expenses are surpassing the expected benefits. Which of the following documents should the business analyst use to deal with the risk of discontinuing the project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder impact matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Stakeholder impact matrix\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business case<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Business case\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project charter<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project charter\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business analysis plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Business analysis plan\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The business case provides the rationale for undertaking the project, including an analysis of the expected benefits, costs, and risks. It is used to justify the project’s continuation or discontinuation by comparing the projected benefits against the actual expenses and risks .<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The stakeholder impact matrix identifies and analyzes the impact of the project on different stakeholders.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The project charter is an initial document that authorizes the project and outlines its objectives, scope, and stakeholders.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The business analysis plan outlines the approach and activities the business analyst will undertake during the project.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The business case provides the rationale for undertaking the project, including an analysis of the expected benefits, costs, and risks. It is used to justify the project’s continuation or discontinuation by comparing the projected benefits against the actual expenses and risks . Option A: The stakeholder impact matrix identifies and analyzes the impact of the project on different stakeholders. Option C: The project charter is an initial document that authorizes the project and outlines its objectives, scope, and stakeholders. Option D: The business analysis plan outlines the approach and activities the business analyst will undertake during the project.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":148,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>How are acceptance criteria related to the Definition of Done?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"How are acceptance criteria related to the Definition of Done?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>They are mutually exclusive concepts<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. They are mutually exclusive concepts\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Acceptance criteria should comply with the Definition of Done<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Acceptance criteria should comply with the Definition of Done\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Acceptance criteria is a broader concept, compared to the Definition of Done<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Acceptance criteria is a broader concept, compared to the Definition of Done\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>User stories should either meet the Definition of Done or the acceptance criteri<span><\\/span>a<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. User stories should either meet the Definition of Done or the acceptance criteri a\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Acceptance criteria define the specific conditions that a product, feature, or user story must meet to be considered complete and acceptable to stakeholders. These criteria are part of the &quot;Definition of Done&quot;, which is a broader concept encompassing all the requirements and standards (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 219).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Acceptance criteria are a subset of the Definition of Done.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Acceptance criteria define conditions for completion at the feature or user story level, not the entire project scope. Therefore, the Definition of Done is a broader concept, compared to the Acceptance criteria.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Both acceptance criteria and definition of done are used together. Acceptance criteria are part of the Definition of Done and help provide clarity on what must be achieved for the work to be considered complete.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Acceptance criteria define the specific conditions that a product, feature, or user story must meet to be considered complete and acceptable to stakeholders. These criteria are part of the \\\"Definition of Done\\\", which is a broader concept encompassing all the requirements and standards (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 219). Option A: Acceptance criteria are a subset of the Definition of Done. Option C: Acceptance criteria define conditions for completion at the feature or user story level, not the entire project scope. Therefore, the Definition of Done is a broader concept, compared to the Acceptance criteria. Option D: Both acceptance criteria and definition of done are used together. Acceptance criteria are part of the Definition of Done and help provide clarity on what must be achieved for the work to be considered complete.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":149,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>When team members are asked to take on work outside their traditional roles, which development approach is being used?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When team members are asked to take on work outside their traditional roles, which development approach is being used?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Predictive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Predictive\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Agile<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Agile\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Incremental<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Incremental\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Traditional<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Traditional\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Team members often adopt a flexible role distribution to meet iteration goals. It is common for individuals to perform tasks outside their typical job function in order to adapt to the dynamic nature of the project and ensure timely delivery (PMI guide to business analysis, page 311).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options A &amp; D:<\\/span> In predictive approaches, i.e., waterfall or traditional, roles are typically more defined and rigid. Each team member's responsibilities are established upfront, and changes to scope or tasks are carefully controlled.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The incremental approach defines a set series of deliverables. In this approach, the project is thoroughly planned out from the beginning. Therefore, team members are unlikely to deviate from their established roles since work is highly structured.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Team members often adopt a flexible role distribution to meet iteration goals. It is common for individuals to perform tasks outside their typical job function in order to adapt to the dynamic nature of the project and ensure timely delivery (PMI guide to business analysis, page 311). Options A & D: In predictive approaches, i.e., waterfall or traditional, roles are typically more defined and rigid. Each team member's responsibilities are established upfront, and changes to scope or tasks are carefully controlled. Option C: The incremental approach defines a set series of deliverables. In this approach, the project is thoroughly planned out from the beginning. Therefore, team members are unlikely to deviate from their established roles since work is highly structured.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":150,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager is managing a project using the Scrum framework. The project manager receives a call from the product owner asking for a meeting with the team to discuss the possible approaches to implement user stories and make some initial size estimations. What type of meeting is the product owner referring to?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is managing a project using the Scrum framework. The project manager receives a call from the product owner asking for a meeting with the team to discuss the possible approaches to implement user stories and make some initial size estimations. What type of meeting is the product owner referring to?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Sprint planning\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Story mapping<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Story mapping\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Backlog refinement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Backlog refinement\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Brainstorming<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Brainstorming\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s65Y\\\">Backlog refinement provides a chance for the product owner to discuss and address stories’ requirements with the team. This can involve discussing requirements, potential approaches, and even estimations in order to end up with a clear vision of how to approach stories (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 179).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Backlog refinement provides a chance for the product owner to discuss and address stories’ requirements with the team. This can involve discussing requirements, potential approaches, and even estimations in order to end up with a clear vision of how to approach stories (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 179).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null}]},{\"id\":\"mock-4\",\"title\":\"Full Mock Exam 4\",\"kind\":\"Full Mock Exam\",\"count\":150,\"questions\":[{\"n\":1,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Mid-execution, a sponsor requests the project manager to terminate the project. What should the project manager do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Mid-execution, a sponsor requests the project manager to terminate the project. What should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Proceed with the close project process<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Proceed with the close project process\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Proceed with claims administration<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Proceed with claims administration\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Convince the sponsor to allow the project continuation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Convince the sponsor to allow the project continuation\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Insist on delivering the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Insist on delivering the project\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">When the project sponsor decides to terminate the project for any reason, the project manager should follow their instructions and terminate the project. In this case, the project manager should immediately start the “close project” process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> This scenario doesn't describe any disputes between the project manager and the sponsor concerning contracts’ terms, consequently claims administration is not the right answer.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A When the project sponsor decides to terminate the project for any reason, the project manager should follow their instructions and terminate the project. In this case, the project manager should immediately start the “close project” process. Option B: This scenario doesn't describe any disputes between the project manager and the sponsor concerning contracts’ terms, consequently claims administration is not the right answer.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":2,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which technique involves prioritizing features, epics, or user stories by business value in a sequential manner?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which technique involves prioritizing features, epics, or user stories by business value in a sequential manner?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Story Slicing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Story Slicing\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use Case Diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Use Case Diagram\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Story Mapping<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Story Mapping\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>User Interface Flow<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. User Interface Flow\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Story Mapping is a technique used where features, epics, or user stories are prioritized and organized by business value in a sequential manner. It helps teams visualize the product from the user's perspective and prioritize work based on delivering the most value first (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 204).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Story slicing involves breaking down larger user stories into smaller, manageable pieces but does not directly focus on prioritization by business value.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> A use case diagram is a visual representation of the interactions between users and the system. It does not focus on prioritizing features by business value.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> User interface flow refers to the flow of screens or steps in a user interface. It's about designing the interaction but does not prioritize features by business value.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Story Mapping is a technique used where features, epics, or user stories are prioritized and organized by business value in a sequential manner. It helps teams visualize the product from the user's perspective and prioritize work based on delivering the most value first (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 204). Option A: Story slicing involves breaking down larger user stories into smaller, manageable pieces but does not directly focus on prioritization by business value. Option B: A use case diagram is a visual representation of the interactions between users and the system. It does not focus on prioritizing features by business value. Option D: User interface flow refers to the flow of screens or steps in a user interface. It's about designing the interaction but does not prioritize features by business value.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":3,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">In which scenario would you use a Use Case Diagram over a Story Map?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In which scenario would you use a Use Case Diagram over a Story Map?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To visualize the steps in a user interface<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. To visualize the steps in a user interface\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To sequence user stories based on business value<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. To sequence user stories based on business value\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To show error-handling mechanisms between systems<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. To show error-handling mechanisms between systems\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To display system-user interactions to complete a goal<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. To display system-user interactions to complete a goal\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Use Case Diagrams are used to visualize the interactions between users (actors) and a system to achieve specific goals. They help in illustrating how a user might interact with the system to complete a task, making it ideal for showcasing the overall relationship between users and system functions.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Visualizing the steps in a user interface is typically done using a User Interface Flow, not a Use Case Diagram. A UI flow maps out the user's navigation through the system screens.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Sequencing user stories based on business value is the purpose of a Story Map, in which user stories are organized by priority and business value.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A Use Case Diagram doesn’t detail error handling between systems. For that, sequence diagrams or flowcharts are more appropriate.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Use Case Diagrams are used to visualize the interactions between users (actors) and a system to achieve specific goals. They help in illustrating how a user might interact with the system to complete a task, making it ideal for showcasing the overall relationship between users and system functions. Option A: Visualizing the steps in a user interface is typically done using a User Interface Flow, not a Use Case Diagram. A UI flow maps out the user's navigation through the system screens. Option B: Sequencing user stories based on business value is the purpose of a Story Map, in which user stories are organized by priority and business value. Option C: A Use Case Diagram doesn’t detail error handling between systems. For that, sequence diagrams or flowcharts are more appropriate.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":4,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A project manager is leading a project that has expanded significantly, including multiple teams, having a longer duration and a huge budget. As a result, the sponsor has been replaced by a steering committee. What should the project manager do to adapt to this change?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a project that has expanded significantly, including multiple teams, having a longer duration and a huge budget. As a result, the sponsor has been replaced by a steering committee. What should the project manager do to adapt to this change?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Acknowledge that the stakeholders’ structure has changed and tailor communication accordingly<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Acknowledge that the stakeholders’ structure has changed and tailor communication accordingly\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work according to the original plan while keeping in mind that the project may now include additional stakeholders<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Work according to the original plan while keeping in mind that the project may now include additional stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Hold a meeting with the new steering committee and continue working on the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Hold a meeting with the new steering committee and continue working on the project\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Share an updated status report with the new steering committee<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Share an updated status report with the new steering committee\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">On large projects, one sponsor might not be enough. A Steering Committee is established when a large project involves multiple business units, organizations, or individuals who all have a substantial stake in the project’s success and outcomes. The project manager needs to be proactive and respond to this change. The initial communication plan for a single sponsor may not work for a <span><\\/span>steering committee. To ensure effective communication with the committee, the project manager must understand their communication requirements and preferences.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A On large projects, one sponsor might not be enough. A Steering Committee is established when a large project involves multiple business units, organizations, or individuals who all have a substantial stake in the project’s success and outcomes. The project manager needs to be proactive and respond to this change. The initial communication plan for a single sponsor may not work for a steering committee. To ensure effective communication with the committee, the project manager must understand their communication requirements and preferences.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":5,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager has made certain that all of the required tasks have been accomplished. However, upon an external post-completion audit, a significant penalty was imposed on the performing organization. What could the project manager have done differently to make sure that no liabilities arose following the audit?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager has made certain that all of the required tasks have been accomplished. However, upon an external post-completion audit, a significant penalty was imposed on the performing organization. What could the project manager have done differently to make sure that no liabilities arose following the audit?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Verify that all of the tasks indicated in the scope statement were completed.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Verify that all of the tasks indicated in the scope statement were completed.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Verify that all identified defects were fixed<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Verify that all identified defects were fixed .\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensure that all documents are updated before closing the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Ensure that all documents are updated before closing the project.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensure that all closing formalities were followed as per the defined contractual procedures.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Ensure that all closing formalities were followed as per the defined contractual procedures.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In the project closing phase, the project team including the project manager, should implement the associated processes to formally complete or close a project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 171). It’s important that the closing process is done formally by following the defined procedures to avoid any future liabilities. Procedures are either established by the organization for internal projects or mutually determined by the customer and the provider in the project contract or master-level agreement (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 76). Completing project work by accomplishing all tasks in the scope, fixing defects, or updating documents, is not sufficient to avoid penalties. These activities, among others, should be formally approved by the customer first.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D In the project closing phase, the project team including the project manager, should implement the associated processes to formally complete or close a project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 171). It’s important that the closing process is done formally by following the defined procedures to avoid any future liabilities. Procedures are either established by the organization for internal projects or mutually determined by the customer and the provider in the project contract or master-level agreement (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 76). Completing project work by accomplishing all tasks in the scope, fixing defects, or updating documents, is not sufficient to avoid penalties. These activities, among others, should be formally approved by the customer first.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":6,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">An organization is launching a project to create an innovative product. The details of the components of work packages have been defined and constraints for each component have been identified. Top management requested a precise cost estimate of the project. What estimating technique should the project manager use?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An organization is launching a project to create an innovative product. The details of the components of work packages have been defined and constraints for each component have been identified. Top management requested a precise cost estimate of the project. What estimating technique should the project manager use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Top-Down<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Top-Down\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Parametric<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Parametric\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Bottom-up<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Bottom-up\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Analogous<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Analogous\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The Bottom-up estimation technique is used when project requirements are decomposed into small, feasible work elements which are then aggregated to estimate the cost of the entire project. The Bottom-up technique can be used to provide a precise estimate of both the project cost and duration.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The Bottom-up estimation technique is used when project requirements are decomposed into small, feasible work elements which are then aggregated to estimate the cost of the entire project. The Bottom-up technique can be used to provide a precise estimate of both the project cost and duration.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":7,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-1\\\">A project manager is facing a market opportunity. How should the project manager categorize an opportunity? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is facing a market opportunity. How should the project manager categorize an opportunity?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Negative risk <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Negative risk\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Positive risk <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Positive risk\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Assumption <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Assumption\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Constraint <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Constraint\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-1\\\"><span>Correct Answer = B<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-1\\\">Positive risks, also known as opportunities, represent potential events or conditions that could benefit the project if they occur. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-2\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Negative risks, or threats, are potential problems or issues that could harm the project. An opportunity is not a threat; it's a chance for a positive outcome. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-2\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Assumptions are conditions or factors that are accepted as true for the purpose of planning, but they are not opportunities. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-2\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Constraints are limitations or restrictions that affect the project, such as budget limits or resource availability. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Positive risks, also known as opportunities, represent potential events or conditions that could benefit the project if they occur. Option A: Negative risks, or threats, are potential problems or issues that could harm the project. An opportunity is not a threat; it's a chance for a positive outcome. Option C: Assumptions are conditions or factors that are accepted as true for the purpose of planning, but they are not opportunities. Option D: Constraints are limitations or restrictions that affect the project, such as budget limits or resource availability.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":8,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">After facing multiple quality issues, the project manager decided to identify top-priority defects by applying the 80/20 rule (aka the Pareto Chart). What should the project manager do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"After facing multiple quality issues, the project manager decided to identify top-priority defects by applying the 80/20 rule (aka the Pareto Chart). What should the project manager do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Find out the impact of each quality issue<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Find out the impact of each quality issue\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Find out the frequency of each quality issue<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Find out the frequency of each quality issue\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Find out the urgency of each quality issue<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Find out the urgency of each quality issue\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Find out the cause of each quality issue<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Find out the cause of each quality issue\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A Pareto diagram is a histogram that ranks issues from the ones with the highest frequency to the ones with the lowest frequency. The diagram is created according to Pareto’s Law, which states that 80 percent of the problems come from 20 percent of the issues (also known as the 80/20 rule).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A Pareto diagram is a histogram that ranks issues from the ones with the highest frequency to the ones with the lowest frequency. The diagram is created according to Pareto’s Law, which states that 80 percent of the problems come from 20 percent of the issues (also known as the 80/20 rule).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":9,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager is assessing the project’s financial status by calculating the difference between Earned Value (EV) and Actual Cost (AC). What is the project manager calculating?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assessing the project’s financial status by calculating the difference between Earned Value (EV) and Actual Cost (AC). What is the project manager calculating?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost Performance Index<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Cost Performance Index\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost Variance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Cost Variance\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Planned Value<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Planned Value\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To-Complete Performance Index<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. To-Complete Performance Index\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The amount of budget deficit or surplus at a given point in time expressed as the difference between the Earned Value (EV) and the Actual Cost (AC), is known as Cost Variance (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 238).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The amount of budget deficit or surplus at a given point in time expressed as the difference between the Earned Value (EV) and the Actual Cost (AC), is known as Cost Variance (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 238).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":10,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Adopting a predictive approach to plan a new project, a project manager chooses the ___________ method to estimate the cost by using work breakdown.<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Adopting a predictive approach to plan a new project, a project manager chooses the ___________ method to estimate the cost by using work breakdown.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Analogous<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Analogous\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Parametric<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Parametric\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Top-dow<span><\\/span>n<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Top-dow n\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Bottom-up<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Bottom-up\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The bottom-up method can be used as an estimation technique for the project's overall cost by estimating the approximate value of smaller components and using the total sum of these values to find the overall cost. This type of estimation is used to create the project schedule or budget. The project work is typically subdivided into smaller parts and each component is given a duration and cost estimate. The individual duration estimates are aggregated to determine the schedule, while the individual cost estimates are aggregated to determine the budget.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The bottom-up method can be used as an estimation technique for the project's overall cost by estimating the approximate value of smaller components and using the total sum of these values to find the overall cost. This type of estimation is used to create the project schedule or budget. The project work is typically subdivided into smaller parts and each component is given a duration and cost estimate. The individual duration estimates are aggregated to determine the schedule, while the individual cost estimates are aggregated to determine the budget.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":11,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">After purchasing a new software needed for the project, a project manager identifies a potential risk; the bought version might be old. In case that risk occurs, the project manager will just need to go to the settings and update the software version. Therefore, the project manager decides to passively accept the risk. In this case, why is passive risk acceptance the appropriate approach?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"After purchasing a new software needed for the project, a project manager identifies a potential risk; the bought version might be old. In case that risk occurs, the project manager will just need to go to the settings and update the software version. Therefore, the project manager decides to passively accept the risk. In this case, why is passive risk acceptance the appropriate approach?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Because the probability of risk occurrence is very low<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Because the probability of risk occurrence is very low\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Because the risk occurrence is difficult to identify<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Because the risk occurrence is difficult to identify\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Because it’s better to deal with trivial risks when they occur<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Because it’s better to deal with trivial risks when they occur\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Because the risk is not on the critical path<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Because the risk is not on the critical path\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Passive risk acceptance is an appropriate approach when it is best to handle the risk when it does occur. No proactive action is needed for passive acceptance other than periodically reviewing the threat to ensure that it does not change signiﬁcantly (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Passive risk acceptance is an appropriate approach when it is best to handle the risk when it does occur. No proactive action is needed for passive acceptance other than periodically reviewing the threat to ensure that it does not change signiﬁcantly (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":12,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager is leading a predictive project. After identifying a risk, the project manager decides to transfer it to another party by:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a predictive project. After identifying a risk, the project manager decides to transfer it to another party by:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Buying insurance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Buying insurance\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Accepting a lower profit in case of cost overrun<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Accepting a lower profit in case of cost overrun\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Asking the sponsor to deal with the risk<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Asking the sponsor to deal with the risk\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Eliminating the risk through beta testing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Eliminating the risk through beta testing\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Risk transfer involves transmitting future risks from one party to another. A common example of risk transfer is purchasing insurance where the risk of a person or an organization is transferred to the insurance company.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Asking the sponsor to deal with the risk is an escalation rather than a risk transfer.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options B &amp; D:<\\/span> Other risk response strategies include avoiding, mitigating, or accepting the risk (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Risk transfer involves transmitting future risks from one party to another. A common example of risk transfer is purchasing insurance where the risk of a person or an organization is transferred to the insurance company. Option C: Asking the sponsor to deal with the risk is an escalation rather than a risk transfer. Options B & D: Other risk response strategies include avoiding, mitigating, or accepting the risk (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":13,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A solar-powered car project is almost finished when the project manager receives an approved change request to replace a defective component of the car batteries. What should the project manager do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A solar-powered car project is almost finished when the project manager receives an approved change request to replace a defective component of the car batteries. What should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Record the problem in the issue log<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Record the problem in the issue log\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Meet with the change control board to discuss the matter<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Meet with the change control board to discuss the matter\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Repair the defective component<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Repair the defective component\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Replace the defective component<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Replace the defective component\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Since the project manager has received an approved change request, they should ensure its appropriate implementation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Since the change request specifically entails the replacement of the defective component, the project manager shouldn’t repair it instead.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Since the project manager has received an approved change request, they should ensure its appropriate implementation. Option C: Since the change request specifically entails the replacement of the defective component, the project manager shouldn’t repair it instead.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":14,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Due to a financial crisis, an organization decided to pause all internal projects to an undefined date. Knowing that a project manager within this organization has a weekly meeting with a subcontractor who provides the majority of the project’s physical resources, what is the best type of communication to inform this subcontractor of the contract discontinuation decision?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Due to a financial crisis, an organization decided to pause all internal projects to an undefined date. Knowing that a project manager within this organization has a weekly meeting with a subcontractor who provides the majority of the project’s physical resources, what is the best type of communication to inform this subcontractor of the contract discontinuation decision?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Informal written<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Informal written\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Formal written<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Formal written\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Informal verbal<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Informal verbal\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Formal verbal<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Formal verbal\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">When dealing with complex issues, such as updating a plan or dealing with legal matters, it would be best to document such discussions and decisions using a formal written format. According to the PMI Process groups Guide and PMBOK Guide 6th Edition (Pages 206 &amp; 499): “The buyer, usually through its authorized procurement administrator, provides the seller with formal written notice that the contract has been completed. Requirements for formal procurement closure are usually deﬁned in the terms and conditions of the contract”.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B When dealing with complex issues, such as updating a plan or dealing with legal matters, it would be best to document such discussions and decisions using a formal written format. According to the PMI Process groups Guide and PMBOK Guide 6th Edition (Pages 206 & 499): “The buyer, usually through its authorized procurement administrator, provides the seller with formal written notice that the contract has been completed. Requirements for formal procurement closure are usually deﬁned in the terms and conditions of the contract”.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":15,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project team is facing a complicated quality problem that they don’t understand its source and causes. What tool or technique should they use to trace the problem source back to its root cause?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project team is facing a complicated quality problem that they don’t understand its source and causes. What tool or technique should they use to trace the problem source back to its root cause?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Pareto diagra<span><\\/span>m<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Pareto diagra m\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Chain diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Chain diagram\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Scatter diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Scatter diagram\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Why Why diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Why Why diagram\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The Why Why diagram, known also as the Cause and effect diagram, fishbone diagram, or Ishikawa diagram, helps determine the primary or root cause of the problem by breaking down the causes of the issue into distinct branches. (PMI - Process groups guide, page 250).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The Why Why diagram, known also as the Cause and effect diagram, fishbone diagram, or Ishikawa diagram, helps determine the primary or root cause of the problem by breaking down the causes of the issue into distinct branches. (PMI - Process groups guide, page 250).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":16,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">An organization in need of accounting software conducts a make-or-buy analysis. The organization decided to go for in-house development since the analysis shows a payback period of fewer than 3 years. However, when acquiring resources, the project manager finds out that the developer's rate included in the make-or-buy analysis is only half the current rate in the market. What should the project manager do first?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An organization in need of accounting software conducts a make-or-buy analysis. The organization decided to go for in-house development since the analysis shows a payback period of fewer than 3 years. However, when acquiring resources, the project manager finds out that the developer's rate included in the make-or-buy analysis is only half the current rate in the market. What should the project manager do first?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Submit a change request.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Submit a change request.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Inform the sponsor about the findings.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Inform the sponsor about the findings.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Nothing; as long as the project’s SPI and CPI are on track, this shouldn’t be a problem.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Nothing; as long as the project’s SPI and CPI are on track, this shouldn’t be a problem.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update the make-or-buy analysis report.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Update the make-or-buy analysis report.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager should notify the sponsor of any identified risks that may impact the business value of the project. Business value measurements are used to ensure that the project deliverables remain consistent with the business case and benefits realization plans. Business value can be financial or non-financial (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 102). A make-or-buy analysis is considered a tool for measuring financial business value. The sponsor can determine whether to continue the investment or not if the payback period turns out to be more than 3 years after updating the make-or-buy analysis.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> If the sponsor agrees to carry on the project and increase its budget according to the new findings, then a change request should be issued. However, when following an adaptive approach, no change requests, SPI, or CPI are used. In this case, the project manager should inform the sponsor or the product owner about their findings and discuss whether it’s still possible to achieve the project goals or not.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> If the project is following a predictive approach, it can show assuring SPI and CPI, especially at the beginning of its execution. However, since the developer’s rate was underestimated, the project will get off-track in terms of cost later on.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The project manager should not update the make or buy analysis report without consulting or referring to the sponsor first.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The project manager should notify the sponsor of any identified risks that may impact the business value of the project. Business value measurements are used to ensure that the project deliverables remain consistent with the business case and benefits realization plans. Business value can be financial or non-financial (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 102). A make-or-buy analysis is considered a tool for measuring financial business value. The sponsor can determine whether to continue the investment or not if the payback period turns out to be more than 3 years after updating the make-or-buy analysis. Option A: If the sponsor agrees to carry on the project and increase its budget according to the new findings, then a change request should be issued. However, when following an adaptive approach, no change requests, SPI, or CPI are used. In this case, the project manager should inform the sponsor or the product owner about their findings and discuss whether it’s still possible to achieve the project goals or not. Option C: If the project is following a predictive approach, it can show assuring SPI and CPI, especially at the beginning of its execution. However, since the developer’s rate was underestimated, the project will get off-track in terms of cost later on. Option D: The project manager should not update the make or buy analysis report without consulting or referring to the sponsor first.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":17,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager is leading a software project using a predictive approach. During execution, a team member developed a new feature that caused regressions on the other features already used by the client. What should the project manager do? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a software project using a predictive approach. During execution, a team member developed a new feature that caused regressions on the other features already used by the client. What should the project manager do? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Submit a change request to fix the resulting regressions.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Submit a change request to fix the resulting regressions.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Inform the concerned stakeholders about the regressions, their impact, and the proposed solutions.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Inform the concerned stakeholders about the regressions, their impact, and the proposed solutions.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Set up a lessons-learned meeting to avoid similar issues in the future.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Set up a lessons-learned meeting to avoid similar issues in the future.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Since it’s an internal problem, try to fix it without the customer’s notice.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Since it’s an internal problem, try to fix it without the customer’s notice.\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Ignore the regressions and focus on completing the project as scheduled.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Ignore the regressions and focus on completing the project as scheduled.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, B, C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">When issues occur, the right course of action implies informing the client of what happened, suggesting potential solutions for the issue, and then submitting a change request. This is aligned with the philosophy stating “don’t bring me problems, bring me solutions” (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 28). Later on, when the issue is fixed, a lessons-learned meeting should be conducted to avoid similar problems in the future.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Holding the information and not updating the customer on what’s going on with the project can have a bad impact, both on the project and its manager’s transparency.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, B, C When issues occur, the right course of action implies informing the client of what happened, suggesting potential solutions for the issue, and then submitting a change request. This is aligned with the philosophy stating “don’t bring me problems, bring me solutions” (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 28). Later on, when the issue is fixed, a lessons-learned meeting should be conducted to avoid similar problems in the future. Option D: Holding the information and not updating the customer on what’s going on with the project can have a bad impact, both on the project and its manager’s transparency.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":18,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">An organization recently transitioned to the agile approach. However, project team members always wait for the project manager to assign them work. How can the project manager help their team be self-organized?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An organization recently transitioned to the agile approach. However, project team members always wait for the project manager to assign them work. How can the project manager help their team be self-organized?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Take a few weeks off to force the team to act on their own<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Take a few weeks off to force the team to act on their own\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Mentor the team on how to make their own decisions<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Mentor the team on how to make their own decisions\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensure that the team includes different functional expertise<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Ensure that the team includes different functional expertise\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Support the team by removing encountered impediments<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Support the team by removing encountered impediments\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager can help their team get self-organized by mentoring them on how to make their own decisions. This will empower them to pick their own tasks without waiting for assignments or asking for permission or direction from the project manager every time.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Taking a vacation is a passive approach to dealing with the problem and it won’t solve it since the team will get back to relying on the project manager as soon as they come back.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Ensuring that the team includes different functional expertise will help the team be cross-functional rather than self-organizing.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Supporting the team by removing encountered impediments is part of the agile project manager’s duties and won’t help make the team <span><\\/span>self-organizing.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The project manager can help their team get self-organized by mentoring them on how to make their own decisions. This will empower them to pick their own tasks without waiting for assignments or asking for permission or direction from the project manager every time. Option A: Taking a vacation is a passive approach to dealing with the problem and it won’t solve it since the team will get back to relying on the project manager as soon as they come back. Option C: Ensuring that the team includes different functional expertise will help the team be cross-functional rather than self-organizing. Option D: Supporting the team by removing encountered impediments is part of the agile project manager’s duties and won’t help make the team self-organizing.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":19,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager is assigned to lead a large project with a cost variance of -$40,000, an actual cost of $200,000, and a planned value of $140,000.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s1GS-1\\\">Based on these numbers, how much is the project’s Earned Value (EV)?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assigned to lead a large project with a cost variance of -$40,000, an actual cost of $200,000, and a planned value of $140,000. Based on these numbers, how much is the project’s Earned Value (EV)?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$100,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. $100,000\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$160,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. $160,000\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$180,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. $180,000\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>$240,00<span><\\/span>0<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. $240,00 0\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Cost Variance (CV) = -$40,000, Actual Cost (AC) = $200,000, and Planned Value (PV) = $140,000. The Earned Value (EV) is calculated using the following cost variance formula: CV = EV - AC, meaning that the project’s EV = CV + AC = -$40,000 + $200,000 = $160,000.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Cost Variance (CV) = -$40,000, Actual Cost (AC) = $200,000, and Planned Value (PV) = $140,000. The Earned Value (EV) is calculated using the following cost variance formula: CV = EV - AC, meaning that the project’s EV = CV + AC = -$40,000 + $200,000 = $160,000.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":20,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">The project manager resorts to management reserves to handle which type of risk?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The project manager resorts to management reserves to handle which type of risk?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Unknown unknowns<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Unknown unknowns\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Known unknowns<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Known unknowns\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business risks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Business risks\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Pure risks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Pure risks\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Management reserve is used to deal with unidentified risks, aka “unknown-unknowns”. Management reserve is part of the project budget, but it’s not part of the cost baseline. It is not an estimated reserve either; it is rather defined according to the organization’s processes and policies. It can represent 5% of the total project cost, for example. As the name indicates, this reserve is controlled by management and not by the project manager. Therefore, any usage of this reserve should be pre-approved by management (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 242).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Management reserve is used to deal with unidentified risks, aka “unknown-unknowns”. Management reserve is part of the project budget, but it’s not part of the cost baseline. It is not an estimated reserve either; it is rather defined according to the organization’s processes and policies. It can represent 5% of the total project cost, for example. As the name indicates, this reserve is controlled by management and not by the project manager. Therefore, any usage of this reserve should be pre-approved by management (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 242).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":21,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which of the following is not considered an Enterprise Environmental Factor?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is not considered an Enterprise Environmental Factor?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Organization culture<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Organization culture\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Market standards<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Market standards\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Corporate knowledge base<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Corporate knowledge base\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work authorization systems<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Work authorization systems\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A corporate knowledge base is part of the Organizational Process Assets. Enterprise Environment Factors (EEFs), however, include procedures, policies, and legislation that have an impact on how the project manager manages a project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 239). Examples of EEFs include Organizational culture, Market standards and conditions, Codes of conduct, Quality standards, Work authorization systems, Risk databases, etc. (PMI Process group, pages 38 &amp; 39)<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A corporate knowledge base is part of the Organizational Process Assets. Enterprise Environment Factors (EEFs), however, include procedures, policies, and legislation that have an impact on how the project manager manages a project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 239). Examples of EEFs include Organizational culture, Market standards and conditions, Codes of conduct, Quality standards, Work authorization systems, Risk databases, etc. (PMI Process group, pages 38 & 39)\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":22,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">From past experience, the project manager of a construction project knows that there is a risk of not receiving the needed sand supply on time. Therefore, the project manager included this potential threat in the risk management plan. If this risk were to occur, the project manager would have to purchase the sand from another supplier. But, in this case, there may be some differences in the sand quality, which would be a ____________ risk.<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"From past experience, the project manager of a construction project knows that there is a risk of not receiving the needed sand supply on time. Therefore, the project manager included this potential threat in the risk management plan. If this risk were to occur, the project manager would have to purchase the sand from another supplier. But, in this case, there may be some differences in the sand quality, which would be a ____________ risk.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Residual<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Residual\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Secondary<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Secondary\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Compliance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Compliance\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Primary<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Primary\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A secondary risk is a risk caused by a response to a primary risk; the secondary risk would not exist if the risk response was not taken.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A secondary risk is a risk caused by a response to a primary risk; the secondary risk would not exist if the risk response was not taken.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":23,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">After releasing the product, the organization faced poor quality claims from the customer. What kind of non-conformance costs the organization might incur?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"After releasing the product, the organization faced poor quality claims from the customer. What kind of non-conformance costs the organization might incur?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Internal costs<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Internal costs\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Appraisal costs<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Appraisal costs\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>External costs<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. External costs\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risks and issue response costs<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Risks and issue response costs\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Money spent during or after the project execution due to poor quality is referred to as the Cost of Non-Conformance.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Internal and External Failure Costs fall under Non-Conformance Costs.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Internal failure costs are failure costs that are associated with defects found by the project team before the product gets released, such as Rework or Scrap costs.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C<\\/span>: External Failure Costs, on the other hand, are failure costs associated with defects found by the customer, meaning costs incurred after the product is delivered to the customer, such as costs of Warranty work, Liabilities, Lost business, etc.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Money spent during or after the project execution due to poor quality is referred to as the Cost of Non-Conformance. Internal and External Failure Costs fall under Non-Conformance Costs. Option A: Internal failure costs are failure costs that are associated with defects found by the project team before the product gets released, such as Rework or Scrap costs. Option C : External Failure Costs, on the other hand, are failure costs associated with defects found by the customer, meaning costs incurred after the product is delivered to the customer, such as costs of Warranty work, Liabilities, Lost business, etc.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":24,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which of the following refers to the start-to-finish time required to develop a potentially shippable product increment?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following refers to the start-to-finish time required to develop a potentially shippable product increment?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Actual Time<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Actual Time\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cycle Time<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Cycle Time\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ideal Time<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Ideal Time\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Real Time<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Real Time\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The time it takes to complete a task from start to finish is referred to as cycle time (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 99).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; D:<\\/span> Actual Time and Real Time are used interchangeably to refer to the daily period during which team members are productively working on their assigned tasks<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> When the Agile team is fully productive and they’re not being interrupted by attending meetings or checking emails, we're talking about the Ideal Time or Ideal Days.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The time it takes to complete a task from start to finish is referred to as cycle time (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 99). Options A & D: Actual Time and Real Time are used interchangeably to refer to the daily period during which team members are productively working on their assigned tasks . Option C: When the Agile team is fully productive and they’re not being interrupted by attending meetings or checking emails, we're talking about the Ideal Time or Ideal Days.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":25,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Upon reviewing user stories, the Agile coach finds that some do not follow the common template format. Which of the following formats should the agile coach instruct the development team to follow for user stories?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Upon reviewing user stories, the Agile coach finds that some do not follow the common template format. Which of the following formats should the agile coach instruct the development team to follow for user stories?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>As a &lt;developer role&gt;, I want to develop &lt;feature&gt;<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. As a <developer role>, I want to develop <feature>\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>As a &lt;user role&gt;, I want to &lt;goal&gt;, so that &lt;benefit&gt;<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. As a <user role>, I want to <goal>, so that <benefit>\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>As a &lt;stakeholder role&gt;, I want to achieve &lt;goal&gt;<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. As a <stakeholder role>, I want to achieve <goal>\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>As a &lt;user role&gt;, I want to &lt;feature&gt;<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. As a <user role>, I want to <feature>\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-1\\\">A predefined template format is usually followed when developing user stories in order to indicate the user’s class (their role), what this class wants to realize (their goal), and why they want to achieve this goal (the benefit) (Cohn 2004). Using the term “so that” in a user story is not mandatory if the purpose is clear enough to everyone; otherwise, “so that” should definitely be used when writing each user story.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A predefined template format is usually followed when developing user stories in order to indicate the user’s class (their role), what this class wants to realize (their goal), and why they want to achieve this goal (the benefit) (Cohn 2004). Using the term “so that” in a user story is not mandatory if the purpose is clear enough to everyone; otherwise, “so that” should definitely be used when writing each user story.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":26,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">During the solution evaluation phase, a business analyst realizes that the implemented solution is underperforming and not meeting the expected business value. What actions should the business analyst take to assess and address the issue? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During the solution evaluation phase, a business analyst realizes that the implemented solution is underperforming and not meeting the expected business value. What actions should the business analyst take to assess and address the issue? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Review stakeholder engagement plans<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Review stakeholder engagement plans\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Implement a prototyping model<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Implement a prototyping model\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Conduct root cause analysis<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Conduct root cause analysis\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Revise the project scope<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Revise the project scope\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Perform cost-benefit analysis<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Perform cost-benefit analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"C\",\"E\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C &amp; E<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">​The root cause analysis technique helps identify the fundamental reasons why the solution is underperforming. It allows the business analyst to investigate why the expected business value is not being realized and uncover the variances between actual and expected results​. The cost-benefit analysis on the other hand, is used to evaluate the solution's performance against its costs. It helps determine whether the solution provides sufficient value to justify its continued use or if changes need to be made.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> While stakeholder engagement is important, it does not help diagnose or fix the underperformance of a solution.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Prototyping is a technique used during the development and design, and not to evaluate the performance of a fully implemented solution.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The issue lies with the performance of the current solution rather than the overall scope of the project. Revising the scope may be a result of findings from root cause or cost-benefit analysis, but it is not the initial step in evaluating why the solution is underperforming.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C & E The root cause analysis technique helps identify the fundamental reasons why the solution is underperforming. It allows the business analyst to investigate why the expected business value is not being realized and uncover the variances between actual and expected results. The cost-benefit analysis on the other hand, is used to evaluate the solution's performance against its costs. It helps determine whether the solution provides sufficient value to justify its continued use or if changes need to be made. Option A: While stakeholder engagement is important, it does not help diagnose or fix the underperformance of a solution. Option B: Prototyping is a technique used during the development and design, and not to evaluate the performance of a fully implemented solution. Option D: The issue lies with the performance of the current solution rather than the overall scope of the project. Revising the scope may be a result of findings from root cause or cost-benefit analysis, but it is not the initial step in evaluating why the solution is underperforming.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":27,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sFM-1\\\">The following chart was presented during a retrospective meeting. Which of the following statements is true regarding this chart?<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"The following chart was presented during a retrospective meeting. Which of the following statements is true regarding this chart?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>This burnup chart shows that there is work left at the end of the sprint.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. This burnup chart shows that there is work left at the end of the sprint.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>This burnup chart shows that the planned work is completed before the end of the sprint.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. This burnup chart shows that the planned work is completed before the end of the sprint.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>This burndown chart shows that there is work left at the end of the sprint.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. This burndown chart shows that there is work left at the end of the sprint.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>This burndown chart shows that the planned work is completed before the end of the sprint.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. This burndown chart shows that the planned work is completed before the end of the sprint.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">This chart is a burndown chart that shows that there is work left at the end of the sprint (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 108). In fact, 3 story points are left to be completed in order to finalize all the planned work for the exhibited 7-day sprint.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C This chart is a burndown chart that shows that there is work left at the end of the sprint (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 108). In fact, 3 story points are left to be completed in order to finalize all the planned work for the exhibited 7-day sprint.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":28,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager is facing some challenges because of a key stakeholder. The project manager collaborated with this stakeholder in previous projects where the latter frequently changed her requirements and created trouble whenever those requirements were not met. How should the project manager deal with this issue?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is facing some challenges because of a key stakeholder. The project manager collaborated with this stakeholder in previous projects where the latter frequently changed her requirements and created trouble whenever those requirements were not met. How should the project manager deal with this issue?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adopt an Agile approach<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Adopt an Agile approach\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Involve the concerned stakeholder right from the start<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Involve the concerned stakeholder right from the start\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ask the concerned stakeholder to mend her ways<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Ask the concerned stakeholder to mend her ways\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Inform management about the issue<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Inform management about the issue\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager should involve the key stakeholder from the very beginning of the project to help reduce and uncover risks, as well as increase her “buy-in.” While implementing an agile approach may benefit the project, it does not address the issue of stakeholder management. If the question were “what’s the appropriate approach for the project?”, then adopting an agile approach would be the right answer taking into consideration the frequently changing requirements.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The project manager should involve the key stakeholder from the very beginning of the project to help reduce and uncover risks, as well as increase her “buy-in.” While implementing an agile approach may benefit the project, it does not address the issue of stakeholder management. If the question were “what’s the appropriate approach for the project?”, then adopting an agile approach would be the right answer taking into consideration the frequently changing requirements.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":29,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A project manager is assigned to lead a project abroad. At the start of the project execution, the project manager gets worried about the country’s high levels of violence in public. The project manager gets approached by a local police officer who pledges to keep the project team safe during their stay in return for a private money transfer.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\">How should the project manager respond?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assigned to lead a project abroad. At the start of the project execution, the project manager gets worried about the country’s high levels of violence in public. The project manager gets approached by a local police officer who pledges to keep the project team safe during their stay in return for a private money transfer. How should the project manager respond?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>Not pay the police officer and ignore this incident.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Not pay the police officer and ignore this incident.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>Not pay the police officer and rather follow the chain of command.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Not pay the police officer and rather follow the chain of command.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7E\\\"><p><span>Pay the police officer and consider it as a facilitation payment.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Pay the police officer and consider it as a facilitation payment.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7H\\\"><p><span>Pay through a 3rd party considering how suspicious the situation is.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Pay through a 3rd party considering how suspicious the situation is.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In such situations, the project manager should not pay and should instead follow the chain of command and solicit their support in providing security to the project team. This situation is considered bribery or at least palm greasing. Nevertheless, the project manager should act proactively and take all security measures.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B In such situations, the project manager should not pay and should instead follow the chain of command and solicit their support in providing security to the project team. This situation is considered bribery or at least palm greasing. Nevertheless, the project manager should act proactively and take all security measures.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":30,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">During a meeting, a team member asks the project manager if there is really a difference between precision and accuracy. How should the project manager reply?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During a meeting, a team member asks the project manager if there is really a difference between precision and accuracy. How should the project manager reply?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Precision and accuracy are mutually exclusive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Precision and accuracy are mutually exclusive\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Accuracy measures exactness while precision measures correctness<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Accuracy measures exactness while precision measures correctness\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Accuracy measures correctness while precision measures exactness<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Accuracy measures correctness while precision measures exactness\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Precision and accuracy are actually the same<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Precision and accuracy are actually the same\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Accuracy describes how close a measurement is to an accepted value. Precision describes the statistical variability of produced measurement (it can be far off the accepted value) (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 55).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Accuracy describes how close a measurement is to an accepted value. Precision describes the statistical variability of produced measurement (it can be far off the accepted value) (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 55).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":31,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What is a User Story?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is a User Story?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A story that refers to the ideal user for your project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A story that refers to the ideal user for your project\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A day in the end-user life<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A day in the end-user life\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A small, granular unit of work that brings added value to the customer<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A small, granular unit of work that brings added value to the customer\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A collection of all the requirements that the customer wants in a project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A collection of all the requirements that the customer wants in a project\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A user story is a brief description of deliverable value for a specific user (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 192). A user story is not a narrative story about users; it is a small, granular work unit.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A user story is a brief description of deliverable value for a specific user (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 192). A user story is not a narrative story about users; it is a small, granular work unit.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":32,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What is the primary benefit of focus groups during requirements elicitation?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the primary benefit of focus groups during requirements elicitation?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Enable direct feedback from customers<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Enable direct feedback from customers\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Provide anonymous feedback<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Provide anonymous feedback\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Are conducted at the project closeout<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Are conducted at the project closeout\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Offer documented responses from stakeholder<span><\\/span>s<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Offer documented responses from stakeholder s\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Focus groups are designed to gather input and feedback directly from participants, typically including customers, users, or prequalified stakeholders, during the requirements elicitation phase of a project. The primary benefit is the opportunity for direct interaction and discussion, which helps uncover detailed requirements, preferences, and issues.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Focus groups are generally not anonymous; the participants are known, and the purpose is to facilitate open discussion where everyone can interact. Anonymous feedback is more characteristic of surveys or other methods that don't involve direct interaction.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Focus groups are not typically conducted at project closeout. They are most useful during the early phases of the project, especially during requirements gathering, to ensure that the project aligns with stakeholder needs.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> While focus groups can produce documented outcomes, this is not their primary benefit. The key value lies in the real-time interaction and discussion rather than just capturing responses. Surveys or interviews are more focused on collecting documented responses.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Focus groups are designed to gather input and feedback directly from participants, typically including customers, users, or prequalified stakeholders, during the requirements elicitation phase of a project. The primary benefit is the opportunity for direct interaction and discussion, which helps uncover detailed requirements, preferences, and issues. Option B: Focus groups are generally not anonymous; the participants are known, and the purpose is to facilitate open discussion where everyone can interact. Anonymous feedback is more characteristic of surveys or other methods that don't involve direct interaction. Option C: Focus groups are not typically conducted at project closeout. They are most useful during the early phases of the project, especially during requirements gathering, to ensure that the project aligns with stakeholder needs. Option D: While focus groups can produce documented outcomes, this is not their primary benefit. The key value lies in the real-time interaction and discussion rather than just capturing responses. Surveys or interviews are more focused on collecting documented responses.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":33,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">An Agile project manager is leading a software project using the Scrum framework. While the team implements user stories during the sprint, what should the product owner do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An Agile project manager is leading a software project using the Scrum framework. While the team implements user stories during the sprint, what should the product owner do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Add more tasks for the team so they can deliver more value<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Add more tasks for the team so they can deliver more value\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Let the team do their work and respond to any questions they might have<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Let the team do their work and respond to any questions they might have\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Protect the team from interruptions and facilitate discussions<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Protect the team from interruptions and facilitate discussions\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Monitor the sprint progress and extend its duration if the team cannot complete the assigned work on time<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Monitor the sprint progress and extend its duration if the team cannot complete the assigned work on time\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The product owner should let the team do their work and answer any questions they might have during the sprint.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The product owner should not add more tasks.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Facilitating and protecting the team from interruptions are among the scrum master’s responsibilities.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The sprint duration is determined at the beginning of the project and typically does not change. Furthermore, any work items that cannot be completed by the team during the sprint should be put back in the backlog and rescheduled for the upcoming sprints<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The product owner should let the team do their work and answer any questions they might have during the sprint. Option A: The product owner should not add more tasks. Option C: Facilitating and protecting the team from interruptions are among the scrum master’s responsibilities. Option D: The sprint duration is determined at the beginning of the project and typically does not change. Furthermore, any work items that cannot be completed by the team during the sprint should be put back in the backlog and rescheduled for the upcoming sprints .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":34,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which technique is best for engaging cross-functional stakeholders in a structured meeting to define product information?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which technique is best for engaging cross-functional stakeholders in a structured meeting to define product information?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Surveys<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Surveys\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Facilitated workshops<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Facilitated workshops\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Observation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Observation\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Focus groups<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Focus groups\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Facilitated workshops are highly effective for engaging cross-functional stakeholders in a structured environment. They bring together different teams or departments to collaboratively define product information, requirements, and solutions. The structured nature of the workshop allows for focused discussions and ensures that stakeholders from various functions can contribute their perspectives.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Surveys are useful for gathering input from a broad group of stakeholders but do not provide the interactive or collaborative engagement needed to define product information in real-time, especially with cross-functional teams.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Observation involves watching how stakeholders or users interact with a product or system, but it doesn’t actively engage them in a structured discussion or collaborative effort to define product information.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Focus groups are used to collect feedback and opinions from a specific group of stakeholders but are less structured and collaborative than facilitated workshops, which are specifically designed to engage cross-functional teams in a focused, interactive environment.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Facilitated workshops are highly effective for engaging cross-functional stakeholders in a structured environment. They bring together different teams or departments to collaboratively define product information, requirements, and solutions. The structured nature of the workshop allows for focused discussions and ensures that stakeholders from various functions can contribute their perspectives. Option A: Surveys are useful for gathering input from a broad group of stakeholders but do not provide the interactive or collaborative engagement needed to define product information in real-time, especially with cross-functional teams. Option C: Observation involves watching how stakeholders or users interact with a product or system, but it doesn’t actively engage them in a structured discussion or collaborative effort to define product information. Option D: Focus groups are used to collect feedback and opinions from a specific group of stakeholders but are less structured and collaborative than facilitated workshops, which are specifically designed to engage cross-functional teams in a focused, interactive environment.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":35,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What is the primary benefit of a traceability matrix in managing scope creep?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the primary benefit of a traceability matrix in managing scope creep?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It tracks the financials of the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. It tracks the financials of the project\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It records all stakeholder decisions<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. It records all stakeholder decisions\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It manages team assignments effectively<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. It manages team assignments effectively\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It ensures that only approved requirements are incorporated into the solution<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. It ensures that only approved requirements are incorporated into the solution\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A traceability matrix helps manage scope creep by linking requirements to their source (e.g., stakeholders, project goals) and ensuring that only approved and necessary changes are incorporated into the final product or solution. This prevents unnecessary features or requirements from being added, which is a primary cause of scope creep.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The traceability matrix is not primarily used for tracking financials; its focus is on tracking requirements and ensuring they are aligned with project objectives and deliverables.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> While the traceability matrix might reference some stakeholder decisions regarding requirements, its main purpose is to track the flow and relationship of requirements rather than serve as a record of all stakeholder decisions.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The traceability matrix is not a tool for managing team assignments; it is used to ensure that requirements are properly addressed and tracked throughout the project to prevent scope creep. Team assignments are typically managed through other project management tools.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D A traceability matrix helps manage scope creep by linking requirements to their source (e.g., stakeholders, project goals) and ensuring that only approved and necessary changes are incorporated into the final product or solution. This prevents unnecessary features or requirements from being added, which is a primary cause of scope creep. Option A: The traceability matrix is not primarily used for tracking financials; its focus is on tracking requirements and ensuring they are aligned with project objectives and deliverables. Option B: While the traceability matrix might reference some stakeholder decisions regarding requirements, its main purpose is to track the flow and relationship of requirements rather than serve as a record of all stakeholder decisions. Option C: The traceability matrix is not a tool for managing team assignments; it is used to ensure that requirements are properly addressed and tracked throughout the project to prevent scope creep. Team assignments are typically managed through other project management tools.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":36,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which of the following is a risk quantification method?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is a risk quantification method?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Decision tree analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Decision tree analysis\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Histogram analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Histogram analysis\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost-benefit analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Cost-benefit analysis\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Benchmarking<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Benchmarking\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Decision Tree Analysis is a risk quantification method that helps project managers evaluate the potential outcomes, risks, and rewards of various decisions. It quantifies risks by assigning probabilities and values to different branches of the tree, aiding in decision-making (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 175).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Histogram Analysis is a tool used to visualize data distribution<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Cost-Benefit Analysis compares the costs and benefits of a project but doesn't directly quantify risks.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Benchmarking involves comparing performance metrics to industry standards or best practices.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Decision Tree Analysis is a risk quantification method that helps project managers evaluate the potential outcomes, risks, and rewards of various decisions. It quantifies risks by assigning probabilities and values to different branches of the tree, aiding in decision-making (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 175). Option B: Histogram Analysis is a tool used to visualize data distribution . Option C: The Cost-Benefit Analysis compares the costs and benefits of a project but doesn't directly quantify risks. Option D: Benchmarking involves comparing performance metrics to industry standards or best practices.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":37,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What is the primary focus of the Measurement Performance Domain?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the primary focus of the Measurement Performance Domain?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Assessing project performance against objectives<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Assessing project performance against objectives\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Tracking project costs<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Tracking project costs\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensuring project timelines are met<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Ensuring project timelines are met\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Managing stakeholder communications<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Managing stakeholder communications\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The Measurement Performance Domain focuses on assessing how well the project is performing in relation to its objectives. It involves tracking progress, evaluating performance metrics, and determining whether the project is meeting its intended goals (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 58).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Tracking project costs is related to cost management.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Ensuring project timelines are met is a part of schedule management.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Managing stakeholder communications is part of communication management.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The Measurement Performance Domain focuses on assessing how well the project is performing in relation to its objectives. It involves tracking progress, evaluating performance metrics, and determining whether the project is meeting its intended goals (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 58). Option B: Tracking project costs is related to cost management. Option C: Ensuring project timelines are met is a part of schedule management. Option D: Managing stakeholder communications is part of communication management.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":38,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">All of the following are values of the Agile Manifesto, except for:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"All of the following are values of the Agile Manifesto, except for:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Individuals and interactions over processes and tools<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Individuals and interactions over processes and tools\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Working software over comprehensive documentatio<span><\\/span>n<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Working software over comprehensive documentatio n\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Customer collaboration over contract negotiation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Customer collaboration over contract negotiation\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Following an iteration over following a plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Following an iteration over following a plan\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The correct value is “Responding to Change over Following a Plan”. All of the other alternatives are the right values of the Agile Manifesto (Agile Practice Guide, page 8).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The correct value is “Responding to Change over Following a Plan”. All of the other alternatives are the right values of the Agile Manifesto (Agile Practice Guide, page 8).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":39,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">In adaptive life cycles, how is the scope of deliverables typically managed?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In adaptive life cycles, how is the scope of deliverables typically managed?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Defined at the beginning of the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Defined at the beginning of the project\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Fixed and unchanging throughout the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Fixed and unchanging throughout the project\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Developed and approved at the beginning of each iteration<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Developed and approved at the beginning of each iteration\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Pre-determined by the project sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Pre-determined by the project sponsor\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In adaptive life cycles such as Agile, the deliverables are developed over multiple iterations. A detailed scope is defined and approved at the beginning of each iteration, allowing flexibility to accommodate changes throughout the project (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 16).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The scope is established upfront and remains largely fixed throughout the project in a predictive (or waterfall) approach, which doesn't apply to adaptive life cycles in which the scope evolves.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> A Fixed and unchanging scope throughout the project contradicts the iterative nature of adaptive life cycles, in which changes and refinements are continuously incorporated at the beginning of each iteration.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> While sponsors may influence the overall direction and high-level objectives, the detailed scope in adaptive life cycles is typically determined by the team and stakeholders at the beginning of each iteration, not pre-determined by a single individual​.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C In adaptive life cycles such as Agile, the deliverables are developed over multiple iterations. A detailed scope is defined and approved at the beginning of each iteration, allowing flexibility to accommodate changes throughout the project (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 16). Option A: The scope is established upfront and remains largely fixed throughout the project in a predictive (or waterfall) approach, which doesn't apply to adaptive life cycles in which the scope evolves. Option B: A Fixed and unchanging scope throughout the project contradicts the iterative nature of adaptive life cycles, in which changes and refinements are continuously incorporated at the beginning of each iteration. Option C: While sponsors may influence the overall direction and high-level objectives, the detailed scope in adaptive life cycles is typically determined by the team and stakeholders at the beginning of each iteration, not pre-determined by a single individual.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":40,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A sales representative of a luxurious hotel chain asked a local carpenter, who owns a small workshop specialized in designing and manufacturing outdoor furniture, to produce a single unit of a new concept of egg chairs as quickly and inexpensively as possible. What is this product called?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A sales representative of a luxurious hotel chain asked a local carpenter, who owns a small workshop specialized in designing and manufacturing outdoor furniture, to produce a single unit of a new concept of egg chairs as quickly and inexpensively as possible. What is this product called?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Pre-production version<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Pre-production version\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product increment<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Product increment\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Minimum viable product<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Minimum viable product\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sample<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Sample\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A Minimum Viable Product (MVP) is a prototype with just enough features to be presented to early users, who can then provide feedback for future product development (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 243)<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> An MVP could be subject to many changes and subsequent prototypes, thus it can’t be considered a pre-production version.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Product increment involves a workable increment delivered at the end of each iteration.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A sample is a small part of a product intended to demonstrate the characteristics of the whole product.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A Minimum Viable Product (MVP) is a prototype with just enough features to be presented to early users, who can then provide feedback for future product development (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 243) . Option A: An MVP could be subject to many changes and subsequent prototypes, thus it can’t be considered a pre-production version. Option B: Product increment involves a workable increment delivered at the end of each iteration. Option D: A sample is a small part of a product intended to demonstrate the characteristics of the whole product.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":41,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What is the role of the project manager in resolving conflicts within the team?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the role of the project manager in resolving conflicts within the team?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Assign responsibility to higher management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Assign responsibility to higher management\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Focus on past conflicts for reference<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Focus on past conflicts for reference\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Avoid confronting conflict<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Avoid confronting conflict\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Focus on the issues and not the people<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Focus on the issues and not the people\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The role of the project manager in resolving conflicts within the team is to focus on the issues and not the people involved. By concentrating on the root cause of the conflict rather than personal differences, the project manager can facilitate constructive dialogue and find solutions that address the problem without creating personal hostility (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 30).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Assigning responsibility to higher management is not an effective conflict resolution strategy for a project manager, as they are expected to handle team conflicts.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Focusing on past conflicts for reference may not be helpful and could lead to unresolved tensions.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Avoiding confrontation is not a proactive way to resolve conflicts and may lead to more significant issues later.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The role of the project manager in resolving conflicts within the team is to focus on the issues and not the people involved. By concentrating on the root cause of the conflict rather than personal differences, the project manager can facilitate constructive dialogue and find solutions that address the problem without creating personal hostility (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 30). Option A: Assigning responsibility to higher management is not an effective conflict resolution strategy for a project manager, as they are expected to handle team conflicts. Option B: Focusing on past conflicts for reference may not be helpful and could lead to unresolved tensions. Option C: Avoiding confrontation is not a proactive way to resolve conflicts and may lead to more significant issues later.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":42,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">In which process does the monitoring of the project status takes place to update project costs and manage the cost baseline?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In which process does the monitoring of the project status takes place to update project costs and manage the cost baseline?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Plan cost management<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Plan cost management\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Control costs<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Control costs\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Determine budget<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Determine budget\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Estimate costs<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Estimate costs\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Control Costs is the process of monitoring and updating project costs while managing changes to the cost baseline. The key benefit is ensuring the cost baseline remains stable throughout the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Plan cost management is the process that determines how the cost will be managed. This process is conducted in the “Planning” phase, while the control costs process is conducted in the “Monitoring &amp; Controlling” phase.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Determine Budget is the process of consolidating the estimated costs of individual activities or work packages to create an authorized cost baseline.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Estimate cost is the process of approximating the financial resources required to complete the project’s work.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Control Costs is the process of monitoring and updating project costs while managing changes to the cost baseline. The key benefit is ensuring the cost baseline remains stable throughout the project. Option A: Plan cost management is the process that determines how the cost will be managed. This process is conducted in the “Planning” phase, while the control costs process is conducted in the “Monitoring & Controlling” phase. Option C: Determine Budget is the process of consolidating the estimated costs of individual activities or work packages to create an authorized cost baseline. Option D: Estimate cost is the process of approximating the financial resources required to complete the project’s work.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":43,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager is managing a web application project using the Agile approach. During the first sprint, the team completed 4 tasks of 3, 5, 8, and 2 story points respectively. They also finished half a 13-story points task. What is the velocity of the team?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is managing a web application project using the Agile approach. During the first sprint, the team completed 4 tasks of 3, 5, 8, and 2 story points respectively. They also finished half a 13-story points task. What is the velocity of the team?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>18 story points<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. 18 story points\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>24.5 story points<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. 24.5 story points\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>31 story points<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. 31 story points\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>13 story point<span><\\/span>s<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. 13 story point s\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Velocity is a measure of the amount of fully completed work in a sprint. Partially done tasks should not be counted. In this case, velocity = 3 + 5 + 8 + 2 = 18 points.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Velocity is a measure of the amount of fully completed work in a sprint. Partially done tasks should not be counted. In this case, velocity = 3 + 5 + 8 + 2 = 18 points.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":44,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager is managing a construction project. The project manager identified a risk that might affect work execution due to an equipment malfunction. Which of the following risk response strategies should the project manager use? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is managing a construction project. The project manager identified a risk that might affect work execution due to an equipment malfunction. Which of the following risk response strategies should the project manager use? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Exploit<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Exploit\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Enhance<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Enhance\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Mitigate<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Mitigate\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Avoid<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Avoid\"}],\"key\":[\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C &amp; D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">This is an example of negative risk, therefore, the project manager should use either mitigation to minimize the impact of the risk or avoidance to completely eliminate the risk<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; B:<\\/span> Exploit and enhance are positive risk response strategies (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 123 &amp; 125).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C & D This is an example of negative risk, therefore, the project manager should use either mitigation to minimize the impact of the risk or avoidance to completely eliminate the risk . Options A & B: Exploit and enhance are positive risk response strategies (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 123 & 125).\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":45,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-1\\\">In order to monitor and track the progress of project performance, the organization’s management uses earned value measurements. Which of the following values is an indication that a project has issues? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In order to monitor and track the progress of project performance, the organization’s management uses earned value measurements. Which of the following values is an indication that a project has issues?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>A CPI of 0.89<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A CPI of 0.89\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An SPI of 0.99<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. An SPI of 0.99\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A CPI of 1.01<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A CPI of 1.01\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A BAC of $100,000<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A BAC of $100,000\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-1\\\"><span>Correct Answer = A<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-1\\\">A Cost Performance Index (CPI) of less than 1 means that the project is over budget. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-2\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> A 0.99 SPI means that the project can be considered on schedule (SPI = 1 means that the project is perfectly on schedule). <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-2\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A CPI of 1 indicates that the project is on budget. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-2\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Requirements can dictate that the project’s final budget should be $100,000 (Budget At Completion, BAC), which is considered a constraint rather than an issue. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A Cost Performance Index (CPI) of less than 1 means that the project is over budget. Option B: A 0.99 SPI means that the project can be considered on schedule (SPI = 1 means that the project is perfectly on schedule). Option C: A CPI of 1 indicates that the project is on budget. Option D: Requirements can dictate that the project’s final budget should be $100,000 (Budget At Completion, BAC), which is considered a constraint rather than an issue.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":46,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What is the significance of performing business analysis before a project initiation?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the significance of performing business analysis before a project initiation?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To ensure a clear and correct definition of the problem<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. To ensure a clear and correct definition of the problem\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To improve the project timeline<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. To improve the project timeline\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To allocate project resources more effectively<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. To allocate project resources more effectively\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To improve stakeholder involvement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. To improve stakeholder involvement\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Business analysis is fundamentally about understanding the problem or opportunity the organization is facing. One of the key roles of business analysis is to conduct a thorough needs assessment to ensure that the root causes of problems are understood, rather than addressing symptoms repeatedly. This step is crucial before project initiation to provide clarity on the problem and set a proper foundation for the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> While business analysis may indirectly contribute to a smoother timeline by reducing rework and clarifying requirements, improving the timeline is not the primary purpose of conducting business analysis before project initiation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Resource allocation is more relevant to project planning, which happens after the initiation phase. Business analysis ensures the problem is well-defined and not directly related to resource management.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Although business analysis involves stakeholders for eliciting requirements, its primary role in the pre-initiation phase is not to improve stakeholder involvement but to clearly define the problem.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Business analysis is fundamentally about understanding the problem or opportunity the organization is facing. One of the key roles of business analysis is to conduct a thorough needs assessment to ensure that the root causes of problems are understood, rather than addressing symptoms repeatedly. This step is crucial before project initiation to provide clarity on the problem and set a proper foundation for the project. Option B: While business analysis may indirectly contribute to a smoother timeline by reducing rework and clarifying requirements, improving the timeline is not the primary purpose of conducting business analysis before project initiation. Option C: Resource allocation is more relevant to project planning, which happens after the initiation phase. Business analysis ensures the problem is well-defined and not directly related to resource management. Option D: Although business analysis involves stakeholders for eliciting requirements, its primary role in the pre-initiation phase is not to improve stakeholder involvement but to clearly define the problem.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":47,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-1\\\">During the planning phase of the project, the project manager observed that several stakeholders were unsupportive, fearing job losses as a result of the project. What should the project manager do to address this issue? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During the planning phase of the project, the project manager observed that several stakeholders were unsupportive, fearing job losses as a result of the project. What should the project manager do to address this issue?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s6GB\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Disregard the project’s unsupportive stakeholders. <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Disregard the project’s unsupportive stakeholders.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s6GE\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use the autocratic leadership style to be able to lead the project. <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Use the autocratic leadership style to be able to lead the project.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s6GE\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create an effective communication management plan and stakeholder engagement plan. <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Create an effective communication management plan and stakeholder engagement plan.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s6GE\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Refuse to work on a project that might lead to job losses. <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Refuse to work on a project that might lead to job losses.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The best course of action for the project manager to handle unsupportive stakeholders is to create an efficient communication plan as well as a stakeholder engagement plan. As a project manager, you can’t disregard or ignore any stakeholders regardless of their attitude towards your project. If anything, you should give more attention and put more effort into engaging unsupportive ones in case they have a key role or big influence on your project. An efficient communication management plan and stakeholder engagement plan will help you identify these unsupportive stakeholders’ level of interest and power and plan your communication and the way you’re going to engage them accordingly, making it easier to ensure their collaboration and even possible to win their support<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Refusing to manage the project doesn’t mean the project will be canceled, thus it won’t change the fact that certain stakeholders will still lose their jobs. Moreover, since the project was chosen for execution, it’s intended to bring added value despite its downside for some involved stakeholders.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The best course of action for the project manager to handle unsupportive stakeholders is to create an efficient communication plan as well as a stakeholder engagement plan. As a project manager, you can’t disregard or ignore any stakeholders regardless of their attitude towards your project. If anything, you should give more attention and put more effort into engaging unsupportive ones in case they have a key role or big influence on your project. An efficient communication management plan and stakeholder engagement plan will help you identify these unsupportive stakeholders’ level of interest and power and plan your communication and the way you’re going to engage them accordingly, making it easier to ensure their collaboration and even possible to win their support . Option D: Refusing to manage the project doesn’t mean the project will be canceled, thus it won’t change the fact that certain stakeholders will still lose their jobs. Moreover, since the project was chosen for execution, it’s intended to bring added value despite its downside for some involved stakeholders.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":48,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager is in the phase of identifying and evaluating the risks of a construction project. One of the identified risks is so complex and ambiguous that the project manager decides to transfer it to the program manager so the latter can make the appropriate decision. How did the project manager respond to the risk?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is in the phase of identifying and evaluating the risks of a construction project. One of the identified risks is so complex and ambiguous that the project manager decides to transfer it to the program manager so the latter can make the appropriate decision. How did the project manager respond to the risk?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Transfer<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Transfer\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Mitigate​<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Mitigate\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Escalate<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Escalate\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Avoi<span><\\/span>d<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Avoi d\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In the described scenario, the project manager has escalated the risk to the program manager. When a threat is considered to be outside the project scope or when the appropriate response exceeds the project manager’s authority, risk escalation is the suitable risk response strategy (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123). Risk escalation involves passing the risk to the right owner (the program manager in this case) to ensure that it is recognized, understood, and managed appropriately.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Transferring the risk entails shifting the threat ownership and responsibility to a third party which may involve payment of a risk premium to the third party assuming the threat.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Risk mitigation implies decreasing the threat probability of occurrence and/or impact.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Avoiding the risk means eliminating the threat or protecting the project from its impact.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C In the described scenario, the project manager has escalated the risk to the program manager. When a threat is considered to be outside the project scope or when the appropriate response exceeds the project manager’s authority, risk escalation is the suitable risk response strategy (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123). Risk escalation involves passing the risk to the right owner (the program manager in this case) to ensure that it is recognized, understood, and managed appropriately. Option A: Transferring the risk entails shifting the threat ownership and responsibility to a third party which may involve payment of a risk premium to the third party assuming the threat. Option B: Risk mitigation implies decreasing the threat probability of occurrence and/or impact. Option D: Avoiding the risk means eliminating the threat or protecting the project from its impact.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":49,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">The process of backlog refinement involves:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The process of backlog refinement involves:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The identification of the work items to be accomplished during the next sprint.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The identification of the work items to be accomplished during the next sprint.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Using a board to keep track of the product and sprint backlogs.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Using a board to keep track of the product and sprint backlogs.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Prioritizing a list of product requirements which is maintained by the project team.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Prioritizing a list of product requirements which is maintained by the project team.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The gradual development of product specifications to meet the needs of the product owner.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The gradual development of product specifications to meet the needs of the product owner.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Backlog refinement refers to the progressive elaboration of project requirements where the Agile team collaboratively integrates reviews and updates with the sole purpose of satisfying the customer and product owner’s needs (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 235).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The identification of the work items to be accomplished during the next sprint is carried out during the sprint planning.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> An information radiator or a Kanban board helps to keep track of the product and sprint backlogs.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The backlog is a prioritized list of product requirements that is maintained by the team.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Backlog refinement refers to the progressive elaboration of project requirements where the Agile team collaboratively integrates reviews and updates with the sole purpose of satisfying the customer and product owner’s needs (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 235). Option A: The identification of the work items to be accomplished during the next sprint is carried out during the sprint planning. Option B: An information radiator or a Kanban board helps to keep track of the product and sprint backlogs. Option C: The backlog is a prioritized list of product requirements that is maintained by the team.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":50,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Despite creating an agenda and timeboxing the meetings, the project manager struggles to engage all attendees. What should the project manager do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Despite creating an agenda and timeboxing the meetings, the project manager struggles to engage all attendees. What should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Make meetings shorter to prevent boredom.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Make meetings shorter to prevent boredom.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Limit the interventions of the most talkative attendees to allow others to participate.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Limit the interventions of the most talkative attendees to allow others to participate.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Change to remote meetings to make everyone feel more comfortable.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Change to remote meetings to make everyone feel more comfortable.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Encourage all attendees to participate and share their thoughts by asking for their opinions on the discussed matters.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Encourage all attendees to participate and share their thoughts by asking for their opinions on the discussed matters.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">As a facilitator, the project manager must ensure that all attendees take part in the meeting by encouraging them to share their ideas and opinions and engaging them in the discussed topics. It’s among their responsibilities as a facilitator to ensure that everyone takes part in the decision-making, problem-solving, brainstorming, etc. activities that take place during meetings.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Promoting participation and maintaining the ideas and discussions flow during such events is an indication of efficient facilitation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; C:<\\/span> Changing meetings from face-to-face to virtual or limiting their duration does not guarantee more engagement or participation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Limiting the intervention of talkative participants will only result in more inactive attendees<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D As a facilitator, the project manager must ensure that all attendees take part in the meeting by encouraging them to share their ideas and opinions and engaging them in the discussed topics. It’s among their responsibilities as a facilitator to ensure that everyone takes part in the decision-making, problem-solving, brainstorming, etc. activities that take place during meetings. Promoting participation and maintaining the ideas and discussions flow during such events is an indication of efficient facilitation. Options A & C: Changing meetings from face-to-face to virtual or limiting their duration does not guarantee more engagement or participation. Option B: Limiting the intervention of talkative participants will only result in more inactive attendees .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":51,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What is Velocity?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is Velocity?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A team's sprint-by-sprint progress rate<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A team's sprint-by-sprint progress rate\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project execution speed<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project execution speed\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Team members’ average capacity<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Team members’ average capacity\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>All of the above<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. All of the above\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Velocity refers to a Scrum development team’s rate of delivering business value. An agile team’s velocity is calculated by simply adding up the estimates or story points of all the features, user stories, requirements, or tasks successfully delivered by all team members during an iteration.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Velocity refers to a Scrum development team’s rate of delivering business value. An agile team’s velocity is calculated by simply adding up the estimates or story points of all the features, user stories, requirements, or tasks successfully delivered by all team members during an iteration.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":52,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A3-1\\\">A project manager is assigned to lead a project. During the project planning phase, the defined scope was approved by management and all stakeholders. During the execution of the project work, two key stakeholders ask the project manager to change a particular part of the scope statement. What should the project manager do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assigned to lead a project. During the project planning phase, the defined scope was approved by management and all stakeholders. During the execution of the project work, two key stakeholders ask the project manager to change a particular part of the scope statement. What should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Ask the stakeholders to submit a change request.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Ask the stakeholders to submit a change request.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Refuse to alter the scope since it has already been approved by all stakeholders.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Refuse to alter the scope since it has already been approved by all stakeholders.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Refuse to alter the scope since it cannot be modified after being officially approved.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Refuse to alter the scope since it cannot be modified after being officially approved.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Refer the stakeholders to the project sponsor.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Refer the stakeholders to the project sponsor.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-1\\\">The stakeholders can submit a change request that can be recorded, evaluated, and either approved or rejected by the Change Control Board (CCB). As long as the change management process is followed, the project scope can be changed. The project sponsor could be part of the CCB which will be deciding on the stakeholders' change request. Therefore, it’s not appropriate for the project manager to escalate the situation to the project sponsor.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The stakeholders can submit a change request that can be recorded, evaluated, and either approved or rejected by the Change Control Board (CCB). As long as the change management process is followed, the project scope can be changed. The project sponsor could be part of the CCB which will be deciding on the stakeholders' change request. Therefore, it’s not appropriate for the project manager to escalate the situation to the project sponsor.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":53,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What acronym describes the characteristics of a well-refined product backlog?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What acronym describes the characteristics of a well-refined product backlog?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>DEEP<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. DEEP\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>SMART<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. SMART\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>INVEST<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. INVEST\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>LEAN<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. LEAN\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The acronym DEEP describes the characteristics of a well-refined product backlog. It stands for:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Detailed appropriately: Items are sufficiently detailed for the stage they are in.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Emergent: The backlog evolves as more is learned about the product.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Estimable: Items should be estimable, meaning the team can provide a rough idea of the effort required.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Prioritized: Items are ranked in order of importance or business value.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> SMART is a common acronym for setting goals (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, and Time-bound).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> INVEST is an acronym used to describe good user stories (Independent, Negotiable, Valuable, Estimable, Small, Testable).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Lean refers to a methodology focused on minimizing waste and maximizing value.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The acronym DEEP describes the characteristics of a well-refined product backlog. It stands for: ● Detailed appropriately: Items are sufficiently detailed for the stage they are in. ● Emergent: The backlog evolves as more is learned about the product. ● Estimable: Items should be estimable, meaning the team can provide a rough idea of the effort required. ● Prioritized: Items are ranked in order of importance or business value. Option B: SMART is a common acronym for setting goals (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, and Time-bound). Option C: INVEST is an acronym used to describe good user stories (Independent, Negotiable, Valuable, Estimable, Small, Testable). Option D: Lean refers to a methodology focused on minimizing waste and maximizing value.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":54,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project involves a large number of stakeholders from various time zones. The project is facing delays due to disagreements on a schedule that accommodates everyone. To address this, the project manager has decided to focus solely on stakeholders within the same time zone. What should the project manager do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project involves a large number of stakeholders from various time zones. The project is facing delays due to disagreements on a schedule that accommodates everyone. To address this, the project manager has decided to focus solely on stakeholders within the same time zone. What should the project manager do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Update the assumption log.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Update the assumption log.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Send the requirements documents to all stakeholders to review them.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Send the requirements documents to all stakeholders to review them.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Update the risk register by adding the associated risks.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Update the risk register by adding the associated risks.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Ignore the low-power stakeholders.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Ignore the low-power stakeholders.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager is facing a risk of not meeting the requirements or expectations of all stakeholders. The artifact of risk identification is the risk register, therefore upon identifying a risk the risk register should be updated.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The project manager is facing a risk not an assumption.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Sending to all stakeholders contradicts the project manager’s intention to focus solely on a group of stakeholders.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The project manager already took the decision to ignore stakeholders based on time zone, not on power.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The project manager is facing a risk of not meeting the requirements or expectations of all stakeholders. The artifact of risk identification is the risk register, therefore upon identifying a risk the risk register should be updated. Option A: The project manager is facing a risk not an assumption. Option B: Sending to all stakeholders contradicts the project manager’s intention to focus solely on a group of stakeholders. Option D: The project manager already took the decision to ignore stakeholders based on time zone, not on power.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":55,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">To estimate the cost of building a standard type of office space, a project manager multiplies the standard rate of one square foot by the total number of square feet required for the new project. What estimation method did the project manager use?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"To estimate the cost of building a standard type of office space, a project manager multiplies the standard rate of one square foot by the total number of square feet required for the new project. What estimation method did the project manager use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p>Analogous estimating <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Analogous estimating\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-1\\\"><p><span>Parametric estimating<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Parametric estimating\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-1\\\"><p><span>Relative estimating<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Relative estimating\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-1\\\"><p><span>Three-point estimating<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Three-point estimating\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Parametric estimating calculates cost or duration by using an algorithm that leverages historical data and project-specific parameters.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Analogous estimating determines the duration or cost of an activity or project by using historical data from similar past activities or projects.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Relative estimating involves creating estimates by comparing the effort, complexity, and uncertainty of a task to similar past work. This method doesn't rely on absolute units of cost or time. Instead, it often uses unitless measures like story points to gauge the relative size and difficulty of tasks.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Three-point estimating calculates cost or duration by averaging or weighting the optimistic, pessimistic, and most likely estimates to address uncertainty in individual activity estimates.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Parametric estimating calculates cost or duration by using an algorithm that leverages historical data and project-specific parameters. Option A: Analogous estimating determines the duration or cost of an activity or project by using historical data from similar past activities or projects. Option C: Relative estimating involves creating estimates by comparing the effort, complexity, and uncertainty of a task to similar past work. This method doesn't rely on absolute units of cost or time. Instead, it often uses unitless measures like story points to gauge the relative size and difficulty of tasks. Option D: Three-point estimating calculates cost or duration by averaging or weighting the optimistic, pessimistic, and most likely estimates to address uncertainty in individual activity estimates.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":56,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">An approach to adaptive project estimation requires evaluating a user story based on uncertainty, size, and what other attribute?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An approach to adaptive project estimation requires evaluating a user story based on uncertainty, size, and what other attribute?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Cost<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Cost\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Scope<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Scope\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Schedule<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Schedule\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Complexity<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Complexity\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Complexity reflects how challenging a user story is to implement. It includes technical difficulties, integration issues, and other factors that affect the effort required to complete the story.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Cost is not used in the initial estimation of user stories.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The scope is related to the overall project goals and deliverables but it's not usually a direct attribute in the initial estimation of individual user stories.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Scheduling is related to the project timeline and milestones, but is not a primary attribute used to estimate individual user stories.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Complexity reflects how challenging a user story is to implement. It includes technical difficulties, integration issues, and other factors that affect the effort required to complete the story. Option A: Cost is not used in the initial estimation of user stories. Option B: The scope is related to the overall project goals and deliverables but it's not usually a direct attribute in the initial estimation of individual user stories. Option C: Scheduling is related to the project timeline and milestones, but is not a primary attribute used to estimate individual user stories.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":57,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What are the components the project team will use to Define Activities? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What are the components the project team will use to Define Activities? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Schedule management plan<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Schedule management plan\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>​Scope baseline<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Scope baseline\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>​Enterprise environmental factors<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Enterprise environmental factors\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>​Project charter<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Project charter\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Project documents<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Project documents\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, B, C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The schedule management plan, scope baseline, and enterprise environmental factors are all inputs to the Define Activities process (PMI Process Groups, page 91).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option E:<\\/span> Project documents are the documentation created throughout the five Process Groups to initiate, plan, execute, manage and control, close, and deliver the project. They are not a required input to the “Define activities” process.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, B, C The schedule management plan, scope baseline, and enterprise environmental factors are all inputs to the Define Activities process (PMI Process Groups, page 91). Option E: Project documents are the documentation created throughout the five Process Groups to initiate, plan, execute, manage and control, close, and deliver the project. They are not a required input to the “Define activities” process.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":58,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project is nearing the final stages, and the project team has completed most of the planned features. However, there are some outstanding high-priority backlog items. How should the team determine if the product is ready for release?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project is nearing the final stages, and the project team has completed most of the planned features. However, there are some outstanding high-priority backlog items. How should the team determine if the product is ready for release?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Conduct a regression test to ensure no features are broken.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Conduct a regression test to ensure no features are broken.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ask the product owner to make the release decision without reviewing the backlog.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Ask the product owner to make the release decision without reviewing the backlog.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Delay the release until every backlog item is completed.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Delay the release until every backlog item is completed.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Review the backlog and ensure that the remaining items are non-critical<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Review the backlog and ensure that the remaining items are non-critical .\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">This approach allows the project team to assess whether the outstanding backlog items are essential for the product's functionality or user satisfaction. If the remaining items are non-critical, the team can proceed with the release while potentially scheduling the unfinished items for future iterations.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> While regression testing is important to ensure existing functionality works as intended, it does not address whether high-priority backlog items are critical for the release<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Releasing without reviewing the backlog would overlook important high-priority items that may impact product quality or user satisfaction.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Not all backlog items need to be completed before a release, especially if some items are non-critical. Delaying the release unnecessarily could waste resources and time when non-essential items can be addressed later.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D This approach allows the project team to assess whether the outstanding backlog items are essential for the product's functionality or user satisfaction. If the remaining items are non-critical, the team can proceed with the release while potentially scheduling the unfinished items for future iterations. Option A: While regression testing is important to ensure existing functionality works as intended, it does not address whether high-priority backlog items are critical for the release . Option B: Releasing without reviewing the backlog would overlook important high-priority items that may impact product quality or user satisfaction. Option C: Not all backlog items need to be completed before a release, especially if some items are non-critical. Delaying the release unnecessarily could waste resources and time when non-essential items can be addressed later.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":59,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">The most commonly used logical dependency between two activities in a project plan is:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The most commonly used logical dependency between two activities in a project plan is:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-1\\\"><p><span>Start-to-finish dependency<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Start-to-finish dependency\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p>Start-to-start dependency <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Start-to-start dependency\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-1\\\"><p><span>Finish-to-finish dependency<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Finish-to-finish dependency\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-1\\\"><p><span>Finish-to-start dependency<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Finish-to-start dependency\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The Finish-to-start dependency consists of a successor activity that cannot start until the predecessor activity finishes.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The Start-to-finish dependency consists of a successor activity that cannot be finished until the predecessor activity starts.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Start-to-start dependency consists of a successor activity that cannot start until the predecessor activity starts.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Finish-to-finish dependency consists of a successor activity that cannot be finished until the predecessor activity finishes.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The Finish-to-start dependency consists of a successor activity that cannot start until the predecessor activity finishes. Option A: The Start-to-finish dependency consists of a successor activity that cannot be finished until the predecessor activity starts. Option B: The Start-to-start dependency consists of a successor activity that cannot start until the predecessor activity starts. Option C: The Finish-to-finish dependency consists of a successor activity that cannot be finished until the predecessor activity finishes.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":60,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">______ is the amount of time a successor task can be advanced before the predecessor task is completed.<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"______ is the amount of time a successor task can be advanced before the predecessor task is completed.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Delay<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Delay\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Lag<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Lag\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Lead<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Lead\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Overlap<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Overlap\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Lead is the amount of time whereby a successor activity can be advanced with respect to a predecessor activity.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Lag is the amount of time whereby a successor activity will be delayed with respect to a predecessor activity.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; D:<\\/span> Delay and overlap are not official terms used by PMI.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Lead is the amount of time whereby a successor activity can be advanced with respect to a predecessor activity. Option B: Lag is the amount of time whereby a successor activity will be delayed with respect to a predecessor activity. Options A & D: Delay and overlap are not official terms used by PMI.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":61,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager estimated the project timeline to end within 4 months +/- 1 month, where should this estimate be documented?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager estimated the project timeline to end within 4 months +/- 1 month, where should this estimate be documented?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Risk register<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Risk register\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Assumption log<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Assumption log\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Meeting minutes<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Meeting minutes\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Basis of estimates<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Basis of estimates\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Basis of estimates are supporting documents that detail the assumptions, constraints, ranges, and confidence levels in establishing project estimates.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A risk register is a centralized repository for documenting and managing risk which is an output of risk management processes. It includes details such as the assigned risk owner, probability, impact, risk score, and planned responses.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The assumption log records all the assumptions and the constraints of the project.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Basis of estimates are supporting documents that detail the assumptions, constraints, ranges, and confidence levels in establishing project estimates. Option A: A risk register is a centralized repository for documenting and managing risk which is an output of risk management processes. It includes details such as the assigned risk owner, probability, impact, risk score, and planned responses. Option B: The assumption log records all the assumptions and the constraints of the project.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":62,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">In a construction project for a new office building, the project manager after analysis and consultations with the engineers and suppliers estimates the cost to be at $75,000 with a range of possible variance of +/- 5%. What type of estimate is described in this example?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In a construction project for a new office building, the project manager after analysis and consultations with the engineers and suppliers estimates the cost to be at $75,000 with a range of possible variance of +/- 5%. What type of estimate is described in this example?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-1\\\"><p><span>Definitive estimate<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Definitive estimate\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-1\\\"><p><span>Conceptual estimate<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Conceptual estimate\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p>Preliminary estimate <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Preliminary estimate\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-1\\\"><p><span>Provisional estimate<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Provisional estimate\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager in this situation has thoroughly reviewed the project requirements and completed a cost analysis to finalize the project budget estimation<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Conceptual estimate is used to narrow down uncertainties by creating a prototype or a mockup in order to help identify potential cost overruns.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The preliminary estimate is not the Correct Answer in this situation as it provides an abstract, introductory estimation. Usually used in the preliminary phase of project planning when there aren’t many details available.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Provisional estimate is a made-up term.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The project manager in this situation has thoroughly reviewed the project requirements and completed a cost analysis to finalize the project budget estimation . Option B: Conceptual estimate is used to narrow down uncertainties by creating a prototype or a mockup in order to help identify potential cost overruns. Option C: The preliminary estimate is not the Correct Answer in this situation as it provides an abstract, introductory estimation. Usually used in the preliminary phase of project planning when there aren’t many details available. Option D: Provisional estimate is a made-up term.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":63,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Due to a lack of knowledge of the involved technology, an agile team was unable to estimate the number of user stories needed in the subsequent iteration. What tool or technique can the project manager recommend to overcome such a problem?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Due to a lack of knowledge of the involved technology, an agile team was unable to estimate the number of user stories needed in the subsequent iteration. What tool or technique can the project manager recommend to overcome such a problem?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Value stream<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Value stream\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Progressive elaboration<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Progressive elaboration\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Spike<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Spike\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Refactoring<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Refactoring\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager should recommend using Spike. As a research story, a spike represents a time-boxed effort that is dedicated to learning, architecture &amp; design, prototypes, etc. to better understand critical technical or functional details and thus make accurate estimations (Agile practice guide, page 56).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Progressive elaboration can be a solution if the used technology can be understood over time. But, since the user stories are going to be implemented during the subsequent iteration, then progressive elaboration is not feasible in this scenario.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Refactoring is a technique for enhancing product quality.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A value stream is used to determine which actions bring more value to customers.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The project manager should recommend using Spike. As a research story, a spike represents a time-boxed effort that is dedicated to learning, architecture & design, prototypes, etc. to better understand critical technical or functional details and thus make accurate estimations (Agile practice guide, page 56). Option B: Progressive elaboration can be a solution if the used technology can be understood over time. But, since the user stories are going to be implemented during the subsequent iteration, then progressive elaboration is not feasible in this scenario. Option D: Refactoring is a technique for enhancing product quality. Option A: A value stream is used to determine which actions bring more value to customers.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":64,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which measure indicates the cost performance needed with the remaining resources to meet the financial goal of the project?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which measure indicates the cost performance needed with the remaining resources to meet the financial goal of the project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>VAC<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"VAC\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>ETC<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"ETC\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>EAC<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"EAC\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>TCPI<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"TCPI\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">To complete performance index (TCPI) answers the question: “What performance rate must be achieved on the remaining work within the remaining resources to stay within budget?” Greater than one indicates harder to complete; less than one indicates easier to complete.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The variance at completion (VAC) answers the question: “By how much will we be over or under budget at the project's completion?” A positive value indicates an under-budget cost, whereas a negative value indicates an over-budget cost.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The estimate to complete (ETC) answers the question: “How much more will the project cost?”<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The estimate at completion (EAC) answers the question: “From this moment, what is the expected total cost of the project?”<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D To complete performance index (TCPI) answers the question: “What performance rate must be achieved on the remaining work within the remaining resources to stay within budget?” Greater than one indicates harder to complete; less than one indicates easier to complete. Option A: The variance at completion (VAC) answers the question: “By how much will we be over or under budget at the project's completion?” A positive value indicates an under-budget cost, whereas a negative value indicates an over-budget cost. Option B: The estimate to complete (ETC) answers the question: “How much more will the project cost?” Option C: The estimate at completion (EAC) answers the question: “From this moment, what is the expected total cost of the project?”\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":65,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Which document typically includes the business analysis approach, level of effort, and stakeholder engagement plan?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which document typically includes the business analysis approach, level of effort, and stakeholder engagement plan?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project charter<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project charter\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business case<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Business case\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business analysis plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Business analysis plan\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder engagement plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stakeholder engagement plan\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A business analysis plan typically includes the business analysis approach, the level of effort, and the stakeholder engagement plan. It provides a summary of all key decisions regarding the business analysis work, such as stakeholder engagement and requirements management​ (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 134)<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The project charter authorizes the project and defines its objectives,  and it doesn't typically include stakeholder engagement and business analysis planning​.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The business case justifies the need for the project by outlining the business value but does not detail the business analysis approach, level of effort, or stakeholder engagement​.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Stakeholder engagement plan addresses stakeholder communication and engagement; it does not encompass the full business analysis approach or level of effort.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A business analysis plan typically includes the business analysis approach, the level of effort, and the stakeholder engagement plan. It provides a summary of all key decisions regarding the business analysis work, such as stakeholder engagement and requirements management (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 134) . Option A: The project charter authorizes the project and defines its objectives,  and it doesn't typically include stakeholder engagement and business analysis planning. Option B: The business case justifies the need for the project by outlining the business value but does not detail the business analysis approach, level of effort, or stakeholder engagement. Option D: The Stakeholder engagement plan addresses stakeholder communication and engagement; it does not encompass the full business analysis approach or level of effort.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":66,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager implemented the project management plan meticulously but she was struggling with leading the project team effectively. Talking to her mentor, the project manager was advised to further focus on developing her leadership skills. In this situation, leadership means:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager implemented the project management plan meticulously but she was struggling with leading the project team effectively. Talking to her mentor, the project manager was advised to further focus on developing her leadership skills. In this situation, leadership means:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Growing an ongoing business over a long period of time<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Growing an ongoing business over a long period of time\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensuring predictability in an uncertain environment<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Ensuring predictability in an uncertain environment\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adhering to standards and procedures<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Adhering to standards and procedures\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Motivating people by establishing and maintaining vision<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Motivating people by establishing and maintaining vision\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Successful leaders are able to communicate the project vision to their team so that everyone has a shared vision of the bigger picture. When the whole project team understands this vision, individuals are able to see where they fit in and how each of them contributes to the success of the project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 23-25).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Successful leaders are able to communicate the project vision to their team so that everyone has a shared vision of the bigger picture. When the whole project team understands this vision, individuals are able to see where they fit in and how each of them contributes to the success of the project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 23-25).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":67,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which process is performed periodically as needed?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which process is performed periodically as needed?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p>Develop project charter <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Develop project charter\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-1\\\"><p><span>Control costs<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Control costs\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-1\\\"><p><span>Monitor and control project work<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Monitor and control project work\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-1\\\"><p><span>Acquire resources<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Acquire resources\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Processes fall into three categories:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Processes used once or at predefined points in the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Processes that are performed periodically as needed.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Processes that are performed continuously throughout the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Acquire resources is performed as resources are needed, therefore it falls under the category of processes that are performed periodically as needed.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Develop project charter is performed once at a predefined point in the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options B &amp; C:<\\/span> Most of the monitoring and controlling processes are under the category of processes that are performed continuously throughout the project.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Processes fall into three categories: ● Processes used once or at predefined points in the project. ● Processes that are performed periodically as needed. ● Processes that are performed continuously throughout the project. Acquire resources is performed as resources are needed, therefore it falls under the category of processes that are performed periodically as needed. Option A: Develop project charter is performed once at a predefined point in the project. Options B & C: Most of the monitoring and controlling processes are under the category of processes that are performed continuously throughout the project.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":68,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">When managing communications, what are the effective techniques the project manager can use? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When managing communications, what are the effective techniques the project manager can use? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Recognition and rewards<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Recognition and rewards\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Overloading information<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Overloading information\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Active listening<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Active listening\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Facilitation<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Facilitation\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Team building<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Team building\"}],\"key\":[\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager should excel in active listening by acknowledging, clarifying, confirming, and addressing barriers that hinder understanding.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager should also possess the ability to build consensus, navigate obstacles, and sustain interest and enthusiasm within the team.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C, D The project manager should excel in active listening by acknowledging, clarifying, confirming, and addressing barriers that hinder understanding. The project manager should also possess the ability to build consensus, navigate obstacles, and sustain interest and enthusiasm within the team.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":69,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager has been leading an Agile project for the last 9 months. When should the project manager stop tailoring the process?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager has been leading an Agile project for the last 9 months. When should the project manager stop tailoring the process?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\" id=\\\"page_271\\\"><p><span>When the Product Owner decides<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"When the Product Owner decides\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>When the Project Manager decides<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"When the Project Manager decides\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>When the cross-functional team members decide<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"When the cross-functional team members decide\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>The tailoring process should never be stopped<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"The tailoring process should never be stopped\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A project manager who truly understands Agile knows that tailoring its processes is a continuous task. Projects are undertaken to create a unique service, product, or result which means that every project is unique. This is where process tailoring steps in. Process tailoring addresses the fact that project management processes are not “one size fits all”. Every project has its own process needs and based on that, the project team needs to conduct the needed adjustments to their processes. This can include adding, removing, or revising processes.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D A project manager who truly understands Agile knows that tailoring its processes is a continuous task. Projects are undertaken to create a unique service, product, or result which means that every project is unique. This is where process tailoring steps in. Process tailoring addresses the fact that project management processes are not “one size fits all”. Every project has its own process needs and based on that, the project team needs to conduct the needed adjustments to their processes. This can include adding, removing, or revising processes.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":70,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">At the end of a sprint retrospective, a team member stated that the meeting output was almost the same as the previous ones and suggested canceling it or at least reducing its frequency.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\">What should the project manager do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"At the end of a sprint retrospective, a team member stated that the meeting output was almost the same as the previous ones and suggested canceling it or at least reducing its frequency. What should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>Extend the sprint timebox in order to allow for more improvements to be discussed in the retrospective.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Extend the sprint timebox in order to allow for more improvements to be discussed in the retrospective.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>Reduce the frequency of retrospectives to once every two sprints.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Reduce the frequency of retrospectives to once every two sprints.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7E\\\"><p><span>Go with voting, and if all team members agree, then skip retrospectives.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Go with voting, and if all team members agree, then skip retrospectives.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7H\\\"><p><span>Keep the same frequency of retrospectives and reflect on how to make them more relevant and actionable.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Keep the same frequency of retrospectives and reflect on how to make them more relevant and actionable.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The sprint retrospective is one of the main scrum events, which aims to help the team adjust and improve their work processes over time. The project manager has to better facilitate the meeting, engage team members, solicit and collect more feedback, check various metrics, and use different investigation techniques such as the why-why method to help them take future actionable measures accordingly.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Extending the sprint timebox denotes smoothing the problem rather than trying to solve it.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options B &amp; C:<\\/span> The project manager should not cancel the retrospective meeting nor reduce its frequency. Instead, the project manager should reflect on why the retrospective meeting is not driving the intended value to the team.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The sprint retrospective is one of the main scrum events, which aims to help the team adjust and improve their work processes over time. The project manager has to better facilitate the meeting, engage team members, solicit and collect more feedback, check various metrics, and use different investigation techniques such as the why-why method to help them take future actionable measures accordingly. Option A: Extending the sprint timebox denotes smoothing the problem rather than trying to solve it. Options B & C: The project manager should not cancel the retrospective meeting nor reduce its frequency. Instead, the project manager should reflect on why the retrospective meeting is not driving the intended value to the team.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":71,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What is the key difference between a traceability matrix and an interaction matrix?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the key difference between a traceability matrix and an interaction matrix?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A traceability matrix is only used in agile projects<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A traceability matrix is only used in agile projects\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An interaction matrix is maintained throughout the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. An interaction matrix is maintained throughout the project\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An interaction matrix is a temporary artifact<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. An interaction matrix is a temporary artifact\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An interaction matrix is used for mapping stakeholder interactions<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. An interaction matrix is used for mapping stakeholder interactions\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">An interaction matrix is typically used as a one-time tool to evaluate the relationships and dependencies between various elements, such as requirements or components, at a specific point in time. It is not meant to be maintained or updated throughout the project; instead, it serves its purpose during a particular phase of the analysis. This distinguishes it from other project documents that may evolve over time, like a traceability matrix, which is maintained throughout the project to ensure ongoing alignment of requirements (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 196).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A traceability matrix can be used in various project types, including predictive, adaptive, and agile projects, to trace requirements and ensure alignment with business goals and deliverables.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> An interaction matrix represents a specific point in time and is not maintained. It is used to evaluate requirements at a given moment during the project​.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> An interaction matrix is used to figure out whether requirements are sufficiently detailed and to evaluate product information, not to map stakeholder interactions.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C An interaction matrix is typically used as a one-time tool to evaluate the relationships and dependencies between various elements, such as requirements or components, at a specific point in time. It is not meant to be maintained or updated throughout the project; instead, it serves its purpose during a particular phase of the analysis. This distinguishes it from other project documents that may evolve over time, like a traceability matrix, which is maintained throughout the project to ensure ongoing alignment of requirements (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 196). Option A: A traceability matrix can be used in various project types, including predictive, adaptive, and agile projects, to trace requirements and ensure alignment with business goals and deliverables. Option B: An interaction matrix represents a specific point in time and is not maintained. It is used to evaluate requirements at a given moment during the project. Option D: An interaction matrix is used to figure out whether requirements are sufficiently detailed and to evaluate product information, not to map stakeholder interactions.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":72,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which action is included in the cost control process?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which action is included in the cost control process?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identify how project costs will be planned, structured, and controlled.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Identify how project costs will be planned, structured, and controlled.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Determine policies, objectives, and responsibilities to meet stakeholder needs.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Determine policies, objectives, and responsibilities to meet stakeholder needs.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Develop an approximation of the monetary resources needed to complete project activities.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Develop an approximation of the monetary resources needed to complete project activities.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Monitor cost performance to isolate and understand variances from the approved cost baseline.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Monitor cost performance to isolate and understand variances from the approved cost baseline.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Monitoring cost performance to isolate and understand variances from the approved cost baseline is a key action in the cost control process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Identifying how project costs will be planned, structured, and controlled is a description of the cost management planning process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Determining policies and objectives is part of the project charter or plan.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Developing an approximation of monetary resources is part of cost estimating.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Monitoring cost performance to isolate and understand variances from the approved cost baseline is a key action in the cost control process. Option A: Identifying how project costs will be planned, structured, and controlled is a description of the cost management planning process. Option B: Determining policies and objectives is part of the project charter or plan. Option C: Developing an approximation of monetary resources is part of cost estimating.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":73,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A project manager is managing a project with 8 stakeholders, how many communication channels exist?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is managing a project with 8 stakeholders, how many communication channels exist?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>16<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"16\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>24<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"24\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7E\\\"><p><span>28<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"28\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7H\\\"><p><span>32<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"32\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The communications channels formula is N * (N-1) / 2, where N is the number of stakeholders. Using this formula 8 * (8-1) / 2 , we get 28 communication channels.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The communications channels formula is N * (N-1) / 2, where N is the number of stakeholders. Using this formula 8 * (8-1) / 2 , we get 28 communication channels.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":74,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A big user story is commonly <span><\\/span>known as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A big user story is commonly known as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Feature<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Feature\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Epic<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Epic\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Release<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Release\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Milestone<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Milestone\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Big user stories or large-scale features are known as Epics. Epics usually involve a high-level feature, requirement, or customer request with a few lines of description, as they might only depict the final desired output. Epics could expand over months and even take over an entire release or several releases.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Big user stories or large-scale features are known as Epics. Epics usually involve a high-level feature, requirement, or customer request with a few lines of description, as they might only depict the final desired output. Epics could expand over months and even take over an entire release or several releases.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":75,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">In a network diagram, the ________________ is based on the assumption that resources will always be available whenever they are needed.<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In a network diagram, the ________________ is based on the assumption that resources will always be available whenever they are needed.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p>Critical Path <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Critical Path\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-1\\\"><p><span>PERT Estimate<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"PERT Estimate\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p>Critical Chain <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Critical Chain\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-1\\\"><p><span>Sprint Planning<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Sprint Planning\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Among the drawbacks of the critical path method is the assumption that all project resources are available all the time, not taking into consideration resource dependencies.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> PERT is an activity estimation technique<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The critical Chain takes resource availability into account.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Sprint Planning is a Scrum event.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Among the drawbacks of the critical path method is the assumption that all project resources are available all the time, not taking into consideration resource dependencies. Option B: PERT is an activity estimation technique Option C: The critical Chain takes resource availability into account. Option D: Sprint Planning is a Scrum event.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":76,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which of the following is NOT a principle of the Dynamic Systems Development Method (DSDM)?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is NOT a principle of the Dynamic Systems Development Method (DSDM)?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Focus on the business need<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Focus on the business need\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Deliver on time<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Deliver on time\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Collaborate and compromise quality<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Collaborate and compromise quality\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Build incrementally from firm foundations<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Build incrementally from firm foundations\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In the Dynamic Systems Development Method (DSDM), one of the core principles is collaborating, but it does not advocate compromising quality (Agile Practice Guide, page 110).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C In the Dynamic Systems Development Method (DSDM), one of the core principles is collaborating, but it does not advocate compromising quality (Agile Practice Guide, page 110).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":77,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which of the following are key processes in the Elicitation Knowledge Area? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following are key processes in the Elicitation Knowledge Area? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Determine Stakeholder Engagement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Determine Stakeholder Engagement\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Prepare for Elicitation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Prepare for Elicitation\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Define and Elaborate Requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Define and Elaborate Requirements\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Conduct Elicitation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Conduct Elicitation\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Confirm Solution Evaluation Approach<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Confirm Solution Evaluation Approach\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B &amp; D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The “Prepare for elicitation” process involves organizing and scheduling resources, and preparing the necessary materials for the elicitation activities. The “Conduct Elicitation” process applies various elicitation techniques to extract information from stakeholders and other sources.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Determine Stakeholder Engagement process is part of stakeholder engagement and not elicitation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Define and Elaborate Requirements belongs to the analysis area, and not directly under elicitation​.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option E:<\\/span> Confirm Solution Evaluation Approach process is related to solution evaluation, and not elicitation.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B & D The “Prepare for elicitation” process involves organizing and scheduling resources, and preparing the necessary materials for the elicitation activities. The “Conduct Elicitation” process applies various elicitation techniques to extract information from stakeholders and other sources. Option A: Determine Stakeholder Engagement process is part of stakeholder engagement and not elicitation. Option C: Define and Elaborate Requirements belongs to the analysis area, and not directly under elicitation. Option E: Confirm Solution Evaluation Approach process is related to solution evaluation, and not elicitation.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":78,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which life cycle approach allows for feedback on unfinished work and encourages modifications based on that feedback?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which life cycle approach allows for feedback on unfinished work and encourages modifications based on that feedback?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Predictive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Predictive\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Iterative<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Iterative\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Incremental<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Incremental\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Waterfall<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Waterfall\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">An Iterative life cycle approach allows for feedback on unfinished work and encourages modifications based on that feedback. In iterative development, a project progresses through repeated cycles (iterations), where feedback is gathered and used to refine and improve the work in each subsequent iteration (Agile practice guide, page 21).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B An Iterative life cycle approach allows for feedback on unfinished work and encourages modifications based on that feedback. In iterative development, a project progresses through repeated cycles (iterations), where feedback is gathered and used to refine and improve the work in each subsequent iteration (Agile practice guide, page 21).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":79,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which of the following is part of the project charter?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is part of the project charter?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Management provisions<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Management provisions\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Detailed project schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Detailed project schedule\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>List of potential stakeholders<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. List of potential stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder registe<span><\\/span>r<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stakeholder registe r\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project charter typically includes high-level information such as management provisions, which outline project governance, roles, and responsibilities, and provide authorization for the project to begin.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The detailed project schedule is part of project planning, not the charter.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options C &amp; D:<\\/span> The list of potential stakeholders and the stakeholder register are part of more detailed planning and stakeholder management.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The project charter typically includes high-level information such as management provisions, which outline project governance, roles, and responsibilities, and provide authorization for the project to begin. Option B: The detailed project schedule is part of project planning, not the charter. Options C & D: The list of potential stakeholders and the stakeholder register are part of more detailed planning and stakeholder management.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":80,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">The most appropriate project lifecycle model for an environment with a high level of change and extensive stakeholder involvement is:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The most appropriate project lifecycle model for an environment with a high level of change and extensive stakeholder involvement is:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adaptive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Adaptive\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Progressive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Progressive\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Predictive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Predictive\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Tailoring<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Tailoring\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">An Adaptive project lifecycle model is best suited for environments with a high level of change and extensive stakeholder involvement. This approach is flexible and responsive, allowing frequent feedback and adjustments throughout the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options B &amp; D:<\\/span> Progressive and tailoring are not standard project lifecycles.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Predictive works best in stable environments with well-defined requirements and minimal change.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A An Adaptive project lifecycle model is best suited for environments with a high level of change and extensive stakeholder involvement. This approach is flexible and responsive, allowing frequent feedback and adjustments throughout the project. Options B & D: Progressive and tailoring are not standard project lifecycles. Option C: Predictive works best in stable environments with well-defined requirements and minimal change.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":81,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">What is the role of a business analyst in relation to the project sponsor?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the role of a business analyst in relation to the project sponsor?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To define the problem, ensure the business vision, and bridge communication with the project team.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. To define the problem, ensure the business vision, and bridge communication with the project team.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To provide technical guidance to the sponsor on software development.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. To provide technical guidance to the sponsor on software development.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To ensure the project is delivered on time and within budget.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. To ensure the project is delivered on time and within budget.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To manage the sponsor’s day-to-day project tasks.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. To manage the sponsor’s day-to-day project tasks.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The business analyst works closely with the sponsor to define the problem, identify solutions, and ensure that the business vision is addressed in the solution. The business analyst also acts as a communication bridge between the sponsor and the project team, ensuring the sponsor's needs are met throughout the project (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 50).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The business analyst may work with technical teams but does not usually provide direct technical guidance to the sponsor.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Ensuring the project is delivered on time and within budget is the responsibility of the project manager, not the business analyst. The business analyst focuses on ensuring the product meets business needs rather than managing the project's schedule or budget​.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The business analyst does not manage the sponsor’s tasks. Their role is to act as a liaison between the sponsor and the project team, advocating for business requirements, rather than managing tasks.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The business analyst works closely with the sponsor to define the problem, identify solutions, and ensure that the business vision is addressed in the solution. The business analyst also acts as a communication bridge between the sponsor and the project team, ensuring the sponsor's needs are met throughout the project (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 50). Option B: The business analyst may work with technical teams but does not usually provide direct technical guidance to the sponsor. Option C: Ensuring the project is delivered on time and within budget is the responsibility of the project manager, not the business analyst. The business analyst focuses on ensuring the product meets business needs rather than managing the project's schedule or budget. Option D: The business analyst does not manage the sponsor’s tasks. Their role is to act as a liaison between the sponsor and the project team, advocating for business requirements, rather than managing tasks.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":82,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which type of manager is assigned by the performing organization to lead the team responsible for achieving the project objectives?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which type of manager is assigned by the performing organization to lead the team responsible for achieving the project objectives?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Program Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Program Manager\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Functional Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Functional Manager\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project Manager\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Portfolio Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Portfolio Manager\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A Project Manager is assigned by the performing organization to lead the team responsible for achieving the project's objectives. The project manager oversees the planning, execution, monitoring, and completion of the project to ensure it meets its goals within scope, time, and budget.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Functional Manager oversees a specific department or function within the organization, but not specific projects.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A Project Manager is assigned by the performing organization to lead the team responsible for achieving the project's objectives. The project manager oversees the planning, execution, monitoring, and completion of the project to ensure it meets its goals within scope, time, and budget. Option B: The Functional Manager oversees a specific department or function within the organization, but not specific projects.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":83,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">The project team is planning the next release but is unsure if the organization is ready to handle the transition to the new system. What should the team conduct to confirm the organization's preparedness for the transition?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The project team is planning the next release but is unsure if the organization is ready to handle the transition to the new system. What should the team conduct to confirm the organization's preparedness for the transition?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Readiness assessment<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Readiness assessment\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>User acceptance testing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. User acceptance testing\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint review<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Sprint review\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stakeholder analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A Readiness assessment is conducted to confirm whether an organization is prepared for a transition to a new system. It evaluates various factors such as the organization's capability, infrastructure, and stakeholders' preparedness to handle the upcoming changes<span> <\\/span>(PMI Guide to Business Analysis, pages 218 &amp; 219).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> User Acceptance Testing (UAT) focuses on verifying that the system meets the business requirements and functions correctly for the end users. While it is important for ensuring system functionality, it does not evaluate the organization's preparedness for transition.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Sprint review is a meeting held at the end of a sprint in agile methodologies to inspect the completed work and gather feedback. It is not used to assess organizational readiness.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Stakeholder analysis helps identify and understand the interests and influence of stakeholders, but it does not assess the organization’s overall readiness to handle a system transition.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A Readiness assessment is conducted to confirm whether an organization is prepared for a transition to a new system. It evaluates various factors such as the organization's capability, infrastructure, and stakeholders' preparedness to handle the upcoming changes (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, pages 218 & 219). Option B: User Acceptance Testing (UAT) focuses on verifying that the system meets the business requirements and functions correctly for the end users. While it is important for ensuring system functionality, it does not evaluate the organization's preparedness for transition. Option C: Sprint review is a meeting held at the end of a sprint in agile methodologies to inspect the completed work and gather feedback. It is not used to assess organizational readiness. Option D: Stakeholder analysis helps identify and understand the interests and influence of stakeholders, but it does not assess the organization’s overall readiness to handle a system transition.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":84,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which document includes the project scope, major deliverables, assumptions, and constraints?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which document includes the project scope, major deliverables, assumptions, and constraints?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Charter<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project Charter\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Scope Statement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project Scope Statement\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope Management Plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Scope Management Plan\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope Baseline<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Scope Baseline\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The Project Scope Statement includes detailed information about the project's scope, major deliverables, assumptions, and constraints. It provides a clear definition of what is included in the project and what is excluded, helping to guide project execution.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Project Charter provides high-level information about the project but does not go into detailed scope, deliverables, assumptions, and constraints.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Scope Management Plan outlines how the scope will be defined, validated, and controlled but does not include the scope itself.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Scope Baseline includes the approved scope statement, Work Breakdown Structure (WBS), and WBS dictionary but is not a standalone document for scope details.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The Project Scope Statement includes detailed information about the project's scope, major deliverables, assumptions, and constraints. It provides a clear definition of what is included in the project and what is excluded, helping to guide project execution. Option A: Project Charter provides high-level information about the project but does not go into detailed scope, deliverables, assumptions, and constraints. Option C: Scope Management Plan outlines how the scope will be defined, validated, and controlled but does not include the scope itself. Option D: Scope Baseline includes the approved scope statement, Work Breakdown Structure (WBS), and WBS dictionary but is not a standalone document for scope details.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":85,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What is NOT included in the Procurement Statement of Work<span><\\/span>?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is NOT included in the Procurement Statement of Work ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Specifications of the product or service to be procured<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Specifications of the product or service to be procured\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost of the product or service to be procured<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Cost of the product or service to be procured\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work location<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Work location\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Period of performance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Period of performance\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The SOW describes the procurement items to allow prospective sellers to determine if they are capable of providing the products, services, or results. The SOW can include specifications, desired quantity, quality levels, performance data, period of performance, work location, and other requirements (PMI Process Groups, page 216). Prospective sellers are responsible for submitting their proposals, including pricing details.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The SOW describes the procurement items to allow prospective sellers to determine if they are capable of providing the products, services, or results. The SOW can include specifications, desired quantity, quality levels, performance data, period of performance, work location, and other requirements (PMI Process Groups, page 216). Prospective sellers are responsible for submitting their proposals, including pricing details.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":86,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Projects may be divided into phases to provide better management control. Collectively, what do these phases form?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Projects may be divided into phases to provide better management control. Collectively, what do these phases form?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product life cycle<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Product life cycle\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project life<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project life\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project life cycle<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project life cycle\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project management life cycle<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Project management life cycle\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The phases of a project are typically grouped together to form the Project Life Cycle, which defines the stages a project goes through from initiation to completion. Each phase provides an opportunity for management control and decision-making, ensuring the project remains aligned with its objectives<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The Product Life Cycle refers to the stages a product goes through from development to retirement, not a project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Project Life is not a recognized term in project management<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Project Management Life Cycle refers to the processes (initiating, planning, executing, etc.) used to manage a project, but it does not define the actual phases of the project itself.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The phases of a project are typically grouped together to form the Project Life Cycle, which defines the stages a project goes through from initiation to completion. Each phase provides an opportunity for management control and decision-making, ensuring the project remains aligned with its objectives . Option A: The Product Life Cycle refers to the stages a product goes through from development to retirement, not a project. Option B: The Project Life is not a recognized term in project management Option D: The Project Management Life Cycle refers to the processes (initiating, planning, executing, etc.) used to manage a project, but it does not define the actual phases of the project itself.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":87,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which of the following statements correctly characterizes \\\"pull\\\" communication?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following statements correctly characterizes \\\"pull\\\" communication?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It includes letters, memos, reports, emails, and faxes.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. It includes letters, memos, reports, emails, and faxes.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Recipients must access the communication content at their own discretion.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Recipients must access the communication content at their own discretion.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It is the most effective way to ensure a common understanding among all participants.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. It is the most effective way to ensure a common understanding among all participants.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It is primarily used when the volume of information to be transferred is minimal.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. It is primarily used when the volume of information to be transferred is minimal.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Pull communication is a method where the information is made available to recipients, but they must take the initiative to retrieve or access it, often from a shared repository (e.g., a website, intranet, or database). This method is commonly used when the volume of information is large, and not everyone needs or wants the same level of detail.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Letters, memos, reports, emails, and faxes all fall under push communication, in which information is actively sent to recipients.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Pull communication is often used for larger volumes of information.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Pull communication is a method where the information is made available to recipients, but they must take the initiative to retrieve or access it, often from a shared repository (e.g., a website, intranet, or database). This method is commonly used when the volume of information is large, and not everyone needs or wants the same level of detail. Option A: Letters, memos, reports, emails, and faxes all fall under push communication, in which information is actively sent to recipients. Option D: Pull communication is often used for larger volumes of information.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":88,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which emotional intelligence component involves the ability to navigate and resolve conflicts within the team?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which emotional intelligence component involves the ability to navigate and resolve conflicts within the team?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Self-awareness<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Self-awareness\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Social skills<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Social skills\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Self-management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Self-management\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Risk management\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Social skills in emotional intelligence involve the ability to build relationships, communicate effectively, and manage conflicts within a team. This component focuses on navigating interpersonal dynamics, including resolving disagreements and fostering collaboration (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 26).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Self-awareness refers to recognizing and understanding one's own emotions.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Self-management involves controlling one's emotions and behaviors, particularly in stressful situations.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Risk management is unrelated to emotional intelligence and deals with identifying and mitigating project risks.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Social skills in emotional intelligence involve the ability to build relationships, communicate effectively, and manage conflicts within a team. This component focuses on navigating interpersonal dynamics, including resolving disagreements and fostering collaboration (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 26). Option A: Self-awareness refers to recognizing and understanding one's own emotions. Option C: Self-management involves controlling one's emotions and behaviors, particularly in stressful situations. Option D: Risk management is unrelated to emotional intelligence and deals with identifying and mitigating project risks.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":89,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager is using the critical path method to define the project schedule. One of the project activities lasts 5 days, with an Early Start (ES) on day 10, and a Late Start (LS) on day 15.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s1GS-1\\\">What is the activity’s total float?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is using the critical path method to define the project schedule. One of the project activities lasts 5 days, with an Early Start (ES) on day 10, and a Late Start (LS) on day 15. What is the activity’s total float?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p>5 <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"5\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-1\\\"><p><span>15<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"15\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p>It cannot be determined since the activity’s Late Finish (LF) is unknown <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"It cannot be determined since the activity’s Late Finish (LF) is unknown\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-1\\\"><p><span>It cannot be determined since the activity’s Early Finish (EF) is unknown<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"It cannot be determined since the activity’s Early Finish (EF) is unknown\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Total Float = Late Start date – Early Start date = 15 - 10 = 5<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Total Float = Late Start date – Early Start date = 15 - 10 = 5\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":90,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">What type of management describes the continuous management of goods and services production to ensure business continuity?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What type of management describes the continuous management of goods and services production to ensure business continuity?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Portfolio<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Portfolio\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Projec<span><\\/span>t<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Projec t\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Program<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Program\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Operations<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Operations\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-1\\\">Operations management refers to the continuous management of the production of goods and services to ensure the smooth functioning of day-to-day business activities and long-term business continuity. It focuses on maintaining efficiency, quality, and productivity in the ongoing processes of a company.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Operations management refers to the continuous management of the production of goods and services to ensure the smooth functioning of day-to-day business activities and long-term business continuity. It focuses on maintaining efficiency, quality, and productivity in the ongoing processes of a company.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":91,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What is a product roadmap used for in business analysis?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is a product roadmap used for in business analysis?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To detail a project timeline<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. To detail a project timeline\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To communicate how a product will develop and mature over time<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. To communicate how a product will develop and mature over time\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To define organizational strategy<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. To define organizational strategy\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To assess current business processes<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. To assess current business processes\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A product roadmap is used to outline the long-term development and evolution of a product, providing a high-level plan of features, milestones, and releases. It serves as a strategic tool in business analysis to show how the product will mature, meet customer needs, and respond to market changes over time. It aligns stakeholders with the vision and direction of the product​.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A project timeline focuses on scheduling tasks and deadlines for a specific project, whereas a product roadmap is broader, focusing on the product’s long-term development rather than detailed timing.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> While a product roadmap can support strategic goals, its primary purpose is not to define the organizational strategy. It focuses on the product’s development path rather than the overall business strategy.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Assessing current business processes involves evaluating how workflows and systems operate, which is not the primary function of a product roadmap. The roadmap is forward-looking, focusing on the future of the product.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A product roadmap is used to outline the long-term development and evolution of a product, providing a high-level plan of features, milestones, and releases. It serves as a strategic tool in business analysis to show how the product will mature, meet customer needs, and respond to market changes over time. It aligns stakeholders with the vision and direction of the product. Option A: A project timeline focuses on scheduling tasks and deadlines for a specific project, whereas a product roadmap is broader, focusing on the product’s long-term development rather than detailed timing. Option C: While a product roadmap can support strategic goals, its primary purpose is not to define the organizational strategy. It focuses on the product’s development path rather than the overall business strategy. Option D: Assessing current business processes involves evaluating how workflows and systems operate, which is not the primary function of a product roadmap. The roadmap is forward-looking, focusing on the future of the product.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":92,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Who is primarily responsible for keeping the project aligned with the business objectives?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Who is primarily responsible for keeping the project aligned with the business objectives?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project Manager\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project Sponsor\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project Team\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Management Office (PMO)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Project Management Office (PMO)\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The Project Sponsor is primarily responsible for ensuring that the project remains aligned with the business objectives. They provide high-level guidance, support, and oversight to ensure that the project's goals and deliverables align with the overall business strategy and objectives (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 207).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The Project Manager is responsible for managing the day-to-day aspects of the project but relies on the sponsor to ensure alignment with business objectives.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Project Team executes the project tasks and contributes to its success.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Project Management Office (PMO) provides support and oversight for project management processes.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The Project Sponsor is primarily responsible for ensuring that the project remains aligned with the business objectives. They provide high-level guidance, support, and oversight to ensure that the project's goals and deliverables align with the overall business strategy and objectives (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 207). Option A: The Project Manager is responsible for managing the day-to-day aspects of the project but relies on the sponsor to ensure alignment with business objectives. Option C: The Project Team executes the project tasks and contributes to its success. Option D: The Project Management Office (PMO) provides support and oversight for project management processes.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":93,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What is the main focus of servant leadership in Agile?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the main focus of servant leadership in Agile?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Leading by authority<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Leading by authority\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Delivering business value<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Delivering business value\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Facilitating collaboration and removing impediments<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Facilitating collaboration and removing impediments\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensuring perfect processes<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Ensuring perfect processes\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In Agile, servant leadership focuses on facilitating collaboration, supporting the team, and removing any obstacles that may impede progress. The goal is to empower the team to self-organize and perform at their best (Agile practice guide, page 34).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Leading by authority contradicts the servant leadership philosophy, which prioritizes serving the team over command-and-control leadership.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Delivering business value is important in Agile but is a team objective, not the main focus of servant leadership specifically.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Ensuring perfect processes is not aligned with the servant leadership approach, which emphasizes flexibility and supporting the team rather than enforcing rigid processes.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C In Agile, servant leadership focuses on facilitating collaboration, supporting the team, and removing any obstacles that may impede progress. The goal is to empower the team to self-organize and perform at their best (Agile practice guide, page 34). Option A: Leading by authority contradicts the servant leadership philosophy, which prioritizes serving the team over command-and-control leadership. Option B: Delivering business value is important in Agile but is a team objective, not the main focus of servant leadership specifically. Option D: Ensuring perfect processes is not aligned with the servant leadership approach, which emphasizes flexibility and supporting the team rather than enforcing rigid processes.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":94,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What approach focuses on making work visible and managing the flow of tasks?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What approach focuses on making work visible and managing the flow of tasks?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scrum<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Scrum\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Iterative<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Iterative\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Kanban<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Kanban\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>SAFe<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. SAFe\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Kanban focuses on making work visible and managing the flow of tasks through a visual board. It helps teams visualize their workflow, limit work in progress (WIP), and optimize the flow of tasks to improve efficiency (Agile Practice Guide, page 12).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Scrum is an Agile framework that focuses on time-boxed sprints and roles like Scrum Master and Product Owner, rather than visualizing task flow.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Iterative refers to a development approach that builds and refines a product through repeated cycles, but it doesn't specifically focus on visualizing tasks.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> SAFe (Scaled Agile Framework) is a comprehensive framework for scaling Agile across large organizations, focusing on coordinating multiple Agile teams and managing large-scale initiatives. While SAFe incorporates elements of Agile and Lean, it doesn't specifically focus on task flow and visibility the way Kanban does.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Kanban focuses on making work visible and managing the flow of tasks through a visual board. It helps teams visualize their workflow, limit work in progress (WIP), and optimize the flow of tasks to improve efficiency (Agile Practice Guide, page 12). Option A: Scrum is an Agile framework that focuses on time-boxed sprints and roles like Scrum Master and Product Owner, rather than visualizing task flow. Option B: Iterative refers to a development approach that builds and refines a product through repeated cycles, but it doesn't specifically focus on visualizing tasks. Option D: SAFe (Scaled Agile Framework) is a comprehensive framework for scaling Agile across large organizations, focusing on coordinating multiple Agile teams and managing large-scale initiatives. While SAFe incorporates elements of Agile and Lean, it doesn't specifically focus on task flow and visibility the way Kanban does.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":95,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">When is a product roadmap typically first developed in the product life cycle?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When is a product roadmap typically first developed in the product life cycle?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>During the product launch phase<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. During the product launch phase\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>After the product backlog is defined<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. After the product backlog is defined\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>As part of the product visioning activity<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. As part of the product visioning activity\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>During the product test phase<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. During the product test phase\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A product roadmap is typically first developed as part of the product visioning activity. During the visioning process, the long-term goals and direction of the product are established, and the roadmap serves as a strategic plan that outlines the major milestones, features, and releases. It provides a high-level view of how the product will evolve over time to achieve the product vision.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; D:<\\/span> The roadmap should be developed before the execution, test, and launch phases.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The product roadmap often comes before the product backlog is fully defined. The roadmap sets the direction, and the backlog is then populated with specific tasks and features that align with the roadmap.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A product roadmap is typically first developed as part of the product visioning activity. During the visioning process, the long-term goals and direction of the product are established, and the roadmap serves as a strategic plan that outlines the major milestones, features, and releases. It provides a high-level view of how the product will evolve over time to achieve the product vision. Options A & D: The roadmap should be developed before the execution, test, and launch phases. Option B: The product roadmap often comes before the product backlog is fully defined. The roadmap sets the direction, and the backlog is then populated with specific tasks and features that align with the roadmap.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":96,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">In an Agile approach, what is the primary measure of progress?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In an Agile approach, what is the primary measure of progress?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Comprehensive documentation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Comprehensive documentation\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Percentage completio<span><\\/span>n<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Percentage completio n\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Working software<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Working software\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adherence to the project schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Adherence to the project schedule\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In an Agile approach, the primary measure of progress is working software. Agile prioritizes delivering functional, usable software frequently over other indicators such as documentation or schedule adherence. The goal is to provide real value through regular, incremental deliveries (Agile Practice Guide, page 9).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Comprehensive documentation is minimized in Agile, as it values working software over documentation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Percentage completion is not a primary measure in Agile, as the focus is on deliverable outcomes.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Adherence to the project schedule is less emphasized in Agile, which is more flexible and adaptable to change.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C In an Agile approach, the primary measure of progress is working software. Agile prioritizes delivering functional, usable software frequently over other indicators such as documentation or schedule adherence. The goal is to provide real value through regular, incremental deliveries (Agile Practice Guide, page 9). Option A: Comprehensive documentation is minimized in Agile, as it values working software over documentation. Option B: Percentage completion is not a primary measure in Agile, as the focus is on deliverable outcomes. Option D: Adherence to the project schedule is less emphasized in Agile, which is more flexible and adaptable to change.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":97,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which term refers to the rhythm of activities conducted throughout the project?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which term refers to the rhythm of activities conducted throughout the project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Sprint\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cadence<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Cadence\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Flow<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Flow\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cycle<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Cycle\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Cadence refers to the rhythm or regularity of activities conducted throughout the project. It often describes the consistent intervals at which tasks or iterations (such as sprints or releases) occur (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 34).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Sprint refers specifically to a time-boxed iteration in Scrum, not the overall rhythm.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Flow refers to the smooth progression of tasks, especially in Kanban, but not the project's rhythm.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Cycle can refer to a repetition of activities but doesn't specifically capture the idea of rhythm as cadence does.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Cadence refers to the rhythm or regularity of activities conducted throughout the project. It often describes the consistent intervals at which tasks or iterations (such as sprints or releases) occur (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 34). Option A: Sprint refers specifically to a time-boxed iteration in Scrum, not the overall rhythm. Option C: Flow refers to the smooth progression of tasks, especially in Kanban, but not the project's rhythm. Option D: Cycle can refer to a repetition of activities but doesn't specifically capture the idea of rhythm as cadence does.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":98,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which leadership style evolves based on the competence and commitment of the team members?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which leadership style evolves based on the competence and commitment of the team members?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Autocratic Leadership<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Autocratic Leadership\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Democratic Leadership<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Democratic Leadership\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Transformational Leadership<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Transformational Leadership\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Situational Leadership<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Situational Leadership\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Situational Leadership adapts and evolves based on the competence and commitment of the team members. Leaders using this style change their approach depending on the team's development level, providing more direction or support as needed (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 156).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Autocratic Leadership is a fixed style where the leader makes decisions unilaterally without evolving based on the team's competence<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Democratic Leadership involves team participation in decision-making but does not evolve specifically based on team competence and commitment.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Transformational Leadership focuses on inspiring and motivating the team to achieve greater goals but doesn't evolve based on the team's development level.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Situational Leadership adapts and evolves based on the competence and commitment of the team members. Leaders using this style change their approach depending on the team's development level, providing more direction or support as needed (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 156). Option A: Autocratic Leadership is a fixed style where the leader makes decisions unilaterally without evolving based on the team's competence Option B: Democratic Leadership involves team participation in decision-making but does not evolve specifically based on team competence and commitment. Option C: Transformational Leadership focuses on inspiring and motivating the team to achieve greater goals but doesn't evolve based on the team's development level.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":99,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">The traditional format of a daily stand-up meeting consists of gathering in a circle near a task board where each member takes their turn to answer a number of questions. Which of the following statements best describes the daily stand-up in Agile?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The traditional format of a daily stand-up meeting consists of gathering in a circle near a task board where each member takes their turn to answer a number of questions. Which of the following statements best describes the daily stand-up in Agile?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It is a meeting during which the upcoming work schedule is discussed.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. It is a meeting during which the upcoming work schedule is discussed.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It is a meeting during which the team is asked about what they did on the previous day and their plan for the current day along with any problems they might have faced during the execution of their tasks.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. It is a meeting during which the team is asked about what they did on the previous day and their plan for the current day along with any problems they might have faced during the execution of their tasks.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It is a daily brainstorming session.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. It is a daily brainstorming session.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It is a daily lessons-learned session.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. It is a daily lessons-learned session.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The daily standup is a meeting held by members of the project team. This meeting brings the team together for a status update, to ensure that everyone is on the same page and has insight into what is going on, whether it’s good or bad. Such a meeting usually takes up to 15 minutes during which every team member is asked three questions: What did you do yesterday that helped your team meet the Sprint goal? What will you do today to help your team meet the Sprint goal? And, Did you face any impediments that prevented you or your team from meeting the Sprint goal? (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 179).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The daily standup is a meeting held by members of the project team. This meeting brings the team together for a status update, to ensure that everyone is on the same page and has insight into what is going on, whether it’s good or bad. Such a meeting usually takes up to 15 minutes during which every team member is asked three questions: What did you do yesterday that helped your team meet the Sprint goal? What will you do today to help your team meet the Sprint goal? And, Did you face any impediments that prevented you or your team from meeting the Sprint goal? (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 179).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":100,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">During an iteration review meeting, the product owner rejected one of the features demonstrated by the development team. What will happen next to the rejected user story?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During an iteration review meeting, the product owner rejected one of the features demonstrated by the development team. What will happen next to the rejected user story?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It will be automatically moved to the next sprint backlog<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. It will be automatically moved to the next sprint backlog\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It will be deleted from the product backlog and from the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. It will be deleted from the product backlog and from the project\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It will be updated to address the reasons why it was rejected<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. It will be updated to address the reasons why it was rejected\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It will be moved back to the product backlog for reprioritization<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. It will be moved back to the product backlog for reprioritization\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The right step consists of understanding why the feature was not accepted in the first place, and then moving on to making the required updates. After that, the feature can be moved back to the backlog for reprioritization.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Deleting the user story is not a rational choice since the feature has already been developed, which implies that it brings added value to the product<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The right step consists of understanding why the feature was not accepted in the first place, and then moving on to making the required updates. After that, the feat";
